    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 September 2025",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.1",
      "values:originalText": "Includes amendments:\nAct No. 38, 2025\nThis compilation is in 2 volumes\nVolume 1:\nsections 1-41A\nVolume 2:\nsections 41B-69\nEndnotes\nEach volume has its own contents\n\nAbout this compilation\nThis compilation\nThis is a compilation of the Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 that shows the text of\nthe law as amended and in force on 5 September 2025 (the compilation date).\nThe notes at the end of this compilation (the endnotes) include information\nabout amending laws and the amendment history of provisions of the compiled\nlaw.\nUncommenced amendments\nThe effect of uncommenced amendments is not shown in the text of the\ncompiled law. The details of amendments made up to, but not commenced at,\nthe compilation date are underlined in the endnotes. Any uncommenced\namendments affecting the law are accessible on the Register\n(www.legislation.gov.au).\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions\nIf the operation of a provision or amendment of the compiled law is affected by\nan application, saving or transitional provision that is not included in this\ncompilation, details are included in the endnotes.\nEditorial changes\nFor more information about any editorial changes made in this compilation, see\nthe endnotes.\nPresentational changes\nThe Legislation Act 2003 provides for First Parliamentary Counsel to make\npresentational changes to a compilation. Presentational changes are applied to\ngive a more consistent look and feel to legislation published on the Register,\nand enable the user to more easily navigate those documents.\nModifications\nIf the compiled law is modified by another law, the compiled law operates as\nmodified but the modification does not amend the text of the law. Accordingly,\nthis compilation does not show the text of the compiled law as modified. Any\nmodifications affecting the law are accessible on the Register.\nSelf-repealing provisions\nIf a provision of the compiled law has been repealed in accordance with a\nprovision of the law, details are included in the endnotes.\n\n\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\ni\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nContents\nChapter 1—Preliminary\n3AA\nHomoeopathic preparations and homoeopathic\n3AB\nAnthroposophic preparations and anthroposophic\n3A\n3B\nDeclaration—country covered by non-EC/EFTA\n3C\n5A\nApplication of the Criminal Code—extended\n6AAA\nCommonwealth consent to conferral of functions\netc. on its officers and authorities by\n6AAB\n6AAC\n6AAD\n6AAE\nConsequences of State law conferring duty,\nfunction or power on Commonwealth officer or\n6B\n6C\nDeclaration that goods are/are not therapeutic\n7AAA\nMinister may determine that goods are therapeutic\n7AA\n7A\n7B\n7C\nSecretary may arrange for use of computer\n7D\n\nii\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nPower to obtain information with respect to\nChapter 2—Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods\n9A\n9C\n9D\n9E\n9F\n9G\nCriminal offences for false statements in requests\n9H\nCivil penalty for false statements in requests for\nChapter 2A—Prohibition on import, export,\nmanufacture or supply of therapeutic\ngoods or vaping goods—international\nagreements\n9J\n9K\nProhibition on import, export, manufacture or\nsupply of therapeutic goods or vaping goods—\n9L\n9M\n9N\nChapter 3—Medicines and other therapeutic goods\nthat are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "Includes amendments:\nAct No. 38, 2025\nThis compilation is in 2 volumes\nVolume 1:\nsections 1-41A\nVolume 2:\nsections 41B-69\nEndnotes\nEach volume has its own contents\n\nAbout this compilation\nThis compilation\nThis is a compilation of the Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 that shows the text of\nthe law as amended and in force on 5 September 2025 (the compilation date).\nThe notes at the end of this compilation (the endnotes) include information\nabout amending laws and the amendment history of provisions of the compiled\nlaw.\nUncommenced amendments\nThe effect of uncommenced amendments is not shown in the text of the\ncompiled law. The details of amendments made up to, but not commenced at,\nthe compilation date are underlined in the endnotes. Any uncommenced\namendments affecting the law are accessible on the Register\n(www.legislation.gov.au).\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions\nIf the operation of a provision or amendment of the compiled law is affected by\nan application, saving or transitional provision that is not included in this\ncompilation, details are included in the endnotes.\nEditorial changes\nFor more information about any editorial changes made in this compilation, see\nthe endnotes.\nPresentational changes\nThe Legislation Act 2003 provides for First Parliamentary Counsel to make\npresentational changes to a compilation. Presentational changes are applied to\ngive a more consistent look and feel to legislation published on the Register,\nand enable the user to more easily navigate those documents.\nModifications\nIf the compiled law is modified by another law, the compiled law operates as\nmodified but the modification does not amend the text of the law. Accordingly,\nthis compilation does not show the text of the compiled law as modified. Any\nmodifications affecting the law are accessible on the Register.\nSelf-repealing provisions\nIf a provision of the compiled law has been repealed in accordance with a\nprovision of the law, details are included in the endnotes.\n\n\nThera",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-5-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ac58f4b00e4a79b9c0f4fb8614645f192b3df3b7a2965fd86f5422dd18071ee5",
      "skos:note": "Compilation information and notes on amendments."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 September 2025",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 1,
      "values:originalText": "Includes amendments:\nAct No. 38, 2025\nThis compilation is in 2 volumes\nVolume 1:\nsections 1-41A\nVolume 2:\nsections 41B-69\nEndnotes\nEach volume has its own contents\n\nAbout this compilation\nThis compilation\nThis is a compilation of the Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 that shows the text of\nthe law as amended and in force on 5 September 2025 (the compilation date).\nThe notes at the end of this compilation (the endnotes) include information\nabout amending laws and the amendment history of provisions of the compiled\nlaw.\nUncommenced amendments\nThe effect of uncommenced amendments is not shown in the text of the\ncompiled law. The details of amendments made up to, but not commenced at,\nthe compilation date are underlined in the endnotes. Any uncommenced\namendments affecting the law are accessible on the Register\n(www.legislation.gov.au).\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions\nIf the operation of a provision or amendment of the compiled law is affected by\nan application, saving or transitional provision that is not included in this\ncompilation, details are included in the endnotes.\nEditorial changes\nFor more information about any editorial changes made in this compilation, see\nthe endnotes.\nPresentational changes\nThe Legislation Act 2003 provides for First Parliamentary Counsel to make\npresentational changes to a compilation. Presentational changes are applied to\ngive a more consistent look and feel to legislation published on the Register,\nand enable the user to more easily navigate those documents.\nModifications\nIf the compiled law is modified by another law, the compiled law operates as\nmodified but the modification does not amend the text of the law. Accordingly,\nthis compilation does not show the text of the compiled law as modified. Any\nmodifications affecting the law are accessible on the Register.\nSelf-repealing provisions\nIf a provision of the compiled law has been repealed in accordance with a\nprovision of the law, details are included in the endnotes.\n\n\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\ni\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nContents\nChapter 1—Preliminary\n3AA\nHomoeopathic preparations and homoeopathic\n3AB\nAnthroposophic preparations and anthroposophic\n3A\n3B\nDeclaration—country covered by non-EC/EFTA\n3C\n5A\nApplication of the Criminal Code—extended\n6AAA\nCommonwealth consent to conferral of functions\netc. on its officers and authorities by\n6AAB\n6AAC\n6AAD\n6AAE\nConsequences of State law conferring duty,\nfunction or power on Commonwealth officer or\n6B\n6C\nDeclaration that goods are/are not therapeutic\n7AAA\nMinister may determine that goods are therapeutic\n7AA\n7A\n7B\n7C\nSecretary may arrange for use of computer\n7D\n\nii\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nPower to obtain information with respect to\nChapter 2—Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods\n9A\n9C\n9D\n9E\n9F\n9G\nCriminal offences for false statements in requests\n9H\nCivil penalty for false statements in requests for\nChapter 2A—Prohibition on import, export,\nmanufacture or supply of therapeutic\ngoods or vaping goods—international\nagreements\n9J\n9K\nProhibition on import, export, manufacture or\nsupply of therapeutic goods or vaping goods—\n9L\n9M\n9N\nChapter 3—Medicines and other therapeutic goods\nthat are not medical devices"
    },
