    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3(5) Interpretation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-3-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.17",
      "values:originalText": "(5) For the purposes of this Act, the presentation of therapeutic goods\nis unacceptable if it is capable of being misleading or confusing as\nto the content or proper use or identification of the goods and,\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\n\nSection 3\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nwithout limiting the previous words in this subsection, the\npresentation of therapeutic goods is unacceptable:\n(a) if it states or suggests that the goods have ingredients,\ncomponents or characteristics that they do not have; or\n(b) if a name applied to the goods is the same as the name\napplied to other therapeutic goods that are supplied in\nAustralia where those other goods contain additional or\ndifferent therapeutically active ingredients; or\n(c) if the label of the goods does not declare the presence of a\ntherapeutically active ingredient; or\n(ca) if the therapeutic goods are medicine included in a class of\nmedicine prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of\nthis paragraph—if the medicine’s label does not contain the\nadvisory statements specified under subsection (5A) in\nrelation to the medicine; or\n(d) if a form of presentation of the goods may lead to unsafe use\nof the goods or suggests a purpose that is not in accordance\nwith conditions applicable to the supply of the goods in\nAustralia; or\n(e) in prescribed cases.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) For the purposes of this Act, the presentation of therapeutic goods\nis unacceptable if it is capable of being misleading or confusing as\nto the content or proper use or identification of the goods and,\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\n\nSection 3\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nwithout limiting the previous words in this subsection, the\npresentation of therapeutic goods is unacceptable:\n(a) if it states or suggests that the goods have ingredients,\ncomponents or characteristics that they do not have; or\n(b) if a name applied to the goods is the same as the name\napplied to other therapeutic goods that are supplied in\nAustralia where those other goods contain additional or\ndifferent therapeutically active ingredients; or\n(c) if the label of the goods does not declare the presence of a\ntherapeutically active ingredient; or\n(ca) if the therapeutic goods are medicine included in a class of\nmedicine prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of\nthis paragraph—if the medicine’s label does not contain the\nadvisory statements specified under subsection (5A) in\nrelation to the medicine; or\n(d) if a form of presentation of the goods may lead to unsafe use\nof the goods or suggests a purpose that is not in accordance\nwith conditions applicable to the supply of the goods in\nAustralia; or\n(e) in prescribed cases.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3-ss-5-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3-ss-5-logic-ltl-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3-ss-5-logic-diffusion-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3-ss-5-logic-cogai-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8f5ef4ffcf78372c7ffab9926afb5106f4af2072d9972353c2b2d2dfc6236662",
      "skos:note": "Presentation of therapeutic goods is unacceptable if it is capable of being misleading or confusing."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-3-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3(5) Interpretation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 17,
      "values:originalText": "(5) For the purposes of this Act, the presentation of therapeutic goods\nis unacceptable if it is capable of being misleading or confusing as\nto the content or proper use or identification of the goods and,\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\n\nSection 3\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nwithout limiting the previous words in this subsection, the\npresentation of therapeutic goods is unacceptable:\n(a) if it states or suggests that the goods have ingredients,\ncomponents or characteristics that they do not have; or\n(b) if a name applied to the goods is the same as the name\napplied to other therapeutic goods that are supplied in\nAustralia where those other goods contain additional or\ndifferent therapeutically active ingredients; or\n(c) if the label of the goods does not declare the presence of a\ntherapeutically active ingredient; or\n(ca) if the therapeutic goods are medicine included in a class of\nmedicine prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of\nthis paragraph—if the medicine’s label does not contain the\nadvisory statements specified under subsection (5A) in\nrelation to the medicine; or\n(d) if a form of presentation of the goods may lead to unsafe use\nof the goods or suggests a purpose that is not in accordance\nwith conditions applicable to the supply of the goods in\nAustralia; or\n(e) in prescribed cases."
    },
