    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3aa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3AA Homoeopathic preparations and homoeopathic standards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-3aa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.39",
      "values:originalText": "Homoeopathic preparation\n(1) For the purposes of this Act, a homoeopathic preparation is a\npreparation:\n(a) manufactured from a mother substance; and\n(b) manufactured in accordance with a manufacturing procedure\ndescribed in a homoeopathic pharmacopoeia.\nHomoeopathic standard\n(2) For the purposes of this Act, if:\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\n\nSection 3AA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) there are therapeutic goods that are a homoeopathic\npreparation; and\n(b) the goods are the subject of one or more monographs (other\nthan a monograph exempt under subsection (4)) in the\nhomoeopathic pharmacopoeia describing the manufacturing\nprocedure that the preparation was manufactured in\naccordance with;\nthen there is a homoeopathic standard, in relation to the goods,\nthat is constituted by the statements (other than statements exempt\nunder subsection (5)) in those monographs, as interpreted in\naccordance with any interpretation sections of that homoeopathic\npharmacopoeia.\nSpecifying publications\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify either or both\nof the following for the purposes of the definition of homoeopathic\npharmacopoeia in subsection 3(1):\n(a) publications;\n(b) parts of publications.\nExempting entire monographs\n(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nspecified monographs in a specified homoeopathic pharmacopoeia\nare exempt for the purposes of paragraph (2)(b).\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\nExempting parts of monographs\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nspecified statements in specified monographs in a specified\nhomoeopathic pharmacopoeia are exempt for the purposes of\nsubsection (2).\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\n\nSection 3AB\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "Homoeopathic preparation\n(1) For the purposes of this Act, a homoeopathic preparation is a\npreparation:\n(a) manufactured from a mother substance; and\n(b) manufactured in accordance with a manufacturing procedure\ndescribed in a homoeopathic pharmacopoeia.\nHomoeopathic standard\n(2) For the purposes of this Act, if:\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\n\nSection 3AA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) there are therapeutic goods that are a homoeopathic\npreparation; and\n(b) the goods are the subject of one or more monographs (other\nthan a monograph exempt under subsection (4)) in the\nhomoeopathic pharmacopoeia describing the manufacturing\nprocedure that the preparation was manufactured in\naccordance with;\nthen there is a homoeopathic standard, in relation to the goods,\nthat is constituted by the statements (other than statements exempt\nunder subsection (5)) in those monographs, as interpreted in\naccordance with any interpretation sections of that homoeopathic\npharmacopoeia.\nSpecifying publications\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify either or both\nof the following for the purposes of the definition of homoeopathic\npharmacopoeia in subsection 3(1):\n(a) publications;\n(b) parts of publications.\nExempting entire monographs\n(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nspecified monographs in a specified homoeopathic pharmacopoeia\nare exempt for the purposes of paragraph (2)(b).\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\nExempting parts of monographs\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nspecified statements in specified monographs in a specified\nhomoeopathic pharmacopoeia are exempt for the purposes of\nsubsection (2).\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\n\nSection 3AB\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3aa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3aa-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3aa-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3aa-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3aa-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3383fc12fd184a212b036669080fed02cfce6c85a65900defc3d341e2543595c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-3aa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3AA Homoeopathic preparations and homoeopathic standards",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 39,
      "values:originalText": "Homoeopathic preparation\n(1) For the purposes of this Act, a homoeopathic preparation is a\npreparation:\n(a) manufactured from a mother substance; and\n(b) manufactured in accordance with a manufacturing procedure\ndescribed in a homoeopathic pharmacopoeia.\nHomoeopathic standard\n(2) For the purposes of this Act, if:\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\n\nSection 3AA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) there are therapeutic goods that are a homoeopathic\npreparation; and\n(b) the goods are the subject of one or more monographs (other\nthan a monograph exempt under subsection (4)) in the\nhomoeopathic pharmacopoeia describing the manufacturing\nprocedure that the preparation was manufactured in\naccordance with;\nthen there is a homoeopathic standard, in relation to the goods,\nthat is constituted by the statements (other than statements exempt\nunder subsection (5)) in those monographs, as interpreted in\naccordance with any interpretation sections of that homoeopathic\npharmacopoeia.\nSpecifying publications\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify either or both\nof the following for the purposes of the definition of homoeopathic\npharmacopoeia in subsection 3(1):\n(a) publications;\n(b) parts of publications.\nExempting entire monographs\n(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nspecified monographs in a specified homoeopathic pharmacopoeia\nare exempt for the purposes of paragraph (2)(b).\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\nExempting parts of monographs\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nspecified statements in specified monographs in a specified\nhomoeopathic pharmacopoeia are exempt for the purposes of\nsubsection (2).\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\n\nSection 3AB\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
