    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3C Exempting monographs in pharmacopoeias",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-3c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.43",
      "values:originalText": "Exempting entire monographs\n(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nspecified monographs in the British Pharmacopoeia, the European\nPharmacopoeia or the United States Pharmacopeia-National\nFormulary are exempt in relation to specified therapeutic goods for\nthe purposes of paragraph (b), (c) or (d) of the definition of\nstandard in subsection 3(1). The determination applies to those\nmonographs as in force from time to time.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\nExempting parts of monographs\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nspecified statements in specified monographs in the British\nPharmacopoeia, the European Pharmacopoeia or the United States\nPharmacopeia-National Formulary are exempt in relation to\nspecified therapeutic goods for the purposes of paragraph (b), (c)\nor (d) of the definition of standard in subsection 3(1). The\ndetermination applies to those statements and monographs as in\nforce from time to time.\nIncorporation of other instruments\n(3) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, a\ndetermination under subsection (1) or (2) of this section may make\nprovision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting or\nincorporating, with or without modification, any matter contained\nin an instrument or other writing as in force or existing from time\nto time.",
      "skos:definition": "Exempting entire monographs\n(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nspecified monographs in the British Pharmacopoeia, the European\nPharmacopoeia or the United States Pharmacopeia-National\nFormulary are exempt in relation to specified therapeutic goods for\nthe purposes of paragraph (b), (c) or (d) of the definition of\nstandard in subsection 3(1). The determination applies to those\nmonographs as in force from time to time.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\nExempting parts of monographs\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nspecified statements in specified monographs in the British\nPharmacopoeia, the European Pharmacopoeia or the United States\nPharmacopeia-National Formulary are exempt in relation to\nspecified therapeutic goods for the purposes of paragraph (b), (c)\nor (d) of the definition of standard in subsection 3(1). The\ndetermination applies to those statements and monographs as in\nforce from time to time.\nIncorporation of other instruments\n(3) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, a\ndetermination under subsection (1) or (2) of this section may make\nprovision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting or\nincorporating, with or without modification, any matter contained\nin an instrument or other writing as in force or existing from time\nto time.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3c-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-3c-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "76e928dcfd1bf39452eac3f6689a84a5d9ec084d04dde922c23dc544cc24e1a2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-3c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3C Exempting monographs in pharmacopoeias",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 43,
      "values:originalText": "Exempting entire monographs\n(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nspecified monographs in the British Pharmacopoeia, the European\nPharmacopoeia or the United States Pharmacopeia-National\nFormulary are exempt in relation to specified therapeutic goods for\nthe purposes of paragraph (b), (c) or (d) of the definition of\nstandard in subsection 3(1). The determination applies to those\nmonographs as in force from time to time.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\nExempting parts of monographs\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nspecified statements in specified monographs in the British\nPharmacopoeia, the European Pharmacopoeia or the United States\nPharmacopeia-National Formulary are exempt in relation to\nspecified therapeutic goods for the purposes of paragraph (b), (c)\nor (d) of the definition of standard in subsection 3(1). The\ndetermination applies to those statements and monographs as in\nforce from time to time.\nIncorporation of other instruments\n(3) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, a\ndetermination under subsection (1) or (2) of this section may make\nprovision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting or\nincorporating, with or without modification, any matter contained\nin an instrument or other writing as in force or existing from time\nto time."
    },
