      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Applicable",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Requires temporal relation between instrument and writing",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Temporal intervals mentioned",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Undertaking"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 Objects of Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.43",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The objects of this Act are to do the following, so far as the\nConstitution permits:\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\n\nSection 5\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) provide for the establishment and maintenance of a national\nsystem of controls relating to the quality, safety, efficacy and\ntimely availability of therapeutic goods that are:\n(i) used in Australia, whether produced in Australia or\nelsewhere; or\n(ii) exported from Australia;\n(b) to provide a framework for the States and Territories to adopt\na uniform approach to control the availability and\naccessibility, and ensure the safe handling, of poisons in\nAustralia;\n(c) provide for a scheme allowing pharmacists to substitute\ncertain medicine for other medicine if the Minister has\ndeclared there is a serious scarcity of the other medicine;\n(d) provide for the establishment and maintenance of a national\nsystem of controls relating to the regulation of vaping goods\nthat are:\n(i) imported into Australia; or\n(ii) manufactured in Australia; or\n(iii) supplied in Australia, whether manufactured in\nAustralia or elsewhere; or\n(iv) exported from Australia.\n(1A) The reference in paragraph (1)(a) to the efficacy of therapeutic\ngoods is a reference, if the goods are medical devices, to the\nperformance of the devices as the manufacturer intended.\n(2) This Act is therefore not intended to apply to the exclusion of a law\nof a State, of the Australian Capital Territory or of the Northern\nTerritory to the extent that the law is capable of operating\nconcurrently with this Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The objects of this Act are to do the following, so far as the\nConstitution permits:\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\n\nSection 5\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) provide for the establishment and maintenance of a national\nsystem of controls relating to the quality, safety, efficacy and\ntimely availability of therapeutic goods that are:\n(i) used in Australia, whether produced in Australia or\nelsewhere; or\n(ii) exported from Australia;\n(b) to provide a framework for the States and Territories to adopt\na uniform approach to control the availability and\naccessibility, and ensure the safe handling, of poisons in\nAustralia;\n(c) provide for a scheme allowing pharmacists to substitute\ncertain medicine for other medicine if the Minister has\ndeclared there is a serious scarcity of the other medicine;\n(d) provide for the establishment and maintenance of a national\nsystem of controls relating to the regulation of vaping goods\nthat are:\n(i) imported into Australia; or\n(ii) manufactured in Australia; or\n(iii) supplied in Australia, whether manufactured in\nAustralia or elsewhere; or\n(iv) exported from Australia.\n(1A) The reference in paragraph (1)(a) to the efficacy of therapeutic\ngoods is a reference, if the goods are medical devices, to the\nperformance of the devices as the manufacturer intended.\n(2) This Act is therefore not intended to apply to the exclusion of a law\nof a State, of the Australian Capital Territory or of the Northern\nTerritory to the extent that the law is capable of operating\nconcurrently with this Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-4-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-4-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-4-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ddb8e56a2fcd0ea3911e4db4a704d057f86312cd87063c380b363159aba23932"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 Objects of Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 43,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The objects of this Act are to do the following, so far as the\nConstitution permits:\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\n\nSection 5\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) provide for the establishment and maintenance of a national\nsystem of controls relating to the quality, safety, efficacy and\ntimely availability of therapeutic goods that are:\n(i) used in Australia, whether produced in Australia or\nelsewhere; or\n(ii) exported from Australia;\n(b) to provide a framework for the States and Territories to adopt\na uniform approach to control the availability and\naccessibility, and ensure the safe handling, of poisons in\nAustralia;\n(c) provide for a scheme allowing pharmacists to substitute\ncertain medicine for other medicine if the Minister has\ndeclared there is a serious scarcity of the other medicine;\n(d) provide for the establishment and maintenance of a national\nsystem of controls relating to the regulation of vaping goods\nthat are:\n(i) imported into Australia; or\n(ii) manufactured in Australia; or\n(iii) supplied in Australia, whether manufactured in\nAustralia or elsewhere; or\n(iv) exported from Australia.\n(1A) The reference in paragraph (1)(a) to the efficacy of therapeutic\ngoods is a reference, if the goods are medical devices, to the\nperformance of the devices as the manufacturer intended.\n(2) This Act is therefore not intended to apply to the exclusion of a law\nof a State, of the Australian Capital Territory or of the Northern\nTerritory to the extent that the law is capable of operating\nconcurrently with this Act."
    },
