    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-7a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7A Authorised persons",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-7a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.53",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may, in writing, authorise any of the following\npersons to exercise powers under a specified provision of this Act:\n(a) an officer of the Department, of another Department or of an\nauthority of the Commonwealth;\n(b) an officer of:\n(i) a Department of State of a State; or\n(ii) a Department or administrative unit of the Public\nService of a Territory; or\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\n\nSection 7B\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(iii) an authority of a State or of a Territory;\nbeing a Department, unit or authority that has functions\nrelating to health matters or law enforcement matters.\n(2) In exercising a power under a provision of this Act under an\nauthorisation under subsection (1), the authorised person must\ncomply with any directions of the Secretary.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary may, in writing, authorise any of the following\npersons to exercise powers under a specified provision of this Act:\n(a) an officer of the Department, of another Department or of an\nauthority of the Commonwealth;\n(b) an officer of:\n(i) a Department of State of a State; or\n(ii) a Department or administrative unit of the Public\nService of a Territory; or\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\n\nSection 7B\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(iii) an authority of a State or of a Territory;\nbeing a Department, unit or authority that has functions\nrelating to health matters or law enforcement matters.\n(2) In exercising a power under a provision of this Act under an\nauthorisation under subsection (1), the authorised person must\ncomply with any directions of the Secretary.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-7a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-7a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3c8e73b31a0d86e983b15656d7421ab2bf89647be34c1a12308595b56417c0a4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-7a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7A Authorised persons",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 53,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may, in writing, authorise any of the following\npersons to exercise powers under a specified provision of this Act:\n(a) an officer of the Department, of another Department or of an\nauthority of the Commonwealth;\n(b) an officer of:\n(i) a Department of State of a State; or\n(ii) a Department or administrative unit of the Public\nService of a Territory; or\n\nChapter 1  Preliminary\n\nSection 7B\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(iii) an authority of a State or of a Territory;\nbeing a Department, unit or authority that has functions\nrelating to health matters or law enforcement matters.\n(2) In exercising a power under a provision of this Act under an\nauthorisation under subsection (1), the authorised person must\ncomply with any directions of the Secretary."
    },
