      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Directions are given at some point in time.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Action must occur after directions are given."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-7b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7B Kits",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-7b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.54",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a package contains one or more goods, the package and each of\nthe goods in the package together constitute a kit for the purposes\nof this Act if:\n(a) the package and each of the goods are for use as a unit; and\n(b) the package and the goods do not constitute a composite\npack; and\n(c) at least one of the goods is therapeutic goods; and\n(d) each item of the therapeutic goods consists of goods that are:\n(i) registered or listed; or\n(ii) exempt goods in relation to Part 3-2; or\n(iii) included in the Register under Part 3-2A; or\n(iv) exempt under subsection 32CA(2) or section 32CB.\n(2) A package and therapeutic goods in the package together constitute\na composite pack if:\n(a) the therapeutic goods are of 2 or more kinds; and\n(b) the package does not contain any medical devices; and\n(c) the therapeutic goods are for administration as a single\ntreatment or as a single course of treatment; and\n(d) it is necessary that the therapeutic goods be combined before\nadministration or that they be administered in a particular\nsequence.\n(3) To avoid doubt, it is declared that a kit constitutes therapeutic\ngoods.\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\n\nSection 7C\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a package contains one or more goods, the package and each of\nthe goods in the package together constitute a kit for the purposes\nof this Act if:\n(a) the package and each of the goods are for use as a unit; and\n(b) the package and the goods do not constitute a composite\npack; and\n(c) at least one of the goods is therapeutic goods; and\n(d) each item of the therapeutic goods consists of goods that are:\n(i) registered or listed; or\n(ii) exempt goods in relation to Part 3-2; or\n(iii) included in the Register under Part 3-2A; or\n(iv) exempt under subsection 32CA(2) or section 32CB.\n(2) A package and therapeutic goods in the package together constitute\na composite pack if:\n(a) the therapeutic goods are of 2 or more kinds; and\n(b) the package does not contain any medical devices; and\n(c) the therapeutic goods are for administration as a single\ntreatment or as a single course of treatment; and\n(d) it is necessary that the therapeutic goods be combined before\nadministration or that they be administered in a particular\nsequence.\n(3) To avoid doubt, it is declared that a kit constitutes therapeutic\ngoods.\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\n\nSection 7C\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-7b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-7b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-7b-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6996cb950cac1eb773c007ecd51838adceff206c04e21ae28a5f1a5e3ec47bd3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-7b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7B Kits",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 54,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a package contains one or more goods, the package and each of\nthe goods in the package together constitute a kit for the purposes\nof this Act if:\n(a) the package and each of the goods are for use as a unit; and\n(b) the package and the goods do not constitute a composite\npack; and\n(c) at least one of the goods is therapeutic goods; and\n(d) each item of the therapeutic goods consists of goods that are:\n(i) registered or listed; or\n(ii) exempt goods in relation to Part 3-2; or\n(iii) included in the Register under Part 3-2A; or\n(iv) exempt under subsection 32CA(2) or section 32CB.\n(2) A package and therapeutic goods in the package together constitute\na composite pack if:\n(a) the therapeutic goods are of 2 or more kinds; and\n(b) the package does not contain any medical devices; and\n(c) the therapeutic goods are for administration as a single\ntreatment or as a single course of treatment; and\n(d) it is necessary that the therapeutic goods be combined before\nadministration or that they be administered in a particular\nsequence.\n(3) To avoid doubt, it is declared that a kit constitutes therapeutic\ngoods.\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\n\nSection 7C\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
