    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-7c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7C Secretary may arrange for use of computer programs to make",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-7c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "decisions\n(1) The Secretary may arrange for the use, under the Secretary’s\ncontrol, of computer programs for any purposes for which the\nSecretary may make decisions under this Act or the regulations.\n(2) A decision made by the operation of a computer program under\nsuch an arrangement is taken to be a decision made by the\nSecretary.\n(3) The Secretary may substitute a decision (the substituted decision)\nfor a decision (the initial decision) made by the operation of a\ncomputer program under such an arrangement if the Secretary is\nsatisfied that the initial decision is incorrect.\n(4) However, the substituted decision may only be made before the\nend of the period of 60 days beginning on the day the initial\ndecision is made.",
      "skos:definition": "decisions\n(1) The Secretary may arrange for the use, under the Secretary’s\ncontrol, of computer programs for any purposes for which the\nSecretary may make decisions under this Act or the regulations.\n(2) A decision made by the operation of a computer program under\nsuch an arrangement is taken to be a decision made by the\nSecretary.\n(3) The Secretary may substitute a decision (the substituted decision)\nfor a decision (the initial decision) made by the operation of a\ncomputer program under such an arrangement if the Secretary is\nsatisfied that the initial decision is incorrect.\n(4) However, the substituted decision may only be made before the\nend of the period of 60 days beginning on the day the initial\ndecision is made.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-7c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-7c-ss-2"
        },
