    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 Arrangements with States etc.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.56",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may make arrangements with the appropriate\nMinister of a State, of the Australian Capital Territory or of the\nNorthern Territory for the carrying out by that State or Territory,\non behalf of the Commonwealth, of:\n(a) the evaluation of therapeutic goods for registration; or\n(aa) the evaluation of a biological, other than a Class 1 biological\nor an export only biological, for inclusion in the Register\nunder Part 3-2A; or\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\n\nSection 9\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) the inspection of manufacturers of therapeutic goods; or\n(c) other functions under this Act or the regulations.\n(2) An arrangement under this section may provide for the payment to\na State or Territory of amounts in respect of the performance of\nfunctions under the arrangement.\n\nChapter 2  Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods\n\nSection 9A\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nChapter 2—Australian Register of\nTherapeutic Goods",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may make arrangements with the appropriate\nMinister of a State, of the Australian Capital Territory or of the\nNorthern Territory for the carrying out by that State or Territory,\non behalf of the Commonwealth, of:\n(a) the evaluation of therapeutic goods for registration; or\n(aa) the evaluation of a biological, other than a Class 1 biological\nor an export only biological, for inclusion in the Register\nunder Part 3-2A; or\n\nPreliminary  Chapter 1\n\nSection 9\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) the inspection of manufacturers of therapeutic goods; or\n(c) other functions under this Act or the regulations.\n(2) An arrangement under this section may provide for the payment to\na State or Territory of amounts in respect of the performance of\nfunctions under the arrangement.\n\nChapter 2  Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods\n\nSection 9A\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nChapter 2—Australian Register of\nTherapeutic Goods",
