    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9A Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.58",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary is to cause to be maintained a register, to be known\nas the Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods, for the purpose of\ncompiling information in relation to, and providing for evaluation\nof, therapeutic goods for use in humans.\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), the Register is to be kept in such form as\nthe Secretary determines.\n(3) The Register is to contain these 5 parts:\n(a) a part for goods to be known as registered goods; and\n(aa) a part for goods to be known as provisionally registered\ngoods; and\n(b) a part for goods to be known as listed goods; and\n(ba) a part for biologicals included in the Register under",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary is to cause to be maintained a register, to be known\nas the Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods, for the purpose of\ncompiling information in relation to, and providing for evaluation\nof, therapeutic goods for use in humans.\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), the Register is to be kept in such form as\nthe Secretary determines.\n(3) The Register is to contain these 5 parts:\n(a) a part for goods to be known as registered goods; and\n(aa) a part for goods to be known as provisionally registered\ngoods; and\n(b) a part for goods to be known as listed goods; and\n(ba) a part for biologicals included in the Register under",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5bec89d0baf53c563934e4d42b5400bf18ac2f91e22fdbdcbc33211c0e47ec0c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9A Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 58,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary is to cause to be maintained a register, to be known\nas the Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods, for the purpose of\ncompiling information in relation to, and providing for evaluation\nof, therapeutic goods for use in humans.\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), the Register is to be kept in such form as\nthe Secretary determines.\n(3) The Register is to contain these 5 parts:\n(a) a part for goods to be known as registered goods; and\n(aa) a part for goods to be known as provisionally registered\ngoods; and\n(b) a part for goods to be known as listed goods; and\n(ba) a part for biologicals included in the Register under"
