    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9a-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9A(3) Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9a-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.58",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The Register is to contain these 5 parts:\n(a) a part for goods to be known as registered goods; and\n(aa) a part for goods to be known as provisionally registered\ngoods; and\n(b) a part for goods to be known as listed goods; and\n(ba) a part for biologicals included in the Register under",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The Register is to contain these 5 parts:\n(a) a part for goods to be known as registered goods; and\n(aa) a part for goods to be known as provisionally registered\ngoods; and\n(b) a part for goods to be known as listed goods; and\n(ba) a part for biologicals included in the Register under",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9a-ss-3-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5b71051ed32004df1a11d6a089c0cd34461efbfa16116f8a988de21e81398973",
      "skos:note": "Classification of goods in the Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9a-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9A(3) Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 58,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The Register is to contain these 5 parts:\n(a) a part for goods to be known as registered goods; and\n(aa) a part for goods to be known as provisionally registered\ngoods; and\n(b) a part for goods to be known as listed goods; and\n(ba) a part for biologicals included in the Register under"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9a-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9a-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9C Inspection of entries in Register",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.59",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person in relation to whom therapeutic goods are entered on the\nRegister may make a written request to the Secretary for a copy of\nthe entry in the Register in relation to the goods.\n(2) If the person makes such a request, the Secretary must send to the\nperson a copy of so much (if any) of that entry as is contained in\nany computer database maintained by the Department for purposes\nconnected with the administration of this Act (other than any part\nof that entry that was supplied in confidence by another person).\n(3) If the person makes such a request, then, instead of providing a\ncopy of an entry to the person, the Secretary may, if the request is\nfor the provision of an electronic copy, provide the information\ncontained in the entry:\n(a) on a data processing device; or\n(b) by way of electronic transmission.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person in relation to whom therapeutic goods are entered on the\nRegister may make a written request to the Secretary for a copy of\nthe entry in the Register in relation to the goods.\n(2) If the person makes such a request, the Secretary must send to the\nperson a copy of so much (if any) of that entry as is contained in\nany computer database maintained by the Department for purposes\nconnected with the administration of this Act (other than any part\nof that entry that was supplied in confidence by another person).\n(3) If the person makes such a request, then, instead of providing a\ncopy of an entry to the person, the Secretary may, if the request is\nfor the provision of an electronic copy, provide the information\ncontained in the entry:\n(a) on a data processing device; or\n(b) by way of electronic transmission.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9c-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9c-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2f1fdfe0f02179cd93bed8a9ae9430278addc08b62938a8fec327c78c57b0a80"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9C Inspection of entries in Register",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 59,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person in relation to whom therapeutic goods are entered on the\nRegister may make a written request to the Secretary for a copy of\nthe entry in the Register in relation to the goods.\n(2) If the person makes such a request, the Secretary must send to the\nperson a copy of so much (if any) of that entry as is contained in\nany computer database maintained by the Department for purposes\nconnected with the administration of this Act (other than any part\nof that entry that was supplied in confidence by another person).\n(3) If the person makes such a request, then, instead of providing a\ncopy of an entry to the person, the Secretary may, if the request is\nfor the provision of an electronic copy, provide the information\ncontained in the entry:\n(a) on a data processing device; or\n(b) by way of electronic transmission."
    },
