    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9d-ss-1c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9D(1C) Variation of entries in Register",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9d-ss-1c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.59",
      "values:originalText": "(1C) If the Secretary proposes to make a variation under subsection (1A)\nor (1B), the Secretary must:\n(a) give the person in relation to whom the medicine is registered\nwritten notice of the proposed variation and of the reasons for\nthe proposed variation; and\n(b) give the person a reasonable opportunity to make a\nsubmission to the Secretary in relation to the proposed\nvariation; and\n\nAustralian Register of Therapeutic Goods  Chapter 2\n\nSection 9D\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(c) if the person makes a submission in accordance with\nparagraph (b)—take the submission into account before\nmaking a decision whether or not to make the variation.",
      "skos:definition": "(1C) If the Secretary proposes to make a variation under subsection (1A)\nor (1B), the Secretary must:\n(a) give the person in relation to whom the medicine is registered\nwritten notice of the proposed variation and of the reasons for\nthe proposed variation; and\n(b) give the person a reasonable opportunity to make a\nsubmission to the Secretary in relation to the proposed\nvariation; and\n\nAustralian Register of Therapeutic Goods  Chapter 2\n\nSection 9D\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(c) if the person makes a submission in accordance with\nparagraph (b)—take the submission into account before\nmaking a decision whether or not to make the variation.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9d"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9d-ss-1c-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9d-ss-1c-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9d-ss-1c-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "85142cccf63885ba5352f3f582139f32a1a19c4606a818191d4c8252a6a97801",
      "skos:note": "Secretary must give notice and opportunity to submit before making variation.",
      "dc:description": "written notice, submission"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9d-ss-1c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9D(1C) Variation of entries in Register",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 59,
      "values:originalText": "(1C) If the Secretary proposes to make a variation under subsection (1A)\nor (1B), the Secretary must:\n(a) give the person in relation to whom the medicine is registered\nwritten notice of the proposed variation and of the reasons for\nthe proposed variation; and\n(b) give the person a reasonable opportunity to make a\nsubmission to the Secretary in relation to the proposed\nvariation; and\n\nAustralian Register of Therapeutic Goods  Chapter 2\n\nSection 9D\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(c) if the person makes a submission in accordance with\nparagraph (b)—take the submission into account before\nmaking a decision whether or not to make the variation."
    },
