      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(6) The Secretary may, by writing:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9d-ss-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9D(7) Variation of entries in Register",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9d-ss-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.59",
      "values:originalText": "(7) If:\n\nAustralian Register of Therapeutic Goods  Chapter 2\n\nSection 9E\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the Secretary has approved a form for, and the manner of\nmaking, a kind of request under this section; and\n(b) either:\n(i) the kind of request is one under subsection (3) and\nwhich, under the regulations, must be decided within\n175 or 255 working days; or\n(ii) the kind of request is one prescribed by the regulations\nfor the purposes of this subparagraph;\nthen a request of that kind is not effective unless:\n(c) the request is in accordance with that form; and\n(d) the request contains the information required by that form;\nand\n(e) the request is made in that manner; and\n(f) any prescribed application fee has been paid; and\n(g) the request is accompanied by information that is:\n(i) of a kind determined under subsection (8); and\n(ii) in a form approved, in writing, by the Secretary.",
      "skos:definition": "(7) If:\n\nAustralian Register of Therapeutic Goods  Chapter 2\n\nSection 9E\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the Secretary has approved a form for, and the manner of\nmaking, a kind of request under this section; and\n(b) either:\n(i) the kind of request is one under subsection (3) and\nwhich, under the regulations, must be decided within\n175 or 255 working days; or\n(ii) the kind of request is one prescribed by the regulations\nfor the purposes of this subparagraph;\nthen a request of that kind is not effective unless:\n(c) the request is in accordance with that form; and\n(d) the request contains the information required by that form;\nand\n(e) the request is made in that manner; and\n(f) any prescribed application fee has been paid; and\n(g) the request is accompanied by information that is:\n(i) of a kind determined under subsection (8); and\n(ii) in a form approved, in writing, by the Secretary.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9d"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9d-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9d-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9d-ss-7-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "78820e3d3a70dc5784d0360e97d151428bf9c084ae08c0fbe6bfe1790a946453",
      "skos:note": "Request for variation of entries in Register must comply with approved form and contain required information.",
      "dc:description": "Form, information, application fee, and prescribed documentation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9d-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9D(7) Variation of entries in Register",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 59,
      "values:originalText": "(7) If:\n\nAustralian Register of Therapeutic Goods  Chapter 2\n\nSection 9E\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the Secretary has approved a form for, and the manner of\nmaking, a kind of request under this section; and\n(b) either:\n(i) the kind of request is one under subsection (3) and\nwhich, under the regulations, must be decided within\n175 or 255 working days; or\n(ii) the kind of request is one prescribed by the regulations\nfor the purposes of this subparagraph;\nthen a request of that kind is not effective unless:\n(c) the request is in accordance with that form; and\n(d) the request contains the information required by that form;\nand\n(e) the request is made in that manner; and\n(f) any prescribed application fee has been paid; and\n(g) the request is accompanied by information that is:\n(i) of a kind determined under subsection (8); and\n(ii) in a form approved, in writing, by the Secretary."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9d-ss-7-norm",
