    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9G Criminal offences for false statements in requests for variation of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "entries in Register\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in or in connection with a request\nunder section 9D for the variation of an entry in the Register\nin relation to therapeutic goods; and\n\nAustralian Register of Therapeutic Goods  Chapter 2\n\nSection 9G\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular;\nand\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of the goods has resulted in, will result in, or is\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the goods, if the goods were used, would\nresult in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury\nto any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in or in connection with a request\nunder section 9D for the variation of an entry in the Register\nin relation to therapeutic goods; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in or in connection with a request\nunder section 9D for the variation of an entry in the Register\nin relation to therapeutic goods; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(6) An offence against subsection (5) is an offence of strict liability.\n\nChapter 2  Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods\n\nSection 9H\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "entries in Register\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in or in connection with a request\nunder section 9D for the variation of an entry in the Register\nin relation to therapeutic goods; and\n\nAustralian Register of Therapeutic Goods  Chapter 2\n\nSection 9G\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular;\nand\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of the goods has resulted in, will result in, or is\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the goods, if the goods were used, would\nresult in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury\nto any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in or in connection with a request\nunder section 9D for the variation of an entry in the Register\nin relation to therapeutic goods; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in or in connection with a request\nunder section 9D for the variation of an entry in the Register\nin relation to therapeutic goods; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(6) An offence against subsection (5) is an offence of strict liability.\n\nChapter 2  Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods\n\nSection 9H\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9g-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9g-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9g-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9g-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8a2cf7facb7b9373af2789f3f8774361565cd5291d5e460ff55ff32a7154e1b3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9G Criminal offences for false statements in requests for variation of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 66,
      "values:originalText": "entries in Register\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in or in connection with a request\nunder section 9D for the variation of an entry in the Register\nin relation to therapeutic goods; and\n\nAustralian Register of Therapeutic Goods  Chapter 2\n\nSection 9G\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular;\nand\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of the goods has resulted in, will result in, or is\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the goods, if the goods were used, would\nresult in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury\nto any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in or in connection with a request\nunder section 9D for the variation of an entry in the Register\nin relation to therapeutic goods; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in or in connection with a request\nunder section 9D for the variation of an entry in the Register\nin relation to therapeutic goods; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(6) An offence against subsection (5) is an offence of strict liability.\n\nChapter 2  Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods\n\nSection 9H\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
