    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9J Simplified outline of this Chapter",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.69",
      "values:originalText": "The regulations may prohibit imports into Australia, exports from\nAustralia, the manufacture in Australia and supplies in Australia of\ntherapeutic goods or vaping goods, or therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods containing a particular ingredient or component, to give\neffect to international agreements to which Australia is a party.\nThere is an offence and a civil penalty for contravening such a\nprohibition.",
      "skos:definition": "The regulations may prohibit imports into Australia, exports from\nAustralia, the manufacture in Australia and supplies in Australia of\ntherapeutic goods or vaping goods, or therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods containing a particular ingredient or component, to give\neffect to international agreements to which Australia is a party.\nThere is an offence and a civil penalty for contravening such a\nprohibition.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9j-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9j-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9j-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f5d6023a0da9969ac44554361e9d3c51868f29fffc9f43a94565cfb7ecf7f812",
      "skos:note": "Regulations may prohibit imports, exports, manufacture, and supplies of certain goods."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9J Simplified outline of this Chapter",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 69,
      "values:originalText": "The regulations may prohibit imports into Australia, exports from\nAustralia, the manufacture in Australia and supplies in Australia of\ntherapeutic goods or vaping goods, or therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods containing a particular ingredient or component, to give\neffect to international agreements to which Australia is a party.\nThere is an offence and a civil penalty for contravening such a\nprohibition."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9j-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9j"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9j-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Regulations prohibit imports, exports, manufacture, and supplies of certain goods.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9j-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Temporal Interval",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Regulations apply to imports, exports, manufacture, and supplies within a specific temporal interval.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9k",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9K Prohibition on import, export, manufacture or supply of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9k"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.69",
      "values:originalText": "therapeutic goods or vaping goods—international\nagreements\nProhibition on therapeutic goods or vaping goods themselves\n(1) If therapeutic goods or vaping goods are the subject of an\ninternational agreement prescribed for the purposes of this\nsubsection, the regulations may prohibit one or more of the\nfollowing:\n(a) the import into Australia of the therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods;\n(b) the export from Australia of the therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods;\n(c) the manufacture in Australia of the therapeutic goods or\nvaping goods;\n\nChapter 2A  Prohibition on import, export, manufacture or supply of therapeutic goods\nor vaping goods—international agreements\n\nSection 9K\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(d) the supply in Australia of the therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods.\n(2) Before regulations are made prescribing an international agreement\nfor the purposes of subsection (1), the Minister must be satisfied\nthat the agreement requires parties to the agreement to take steps to\nprohibit or restrict one or more of the import, export, manufacture\nand supply of certain goods.\nProhibition on therapeutic goods or vaping goods containing an\ningredient or component\n(3) If an ingredient or component of therapeutic goods or vaping goods\nis the subject of an international agreement prescribed for the\npurposes of this subsection, the regulations may prohibit one or\nmore of the following:\n(a) the import into Australia of all or specified therapeutic goods\nor vaping goods that contain that ingredient or component;\n(b) the export from Australia of all or specified therapeutic\ngoods or vaping goods that contain that ingredient or\ncomponent;\n(c) the manufacture in Australia of all or specified therapeutic\ngoods or vaping goods that contain that ingredient or\ncomponent;\n(d) the supply in Australia of all or specified therapeutic goods\nor vaping goods that contain that ingredient or component.\n(4) Before regulations are made prescribing an international agreement\nfor the purposes of subsection (3), the Minister must be satisfied\nthat the agreement requires parties to the agreement to take steps to\nprohibit or restrict one or more of the import, export, manufacture\nand supply of goods containing that ingredient or component.\nNature of prohibition\n(5) A prohibition referred to in subsection (1) or (3) may be absolute\nor be subject to such conditions as are prescribed.\n\nProhibition on import, export, manufacture or supply of therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods—international agreements  Chapter 2A\n\nSection 9L\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nProcedural requirements for regulations containing prohibition\n(6) Regulations containing a prohibition referred to in subsection (1)\nor (3) must not be made unless:\n(a) the Minister causes to be published on the Department’s\nwebsite a notice setting out details of:\n(i) the international agreement; and\n(ii) the Minister’s satisfaction mentioned in subsection (2)\nor (4); and\n(iii) the proposed prohibition; and\n(b) a period of 30 days has passed since the notice was\npublished.\nCommencement of regulations containing prohibition\n(7) Regulations containing a prohibition referred to in subsection (1)\nor (3) must not be expressed to commence on a day earlier than the\nday the international agreement enters into force for Australia.\nContent of regulations containing prohibition\n(8) Without limiting subsection (5), regulations prescribing conditions\nreferred to in that subsection may do one or more of the following:\n(a) make provision in relation to a matter by conferring on the\nMinister or Secretary a power to make a decision of an\nadministrative character;\n(b) refer to the Minister or Secretary being satisfied of one or\nmore specified matters;\n(c) make provision for and in relation to the Minister or\nSecretary delegating powers to an SES employee, or acting\nSES employee, in the Department.",
      "skos:definition": "therapeutic goods or vaping goods—international\nagreements\nProhibition on therapeutic goods or vaping goods themselves\n(1) If therapeutic goods or vaping goods are the subject of an\ninternational agreement prescribed for the purposes of this\nsubsection, the regulations may prohibit one or more of the\nfollowing:\n(a) the import into Australia of the therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods;\n(b) the export from Australia of the therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods;\n(c) the manufacture in Australia of the therapeutic goods or\nvaping goods;\n\nChapter 2A  Prohibition on import, export, manufacture or supply of therapeutic goods\nor vaping goods—international agreements\n\nSection 9K\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(d) the supply in Australia of the therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods.\n(2) Before regulations are made prescribing an international agreement\nfor the purposes of subsection (1), the Minister must be satisfied\nthat the agreement requires parties to the agreement to take steps to\nprohibit or restrict one or more of the import, export, manufacture\nand supply of certain goods.\nProhibition on therapeutic goods or vaping goods containing an\ningredient or component\n(3) If an ingredient or component of therapeutic goods or vaping goods\nis the subject of an international agreement prescribed for the\npurposes of this subsection, the regulations may prohibit one or\nmore of the following:\n(a) the import into Australia of all or specified therapeutic goods\nor vaping goods that contain that ingredient or component;\n(b) the export from Australia of all or specified therapeutic\ngoods or vaping goods that contain that ingredient or\ncomponent;\n(c) the manufacture in Australia of all or specified therapeutic\ngoods or vaping goods that contain that ingredient or\ncomponent;\n(d) the supply in Australia of all or specified therapeutic goods\nor vaping goods that contain that ingredient or component.\n(4) Before regulations are made prescribing an international agreement\nfor the",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9k-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9k-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9k-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9k-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9k-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9k-ss-6"
