      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Infer",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Regulations with prohibition infer the international agreement.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(7) Regulations containing a prohibition referred to in subsection (1)\nor (3)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "must not be expressed to commence on a day earlier than the\nday the international agreement enters into force for Australia."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9k-ss-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9K(8) Prohibition on import, export, manufacture or supply of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9k-ss-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.69",
      "values:originalText": "(8) Without limiting subsection (5), regulations prescribing conditions\nreferred to in that subsection may do one or more of the following:\n(a) make provision in relation to a matter by conferring on the\nMinister or Secretary a power to make a decision of an\nadministrative character;\n(b) refer to the Minister or Secretary being satisfied of one or\nmore specified matters;\n(c) make provision for and in relation to the Minister or\nSecretary delegating powers to an SES employee, or acting\nSES employee, in the Department.",
      "skos:definition": "(8) Without limiting subsection (5), regulations prescribing conditions\nreferred to in that subsection may do one or more of the following:\n(a) make provision in relation to a matter by conferring on the\nMinister or Secretary a power to make a decision of an\nadministrative character;\n(b) refer to the Minister or Secretary being satisfied of one or\nmore specified matters;\n(c) make provision for and in relation to the Minister or\nSecretary delegating powers to an SES employee, or acting\nSES employee, in the Department.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9k"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9k-ss-8-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "db29f6246b2ea2103822fbb9d3b5941d6a90f6bd69503813aa7342e156cb5ab8",
      "skos:note": "Regulations may confer power on Minister or Secretary to make administrative decisions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9k-ss-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9K(8) Prohibition on import, export, manufacture or supply of",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 69,
      "values:originalText": "(8) Without limiting subsection (5), regulations prescribing conditions\nreferred to in that subsection may do one or more of the following:\n(a) make provision in relation to a matter by conferring on the\nMinister or Secretary a power to make a decision of an\nadministrative character;\n(b) refer to the Minister or Secretary being satisfied of one or\nmore specified matters;\n(c) make provision for and in relation to the Minister or\nSecretary delegating powers to an SES employee, or acting\nSES employee, in the Department."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9k-ss-8-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9k-ss-8"
