      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9l",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9L Offence and civil penalty",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9l"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.71",
      "values:originalText": "Offence\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\nChapter 2A  Prohibition on import, export, manufacture or supply of therapeutic goods\nor vaping goods—international agreements\n\nSection 9L\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports into Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(ii) exports from Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(iii) manufactures in Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(iv) supplies in Australia therapeutic goods or vaping goods;\nand\n(b) the import, export, manufacture or supply contravenes:\n(i) an absolute prohibition in force for the purposes of\nsubsection 9K(1) or (3); or\n(ii) one or more conditions of a prohibition in force for the\npurposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3).\nPenalty: 300 penalty units.\nCivil penalty\n(2) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports into Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(ii) exports from Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(iii) manufactures in Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(iv) supplies in Australia therapeutic goods or vaping goods;\nand\n(b) the import, export, manufacture or supply contravenes:\n(i) an absolute prohibition in force for the purposes of\nsubsection 9K(1) or (3); or\n(ii) one or more conditions of a prohibition in force for the\npurposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3).\nMaximum civil penalty:\n\nProhibition on import, export, manufacture or supply of therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods—international agreements  Chapter 2A\n\nSection 9M\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) for an individual—300 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—3,000 penalty units.",
      "skos:definition": "Offence\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\nChapter 2A  Prohibition on import, export, manufacture or supply of therapeutic goods\nor vaping goods—international agreements\n\nSection 9L\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports into Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(ii) exports from Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(iii) manufactures in Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(iv) supplies in Australia therapeutic goods or vaping goods;\nand\n(b) the import, export, manufacture or supply contravenes:\n(i) an absolute prohibition in force for the purposes of\nsubsection 9K(1) or (3); or\n(ii) one or more conditions of a prohibition in force for the\npurposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3).\nPenalty: 300 penalty units.\nCivil penalty\n(2) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports into Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(ii) exports from Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(iii) manufactures in Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(iv) supplies in Australia therapeutic goods or vaping goods;\nand\n(b) the import, export, manufacture or supply contravenes:\n(i) an absolute prohibition in force for the purposes of\nsubsection 9K(1) or (3); or\n(ii) one or more conditions of a prohibition in force for the\npurposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3).\nMaximum civil penalty:\n\nProhibition on import, export, manufacture or supply of therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods—international agreements  Chapter 2A\n\nSection 9M\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) for an individual—300 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—3,000 penalty units.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9l-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9l-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cd25b8565d4b57e8f856cf50c696d80d49eb0c79087d2888c0de2bddefadce7e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-9l",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9L Offence and civil penalty",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 71,
      "values:originalText": "Offence\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\nChapter 2A  Prohibition on import, export, manufacture or supply of therapeutic goods\nor vaping goods—international agreements\n\nSection 9L\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports into Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(ii) exports from Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(iii) manufactures in Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(iv) supplies in Australia therapeutic goods or vaping goods;\nand\n(b) the import, export, manufacture or supply contravenes:\n(i) an absolute prohibition in force for the purposes of\nsubsection 9K(1) or (3); or\n(ii) one or more conditions of a prohibition in force for the\npurposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3).\nPenalty: 300 penalty units.\nCivil penalty\n(2) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports into Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(ii) exports from Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(iii) manufactures in Australia therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods; or\n(iv) supplies in Australia therapeutic goods or vaping goods;\nand\n(b) the import, export, manufacture or supply contravenes:\n(i) an absolute prohibition in force for the purposes of\nsubsection 9K(1) or (3); or\n(ii) one or more conditions of a prohibition in force for the\npurposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3).\nMaximum civil penalty:\n\nProhibition on import, export, manufacture or supply of therapeutic goods or vaping\ngoods—international agreements  Chapter 2A\n\nSection 9M\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) for an individual—300 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—3,000 penalty units."
    },
