    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-10-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10(4) Determination of standards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-10-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, an order\nunder subsection (1) of this section, or a variation of such an order,\nmay make provision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting\nor incorporating, with or without modification, any matter\ncontained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing\nfrom time to time.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, an order\nunder subsection (1) of this section, or a variation of such an order,\nmay make provision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting\nor incorporating, with or without modification, any matter\ncontained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing\nfrom time to time.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-10"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
