        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "52046a47fc4bce7b893fb6f69f731205e0c09189c24efaea579396237c5ac80b",
      "skos:note": "May incorporate existing provisions from instruments or writings."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-10-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10(4) Determination of standards",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, an order\nunder subsection (1) of this section, or a variation of such an order,\nmay make provision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting\nor incorporating, with or without modification, any matter\ncontained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing\nfrom time to time.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
    {
