        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8fd75bf8793b773bc7f8f17d29d5f63613e01cdae4ebd564216332a966d4c24e",
      "skos:note": "If two default standards apply to different parts of a class of therapeutic goods, the more restrictive standard applies."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-13-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13(3) Special provisions relating to Ministerial standards and default",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 76,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If:\n(a) a default standard applies to a class of therapeutic goods; and\n(b) another default standard applies to only some of the\ntherapeutic goods within that class; and\n(c) those standards are inconsistent;\nthe standard referred to in paragraph (a) does not apply in relation\nto the goods referred to in paragraph (b)."
    },
