    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-13a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13A Special provisions relating to homoeopathic standards and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-13a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.77",
      "values:originalText": "anthroposophic standards\n(1) For the purposes of this Act, if a statement (the main statement) in\na monograph in a homoeopathic pharmacopoeia or an\nanthroposophic pharmacopoeia refers to a statement in a\nmonograph in another publication, the main statement is taken to\ninclude the other statement.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "anthroposophic standards\n(1) For the purposes of this Act, if a statement (the main statement) in\na monograph in a homoeopathic pharmacopoeia or an\nanthroposophic pharmacopoeia refers to a statement in a\nmonograph in another publication, the main statement is taken to\ninclude the other statement.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-13a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-13a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0550e76a3096121d9b65c4ac809b9b3e78d680315a4369bec6571140eb8170cf",
      "skos:note": "If a statement in a monograph refers to another statement, the main statement includes the other statement."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-13a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13A Special provisions relating to homoeopathic standards and",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 77,
      "values:originalText": "anthroposophic standards\n(1) For the purposes of this Act, if a statement (the main statement) in\na monograph in a homoeopathic pharmacopoeia or an\nanthroposophic pharmacopoeia refers to a statement in a\nmonograph in another publication, the main statement is taken to\ninclude the other statement.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-13a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-13a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-13a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "includes",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Includes other statement when referring to it",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Statement A refers to Statement B",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Statement A includes Statement B"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-14",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "14 Criminal offences for importing, supplying or exporting goods",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-14"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.78",
      "values:originalText": "that do not comply with standards\nOffences relating to importing goods into Australia\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person imports therapeutic goods into Australia; and\n(b) the goods are imported without the consent in writing of the\nSecretary; and\n(c) the goods do not conform with a standard applicable to the\ngoods (other than by reason of a matter relating to labelling\nor packaging); and\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of the goods has resulted in, will result in, or is\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the goods, if the goods were used, would\nresult in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury\nto any person; and\n(e) the harm or injury has resulted, will result, is likely to result,\nwould result, or would be likely to result, because the goods\ndo not conform with the standard.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nStandards  Part 3-1\n\nSection 14\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person imports therapeutic goods into Australia; and\n(b) the goods are imported without the consent in writing of the\nSecretary; and\n(c) the goods do not conform with a standard applicable to the\ngoods (other than by reason of a matter relating to labelling\nor packaging).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(4A) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person imports therapeutic goods into Australia; and\n(b) the goods are imported without the consent in writing of the\nSecretary; and\n(c) the goods do not conform with a standard applicable to the\ngoods (other than by reason of a matter relating to labelling\nor packaging).\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(4B) An offence against subsection (4A) is an offence of strict liability.\nException\n(5A) Subsection (1), (4) or (4A) does not apply if:\n(a) the therapeutic goods are a biological; and\n(b) the person imports the biological after the circumstances\nprescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this\nparagraph have occurred.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (5A): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\nOffences relating to supplying goods for use in Australia\n(6) A person commits an offence if:\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "that do not comply with standards\nOffences relating to importing goods into Australia\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person imports therapeutic goods into Australia; and\n(b) the goods are imported without the consent in writing of the\nSecretary; and\n(c) the goods do not conform with a standard applicable to the\ngoods (other than by reason of a matter relating to labelling\nor packaging); and\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of the goods has resulted in, will result in, or is\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the goods, if the goods were used, would\nresult in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury\nto any person; and\n(e) the harm or injury has resulted, will result, is likely to result,\nwould result, or would be likely to result, because the goods\ndo not conform with the standard.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nStandards  Part 3-1\n\nSection 14\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person imports therapeutic goods into Australia; and\n(b) the goods are imported without the consent in writing of the\nSecretary; and\n(c) the goods do not conform with a standard applicable to the\ngoods (other than by reason of a matter relating to labelling\nor packaging).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(4A) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person imports therapeutic goods into Australia; and\n(b) the goods are imported without the consent in writing of the\nSecretary; and\n(c) the goods do not conform with a standard applicable to the\ngoods (other than by reason of a matter",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-14-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-14-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-14-ss-4a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-14-ss-4b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-14-ss-5a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-14-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "146ba93cf47044972733d189ffb9dd50623b84e42edb0be4b1c7ffbf24cfbd6c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-14",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14 Criminal offences for importing, supplying or exporting goods",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 78,
      "values:originalText": "that do not comply with standards\nOffences relating to importing goods into Australia\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person imports therapeutic goods into Australia; and\n(b) the goods are imported without the consent in writing of the\nSecretary; and\n(c) the goods do not conform with a standard applicable to the\ngoods (other than by reason of a matter relating to labelling\nor packaging); and\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of the goods has resulted in, will result in, or is\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the goods, if the goods were used, would\nresult in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury\nto any person; and\n(e) the harm or injury has resulted, will result, is likely to result,\nwould result, or would be likely to result, because the goods\ndo not conform with the standard.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nStandards  Part 3-1\n\nSection 14\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person imports therapeutic goods into Australia; and\n(b) the goods are imported without the consent in writing of the\nSecretary; and\n(c) the goods do not conform with a standard applicable to the\ngoods (other than by reason of a matter relating to labelling\nor packaging).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(4A) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person imports therapeutic goods into Australia; and\n(b) the goods are imported without the consent in writing of the\nSecretary; and\n(c) the goods do not conform with a standard applicable to the\ngoods (other than by reason of a matter relating to labelling\nor packaging).\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(4B) An offence against subsection (4A) is an offence of strict liability.\nException\n(5A) Subsection (1), (4) or (4A) does not apply if:\n(a) the therapeutic goods are a biological; and\n(b) the person imports the biological after the circumstances\nprescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this\nparagraph have occurred.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (5A): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\nOffences relating to supplying goods for use in Australia\n(6) A person commits an offence if:\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
    {
