    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-16",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16 Therapeutic goods and gazetted groups",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-16"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.89",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, therapeutic goods (other than\nmedicine of the kind to which subsection (1A) applies) are to be\ntaken to be separate and distinct from other therapeutic goods if\nthey have:\n(a) a different formulation, composition or design specification;\nor\n(b) a different strength or size (disregarding pack size); or\n(c) a different dosage form or model; or\n(d) a different name; or\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, therapeutic goods (other than\nmedicine of the kind to which subsection (1A) applies) are to be\ntaken to be separate and distinct from other therapeutic goods if\nthey have:\n(a) a different formulation, composition or design specification;\nor\n(b) a different strength or size (disregarding pack size); or\n(c) a different dosage form or model; or\n(d) a different name; or\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-16-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-16-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "332e821bf3e340d296550535e75847a6b2321f16e76111ab1ed0f75d5815c2bb",
      "skos:note": "Therapeutic goods must be taken to be separate and distinct from other therapeutic goods if they have a different formulation, composition or design specification; or a different strength or size (disregarding pack size); or a different dosage form or model; or a different name;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-16",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16 Therapeutic goods and gazetted groups",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 89,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, therapeutic goods (other than\nmedicine of the kind to which subsection (1A) applies) are to be\ntaken to be separate and distinct from other therapeutic goods if\nthey have:\n(a) a different formulation, composition or design specification;\nor\n(b) a different strength or size (disregarding pack size); or\n(c) a different dosage form or model; or\n(d) a different name; or\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
