    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-18",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "18 Exempt goods",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-18"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.91",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may, subject to such conditions (if any) as are\nspecified in the regulations, exempt:\n(a) all therapeutic goods, except those included in a class of\ngoods prescribed for the purposes of this paragraph; or\n(b) specified therapeutic goods; or\n(c) a specified class of therapeutic goods;\nfrom the operation of this Part (except section 31A and\nsections 31C to 31F).\n(2) An exemption in terms of paragraph (1)(a) has effect only in\nrelation to such classes of persons as are prescribed for the\npurposes of this subsection.\n(3) Where the regulations revoke an exemption, the revocation takes\neffect on the day, not being earlier than 28 days after the day on\nwhich the regulations are made, specified in the regulations.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The regulations may, subject to such conditions (if any) as are\nspecified in the regulations, exempt:\n(a) all therapeutic goods, except those included in a class of\ngoods prescribed for the purposes of this paragraph; or\n(b) specified therapeutic goods; or\n(c) a specified class of therapeutic goods;\nfrom the operation of this Part (except section 31A and\nsections 31C to 31F).\n(2) An exemption in terms of paragraph (1)(a) has effect only in\nrelation to such classes of persons as are prescribed for the\npurposes of this subsection.\n(3) Where the regulations revoke an exemption, the revocation takes\neffect on the day, not being earlier than 28 days after the day on\nwhich the regulations are made, specified in the regulations.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-18-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-18-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-18-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3b12d79ed73f4eaaa998bd034ef6f0b956b52a2b91535c31b4ce5b69f425de6e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-18",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18 Exempt goods",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 91,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may, subject to such conditions (if any) as are\nspecified in the regulations, exempt:\n(a) all therapeutic goods, except those included in a class of\ngoods prescribed for the purposes of this paragraph; or\n(b) specified therapeutic goods; or\n(c) a specified class of therapeutic goods;\nfrom the operation of this Part (except section 31A and\nsections 31C to 31F).\n(2) An exemption in terms of paragraph (1)(a) has effect only in\nrelation to such classes of persons as are prescribed for the\npurposes of this subsection.\n(3) Where the regulations revoke an exemption, the revocation takes\neffect on the day, not being earlier than 28 days after the day on\nwhich the regulations are made, specified in the regulations."
    },
