      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines temporal interval for revocation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Revocation takes effect on a specified day",
      "cml:conclusionText": "After 28 days from the regulations' effective date"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-18a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "18A Exemption because of emergency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-18a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.91",
      "values:originalText": "Minister’s power\n(1) The Minister may exempt from the operation of Division 2 of this\nPart:\n(a) specified therapeutic goods; or\n(b) therapeutic goods in a specified class.\nThe exemption must be made in writing.\n(1A) The Minister may exempt goods under subsection (1) only if the\nMinister is satisfied of the matter in subsection (2) or (2A).\n(2) The matter in this subsection is that in the national interest:\n(a) the exemption should be made so that the goods may be\nstockpiled as quickly as possible in order to create a\npreparedness to deal with a potential threat to public health\nthat may be caused by a possible future emergency; or\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "Minister’s power\n(1) The Minister may exempt from the operation of Division 2 of this\nPart:\n(a) specified therapeutic goods; or\n(b) therapeutic goods in a specified class.\nThe exemption must be made in writing.\n(1A) The Minister may exempt goods under subsection (1) only if the\nMinister is satisfied of the matter in subsection (2) or (2A).\n(2) The matter in this subsection is that in the national interest:\n(a) the exemption should be made so that the goods may be\nstockpiled as quickly as possible in order to create a\npreparedness to deal with a potential threat to public health\nthat may be caused by a possible future emergency; or\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
