    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19(2) Approvals or authorities for certain uses",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-19-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.96",
      "values:originalText": "(2) An application for an approval must be made to the Secretary and\nmust:\n(a) in the case of an application for use of the kind referred to in\nparagraph (1)(a)—be in a form (if any) approved, in writing,\nby the Secretary and be accompanied by such information\nrelating to the goods the subject of the application as is\nrequired by the Secretary; and\n(b) in the case of an application for use of the kind referred to in\nparagraph (1)(b):\n(i) be in a form (if any) approved, in writing, by the\nSecretary; and\n(ii) be accompanied by such information relating to the\ngoods the subject of the application as is required by the\nSecretary; and\n(iii) be accompanied by the prescribed evaluation fee.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nPreliminary  Division 1\nSection 19\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(2) An application for an approval must be made to the Secretary and\nmust:\n(a) in the case of an application for use of the kind referred to in\nparagraph (1)(a)—be in a form (if any) approved, in writing,\nby the Secretary and be accompanied by such information\nrelating to the goods the subject of the application as is\nrequired by the Secretary; and\n(b) in the case of an application for use of the kind referred to in\nparagraph (1)(b):\n(i) be in a form (if any) approved, in writing, by the\nSecretary; and\n(ii) be accompanied by such information relating to the\ngoods the subject of the application as is required by the\nSecretary; and\n(iii) be accompanied by the prescribed evaluation fee.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nPreliminary  Division 1\nSection 19\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0b8e578f3db5a8de62b31c3747a5eeb555da57071d6f3b281f59880be47d7daf",
      "skos:note": "Application for approval must be made to the Secretary and meet certain requirements.",
      "dc:description": "Information relating to goods subject to application, evaluation fee"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-19-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19(2) Approvals or authorities for certain uses",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "(2) An application for an approval must be made to the Secretary and\nmust:\n(a) in the case of an application for use of the kind referred to in\nparagraph (1)(a)—be in a form (if any) approved, in writing,\nby the Secretary and be accompanied by such information\nrelating to the goods the subject of the application as is\nrequired by the Secretary; and\n(b) in the case of an application for use of the kind referred to in\nparagraph (1)(b):\n(i) be in a form (if any) approved, in writing, by the\nSecretary; and\n(ii) be accompanied by such information relating to the\ngoods the subject of the application as is required by the\nSecretary; and\n(iii) be accompanied by the prescribed evaluation fee.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nPreliminary  Division 1\nSection 19\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
