    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19(4) Approvals or authorities for certain uses",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-19-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.96",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Where an application for an approval is made, the Secretary must,\nafter having considered the application and, in the case of an\napplication for the use of therapeutic goods for experimental\npurposes in humans, after having evaluated the information\nsubmitted with the application, notify the applicant of the decision\non the application within 28 days of making the decision and, in\nthe case of a decision not to grant the approval, of the reasons for\nthe decision.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Where an application for an approval is made, the Secretary must,\nafter having considered the application and, in the case of an\napplication for the use of therapeutic goods for experimental\npurposes in humans, after having evaluated the information\nsubmitted with the application, notify the applicant of the decision\non the application within 28 days of making the decision and, in\nthe case of a decision not to grant the approval, of the reasons for\nthe decision.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2444276c81866ecd86b77a89a253735c272a7de395f037589e5c55cbc5e0431a",
      "skos:note": "Notify applicant of decision on approval within 28 days.",
      "dc:description": "Reasons for decision (if not granting approval)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-19-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19(4) Approvals or authorities for certain uses",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Where an application for an approval is made, the Secretary must,\nafter having considered the application and, in the case of an\napplication for the use of therapeutic goods for experimental\npurposes in humans, after having evaluated the information\nsubmitted with the application, notify the applicant of the decision\non the application within 28 days of making the decision and, in\nthe case of a decision not to grant the approval, of the reasons for\nthe decision."
    },
    {
