    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19A Approvals where unavailability etc. of therapeutic goods",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-19a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.101",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may, by notice in writing, grant an approval to a\nperson for the importation into Australia, or the supply in\nAustralia, of specified therapeutic goods if the Secretary is satisfied\nthat:\n(a) registered goods that could act as a substitute for the goods:\n(i) are unavailable or are in short supply; or\n(ii) may, in the reasonably foreseeable future, become\nunavailable or be in short supply; and\n(b) either:\n(i) the goods that are the subject of the application are\nregistered or approved for general marketing in at least\none foreign country specified by the Secretary in a\ndetermination under subsection (3); or\n(ii) an application under section 23 has been made for\nregistration of the goods and the application has passed\npreliminary assessment; and\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary may, by notice in writing, grant an approval to a\nperson for the importation into Australia, or the supply in\nAustralia, of specified therapeutic goods if the Secretary is satisfied\nthat:\n(a) registered goods that could act as a substitute for the goods:\n(i) are unavailable or are in short supply; or\n(ii) may, in the reasonably foreseeable future, become\nunavailable or be in short supply; and\n(b) either:\n(i) the goods that are the subject of the application are\nregistered or approved for general marketing in at least\none foreign country specified by the Secretary in a\ndetermination under subsection (3); or\n(ii) an application under section 23 has been made for\nregistration of the goods and the application has passed\npreliminary assessment; and\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19a-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19a-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19a-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19a-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c08d18d286923cefe07aafbd020c063b168a8af45954d7225017ab722404396e",
      "skos:note": "Secretary may grant approval for importation or supply of therapeutic goods under certain conditions."
    },
