    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19C Notice required to adduce evidence in support of exception",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-19c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.109",
      "values:originalText": "under subsection 19B(6)\n(1) If:\n(a) a defendant is committed for trial for an offence against\nsubsection 19B(1); or\n(b) an offence against subsection 19B(1) is to be heard and\ndetermined by a court of summary jurisdiction;\nthe committing magistrate or the court must:\n(c) inform the defendant of the requirements of this section; and\n(d) cause a copy of this section to be given to the defendant.\n(2) A defendant must not, without leave of the court, adduce evidence\nin support of the exception under subsection 19B(6) unless:\n(a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies—more than 21 days before the\ntrial begins; or\n(b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—more than 21 days before the\nhearing of the offence begins;\nhe or she gives notice of particulars of the exception.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "under subsection 19B(6)\n(1) If:\n(a) a defendant is committed for trial for an offence against\nsubsection 19B(1); or\n(b) an offence against subsection 19B(1) is to be heard and\ndetermined by a court of summary jurisdiction;\nthe committing magistrate or the court must:\n(c) inform the defendant of the requirements of this section; and\n(d) cause a copy of this section to be given to the defendant.\n(2) A defendant must not, without leave of the court, adduce evidence\nin support of the exception under subsection 19B(6) unless:\n(a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies—more than 21 days before the\ntrial begins; or\n(b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—more than 21 days before the\nhearing of the offence begins;\nhe or she gives notice of particulars of the exception.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19c-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "77146b6ede20dfed3c542c124cb75182179bf06dcb289624c7d97eac832e7e37"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-19c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19C Notice required to adduce evidence in support of exception",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 109,
      "values:originalText": "under subsection 19B(6)\n(1) If:\n(a) a defendant is committed for trial for an offence against\nsubsection 19B(1); or\n(b) an offence against subsection 19B(1) is to be heard and\ndetermined by a court of summary jurisdiction;\nthe committing magistrate or the court must:\n(c) inform the defendant of the requirements of this section; and\n(d) cause a copy of this section to be given to the defendant.\n(2) A defendant must not, without leave of the court, adduce evidence\nin support of the exception under subsection 19B(6) unless:\n(a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies—more than 21 days before the\ntrial begins; or\n(b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—more than 21 days before the\nhearing of the offence begins;\nhe or she gives notice of particulars of the exception.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
    {
