    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19c-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19C(2) Notice required to adduce evidence in support of exception",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-19c-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.109",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A defendant must not, without leave of the court, adduce evidence\nin support of the exception under subsection 19B(6) unless:\n(a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies—more than 21 days before the\ntrial begins; or\n(b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—more than 21 days before the\nhearing of the offence begins;\nhe or she gives notice of particulars of the exception.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A defendant must not, without leave of the court, adduce evidence\nin support of the exception under subsection 19B(6) unless:\n(a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies—more than 21 days before the\ntrial begins; or\n(b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—more than 21 days before the\nhearing of the offence begins;\nhe or she gives notice of particulars of the exception.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19c-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19c-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2fb5cdbb61f9ca020106a6a2397abe081a92e8e8a25dcb5dc0e23a20f570769e",
      "skos:note": "No evidence in support of exception can be adduced without notice.",
      "dc:description": "Notice of particulars of the exception"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-19c-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19C(2) Notice required to adduce evidence in support of exception",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 109,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A defendant must not, without leave of the court, adduce evidence\nin support of the exception under subsection 19B(6) unless:\n(a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies—more than 21 days before the\ntrial begins; or\n(b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—more than 21 days before the\nhearing of the offence begins;\nhe or she gives notice of particulars of the exception.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
    {
