    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-21a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21A General criminal offences relating to this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-21a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.117",
      "values:originalText": "Offences for making a false or misleading statement\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in or in connection with a certification\nof any matter under subsection 26A(2) or 26AB(2); and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular;\nand\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of the medicine has resulted in, will result in, or\nis likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the medicine, if the medicine were used,\nwould result in, or would be likely to result in, harm or\ninjury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "Offences for making a false or misleading statement\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in or in connection with a certification\nof any matter under subsection 26A(2) or 26AB(2); and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular;\nand\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of the medicine has resulted in, will result in, or\nis likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the medicine, if the medicine were used,\nwould result in, or would be likely to result in, harm or\ninjury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-21a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-21a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-21a-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-21a-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-21a-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-21a-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3761e724949345bd4afb4fd92f44ec3fcb1847967ffca46dc3929cafdd314a2f",
      "skos:note": "Making false or misleading statements in certification is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-21a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21A General criminal offences relating to this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 117,
      "values:originalText": "Offences for making a false or misleading statement\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in or in connection with a certification\nof any matter under subsection 26A(2) or 26AB(2); and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular;\nand\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of the medicine has resulted in, will result in, or\nis likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the medicine, if the medicine were used,\nwould result in, or would be likely to result in, harm or\ninjury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
