    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-22f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "22F Revocation of provisional determination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-22f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.136",
      "values:originalText": "Revocation on Secretary’s own initiative\n(1) The Secretary may revoke a provisional determination under\nsection 22D relating to a person and a medicine if the Secretary is\nsatisfied that the criteria prescribed by the regulations for the\npurposes of subsection 22D(2) are no longer met in relation to the\nmedicine.\nRevocation on request\n(2) The Secretary must revoke a provisional determination under\nsection 22D relating to a person and a medicine if the person\nrequests the Secretary, in writing, to do so.\nNotice of revocation\n(3) As soon as practicable after making a revocation under this section,\nthe Secretary must:\n(a) give the person written notice of the revocation; and\n(b) for a revocation under subsection (1)—set out the reasons for\nthe revocation in the notice.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nProvisional determinations for medicine  Division 1A\nSection 22F\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nDay revocation takes effect\n(4) A revocation under this section takes effect on the day on which\nthe Secretary gives the person notice of the revocation.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "Revocation on Secretary’s own initiative\n(1) The Secretary may revoke a provisional determination under\nsection 22D relating to a person and a medicine if the Secretary is\nsatisfied that the criteria prescribed by the regulations for the\npurposes of subsection 22D(2) are no longer met in relation to the\nmedicine.\nRevocation on request\n(2) The Secretary must revoke a provisional determination under\nsection 22D relating to a person and a medicine if the person\nrequests the Secretary, in writing, to do so.\nNotice of revocation\n(3) As soon as practicable after making a revocation under this section,\nthe Secretary must:\n(a) give the person written notice of the revocation; and\n(b) for a revocation under subsection (1)—set out the reasons for\nthe revocation in the notice.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nProvisional determinations for medicine  Division 1A\nSection 22F\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nDay revocation takes effect\n(4) A revocation under this section takes effect on the day on which\nthe Secretary gives the person notice of the revocation.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-22f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-22f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-22f-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-22f-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6e75ab479905bdbba7c1e57d0311cfe9c0adf3a3549977464ca792bb1bc13261"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-22f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22F Revocation of provisional determination",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 136,
      "values:originalText": "Revocation on Secretary’s own initiative\n(1) The Secretary may revoke a provisional determination under\nsection 22D relating to a person and a medicine if the Secretary is\nsatisfied that the criteria prescribed by the regulations for the\npurposes of subsection 22D(2) are no longer met in relation to the\nmedicine.\nRevocation on request\n(2) The Secretary must revoke a provisional determination under\nsection 22D relating to a person and a medicine if the person\nrequests the Secretary, in writing, to do so.\nNotice of revocation\n(3) As soon as practicable after making a revocation under this section,\nthe Secretary must:\n(a) give the person written notice of the revocation; and\n(b) for a revocation under subsection (1)—set out the reasons for\nthe revocation in the notice.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nProvisional determinations for medicine  Division 1A\nSection 22F\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nDay revocation takes effect\n(4) A revocation under this section takes effect on the day on which\nthe Secretary gives the person notice of the revocation.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
