      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.138",
      "values:originalText": "(5) A person may request the Secretary for advice about whether, if the\nperson were to make an application under section 23 for\nregistration of a medicine, a prescribed aspect of the efficacy of the\nmedicine, for the purposes identified by the person as purposes for\nwhich the medicine may be used, has been satisfactorily\nestablished.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nScientific advice about aspects of quality, safety or efficacy of medicine  Division 1B\nSection 22G\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(5) A person may request the Secretary for advice about whether, if the\nperson were to make an application under section 23 for\nregistration of a medicine, a prescribed aspect of the efficacy of the\nmedicine, for the purposes identified by the person as purposes for\nwhich the medicine may be used, has been satisfactorily\nestablished.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nScientific advice about aspects of quality, safety or efficacy of medicine  Division 1B\nSection 22G\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
