      "values:originalText": "(2) The application complies with this section if:\n(a) the application is made in accordance with a form approved,\nin writing, by the Secretary or in such other manner as is\napproved, in writing, by the Secretary for the purposes of this\nparagraph; and\n(b) the application is delivered to an office of the Department\nspecified by the Secretary; and\n(c) the prescribed application fee has been paid; and\n(d) the applicant has delivered to the office to which the\napplication was made such information, in a form approved,\nin writing, by the Secretary, as will allow the determination\nof the application; and\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 23C\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(e) if the Secretary so requires—the applicant has delivered to\nthe office to which the application was made a reasonable\nnumber of samples of the goods; and\n(f) if there are one or more absolute prohibitions in force for the\npurposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3)—the application is\naccompanied by a statement from the applicant certifying\nthat:\n(i) if those prohibitions cover imports—any imports into\nAustralia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant,\nwill not contravene those prohibitions; and\n(ii) if those prohibitions cover exports—any exports from\nAustralia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant,\nwill not contravene those prohibitions; and\n(iii) if those prohibitions cover supplies—any supplies in\nAustralia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant,\nwill not contravene those prohibitions; and\n(g) if there are one or more prohibitions in force for the purposes\nof subsection 9K(1) or (3) that are subject to conditions—the\napplication is accompanied by a statement from the applicant\ncertifying that:\n(i) if those prohibitions cover imports—any imports into\nAustralia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant,\nwill not contravene those conditions; and\n(ii) if those prohibitions cover exports—any exports from\nAustralia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant,\nwill not contravene those conditions; and\n(iii) if those prohibitions cover supplies—any supplies in\nAustralia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant,\nwill not contravene those conditions.\nNote:\nTo be listed, an application must comply with this section: see\nsections 26, 26A and 26AB.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The application complies with this section if:\n(a) the application is made in accordance with a form approved,\nin writing, by the Secretary or in such other manner as is\napproved, in writing, by the Secretary for the purposes of this\nparagraph; and\n(b) the application is delivered to an office of the Department\nspecified by the Secretary; and\n(c) the prescribed application fee has been paid; and\n(d) the applicant has delivered to the office to which the\napplication was made such information, in a form approved,\nin writing, by the Secretary, as will allow the determination\nof the application; and\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 23C\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(e) if the Secretary so requires—the applicant has delivered to\nthe office to which the application was made a reasonable\nnumber of samples of the goods; and\n(f) if there are one or more absolute prohibitions in force for the\npurposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3)—the application is\naccompanied by a statement from the applicant certifying\nthat:\n(i) if those prohibitions cover imports—any imports into\nAustralia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant,\nwill not contravene those prohibitions; and\n(ii) if those prohibitions cover exports—any exports from\nAustralia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant,\nwill not contravene those prohibitions; and\n(iii) if those prohibitions cover supplies—any supplies in\nAustralia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant,\nwill not contravene those prohibitions; and\n(g) if there are one or more prohibitions in force for the purposes\nof subsection 9K(1) or (3) that are subject to conditions—the\napplication is accompanied by a statement from the applicant\ncertifying that:\n(i) if those prohibitions cover imports—any imports into\nAustralia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant,\nwill n",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-23c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-23c-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-23c-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6f4e6b6a0e110c11650053374d4c34403c4842a6ca20d297562c7da1af2b791c",
      "skos:note": "Application must comply with requirements to be listed.",
      "dc:description": "Information, application fee, and samples (if required)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-23c-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23C(2) Requirements relating to applications for listing of therapeutic",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 144,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The application complies with this section if:\n(a) the application is made in accordance with a form approved,\nin writing, by the Secretary or in such other manner as is\napproved, in writing, by the Secretary for the purposes of this\nparagraph; and\n(b) the application is delivered to an office of the Department\nspecified by the Secretary; and\n(c) the prescribed application fee has been paid; and\n(d) the applicant has delivered to the office to which the\napplication was made such information, in a form approved,\nin writing, by the Secretary, as will allow the determination\nof the application; and\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 23C\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(e) if the Secretary so requires—the applicant has delivered to\nthe office to which the application was made a reasonable\nnumber of samples of the goods; and\n(f) if there are one or more absolute prohibitions in force for the\npurposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3)—the application is\naccompanied by a statement from the applicant certifying\nthat:\n(i) if those prohibitions cover imports—any imports into\nAustralia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant,\nwill not contravene those prohibitions; and\n(ii) if those prohibitions cover exports—any exports from\nAustralia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant,\nwill not contravene those prohibitions; and\n(iii) if those prohibitions cover supplies—any supplies in\nAustralia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant,\nwill not contravene those prohibitions; and\n(g) if there are one or more prohibitions in force for the purposes\nof subsection 9K(1) or (3) that are subject to conditions—the\napplication is accompanied by a statement from the applicant\ncertifying that:\n(i) if those prohibitions cover imports—any imports into\nAustralia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant,\nwill not contravene those conditions; and\n(ii) if those prohibitions cover exports—any exports from\nAustralia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant,\nwill not contravene those conditions; and\n(iii) if those prohibitions cover supplies—any supplies in\nAustralia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant,\nwill not contravene those conditions.\nNote:\nTo be listed, an application must comply with this section: see\nsections 26, 26A and 26AB."
    },
