    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24(2) Applications for registration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-24-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.146",
      "values:originalText": "(2) An application for registration of therapeutic goods lapses if:\n(a) any part of the evaluation fee payable in respect of those\ngoods remains unpaid at the end of the period of 2 months\nafter the day on which the amount became due and payable;\nor\n(b) the application contains information that is inaccurate or\nmisleading in a material particular; or\n(c) information given to the Secretary by, or on behalf of, the\napplicant in connection with the application, including\ninformation given for the purpose of a requirement under\nsection 31, is inaccurate or misleading in a material\nparticular; or\n(d) the applicant fails to comply with a requirement under\nsection 31 to give information consisting of individual patient\ndata in relation to the goods.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) An application for registration of therapeutic goods lapses if:\n(a) any part of the evaluation fee payable in respect of those\ngoods remains unpaid at the end of the period of 2 months\nafter the day on which the amount became due and payable;\nor\n(b) the application contains information that is inaccurate or\nmisleading in a material particular; or\n(c) information given to the Secretary by, or on behalf of, the\napplicant in connection with the application, including\ninformation given for the purpose of a requirement under\nsection 31, is inaccurate or misleading in a material\nparticular; or\n(d) the applicant fails to comply with a requirement under\nsection 31 to give information consisting of individual patient\ndata in relation to the goods.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d2966e67656883a64279bc5ef7ad530015eb760ff07bbf8c85500d060c96906b",
      "skos:note": "Application for registration lapses if fee remains unpaid or application contains inaccurate information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-24-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24(2) Applications for registration",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 146,
      "values:originalText": "(2) An application for registration of therapeutic goods lapses if:\n(a) any part of the evaluation fee payable in respect of those\ngoods remains unpaid at the end of the period of 2 months\nafter the day on which the amount became due and payable;\nor\n(b) the application contains information that is inaccurate or\nmisleading in a material particular; or\n(c) information given to the Secretary by, or on behalf of, the\napplicant in connection with the application, including\ninformation given for the purpose of a requirement under\nsection 31, is inaccurate or misleading in a material\nparticular; or\n(d) the applicant fails to comply with a requirement under\nsection 31 to give information consisting of individual patient\ndata in relation to the goods."
    },
