    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24(3) Applications for registration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-24-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.146",
      "values:originalText": "(3) In this section, individual patient data, in relation to therapeutic\ngoods, means information, derived from clinical trials, relating to\nindividuals before, during and after the administration of the goods\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 24A\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nto those individuals, including, but not limited to, demographic,\nbiochemical and haematological information.\n24A  When evaluation fee due for payment\nSubject to section 24B, an evaluation fee under section 24 payable\nby an applicant is due and payable on the day on which the\napplicant is notified of the amount of the evaluation fee.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) In this section, individual patient data, in relation to therapeutic\ngoods, means information, derived from clinical trials, relating to\nindividuals before, during and after the administration of the goods\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 24A\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nto those individuals, including, but not limited to, demographic,\nbiochemical and haematological information.\n24A  When evaluation fee due for payment\nSubject to section 24B, an evaluation fee under section 24 payable\nby an applicant is due and payable on the day on which the\napplicant is notified of the amount of the evaluation fee.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24-ss-3-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6ee405ee2747e8f15f2326f23909f2c045cf91d8f952f24670913dd3dea48119",
      "skos:note": "Evaluation fee due on notification of amount"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-24-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24(3) Applications for registration",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 146,
      "values:originalText": "(3) In this section, individual patient data, in relation to therapeutic\ngoods, means information, derived from clinical trials, relating to\nindividuals before, during and after the administration of the goods\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 24A\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nto those individuals, including, but not limited to, demographic,\nbiochemical and haematological information.\n24A  When evaluation fee due for payment\nSubject to section 24B, an evaluation fee under section 24 payable\nby an applicant is due and payable on the day on which the\napplicant is notified of the amount of the evaluation fee."
    },
