    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24B Payment of evaluation fee by instalments",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-24b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.147",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may provide for the payment of an evaluation fee\nunder section 24 to be made by such instalments and at such times\nas are ascertained in accordance with the regulations, and the\nevaluation fee is due and payable accordingly.\n(2) Regulations made for the purposes of subsection (1) may provide\nthat a person is not allowed to pay an evaluation fee under section 24\nby instalments if any part of an instalment of:\n(a) that or any other evaluation fee under section 24 payable by\nthe person; or\n(b) any assessment fee under section 41LA payable by the\nperson;\nwas unpaid immediately after the time when it became due for\npayment.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit the generality of subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The regulations may provide for the payment of an evaluation fee\nunder section 24 to be made by such instalments and at such times\nas are ascertained in accordance with the regulations, and the\nevaluation fee is due and payable accordingly.\n(2) Regulations made for the purposes of subsection (1) may provide\nthat a person is not allowed to pay an evaluation fee under section 24\nby instalments if any part of an instalment of:\n(a) that or any other evaluation fee under section 24 payable by\nthe person; or\n(b) any assessment fee under section 41LA payable by the\nperson;\nwas unpaid immediately after the time when it became due for\npayment.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit the generality of subsection (1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24b-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c947ec1cf3212bbb031f4121d1d4b2a7863a3d88508e1e4c988886a518722071"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-24b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24B Payment of evaluation fee by instalments",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 147,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may provide for the payment of an evaluation fee\nunder section 24 to be made by such instalments and at such times\nas are ascertained in accordance with the regulations, and the\nevaluation fee is due and payable accordingly.\n(2) Regulations made for the purposes of subsection (1) may provide\nthat a person is not allowed to pay an evaluation fee under section 24\nby instalments if any part of an instalment of:\n(a) that or any other evaluation fee under section 24 payable by\nthe person; or\n(b) any assessment fee under section 41LA payable by the\nperson;\nwas unpaid immediately after the time when it became due for\npayment.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit the generality of subsection (1)."
    },
