    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-25",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "25 Evaluation of therapeutic goods",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-25"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.149",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n(a) an application is made for the registration of therapeutic\ngoods in relation to a person under section 23; and\n(b) the application has passed preliminary assessment;\nthe Secretary must evaluate the goods for registration having\nregard to:\n(c) unless the application is one referred to in paragraph (d)—\nwhether the quality, safety and efficacy of the goods for the\npurposes for which they are to be used have been\nsatisfactorily established; and\n(d) for an application for provisional registration of a medicine:\n(i) whether, based on preliminary clinical data, the safety\nand efficacy of the medicine for the purposes for which\nit is to be used have been satisfactorily established; and\n(ii) whether the quality of the medicine for the purposes for\nwhich it is to be used has been satisfactorily established;\nand\n(iii) if subsection 23AA(1) applies in relation to the\napplication—whether, if the Secretary were to register\nthe medicine, the Secretary is satisfied with the\napplicant’s plan to submit comprehensive clinical data\non the safety and efficacy of the medicine before the\nend of the 6 years that would start on the day that\nregistration would commence; and\n(da) if:\n(i) the applicant is applying for the registration of restricted\nmedicine; or\n(ii) the applicant is applying for the registration of medicine\n(other than restricted medicine) and the applicant has\nbeen given a notice in writing by the Secretary requiring\nthe applicant to give to the Secretary product\ninformation, in relation to the medicine, that is in the\nform approved under section 7D in relation to the\nmedicine;\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n(a) an application is made for the registration of therapeutic\ngoods in relation to a person under section 23; and\n(b) the application has passed preliminary assessment;\nthe Secretary must evaluate the goods for registration having\nregard to:\n(c) unless the application is one referred to in paragraph (d)—\nwhether the quality, safety and efficacy of the goods for the\npurposes for which they are to be used have been\nsatisfactorily established; and\n(d) for an application for provisional registration of a medicine:\n(i) whether, based on preliminary clinical data, the safety\nand efficacy of the medicine for the purposes for which\nit is to be used have been satisfactorily established; and\n(ii) whether the quality of the medicine for the purposes for\nwhich it is to be used has been satisfactorily established;\nand\n(iii) if subsection 23AA(1) applies in relation to the\napplication—whether, if the Secretary were to register\nthe medicine, the Secretary is satisfied with the\napplicant’s plan to submit comprehensive clinical data\non the safety and efficacy of the medicine before the\nend of the 6 years that would start on the day that\nregistration would commence; and\n(da) if:\n(i) the applicant is applying for the registration of restricted\nmedicine; or\n(ii) the applicant is applying for the registration of medicine\n(other than restricted medicine) and the applicant has\nbeen given a notice in writing by the Secretary requiring\nthe applicant to give to the Secretary product\ninformation, in relation to the medicine, that is in the\nform approved under section 7D in relation to the\nmedicine;\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-25-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-25-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "20c3419d869a5e99429a6f76dde03bc8beb01c71c6ee4018189f44a0c5894d12",
      "skos:note": "The Secretary must evaluate therapeutic goods for registration having regard to the quality, safety and efficacy of the goods."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-25",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "25 Evaluation of therapeutic goods",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 149,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n(a) an application is made for the registration of therapeutic\ngoods in relation to a person under section 23; and\n(b) the application has passed preliminary assessment;\nthe Secretary must evaluate the goods for registration having\nregard to:\n(c) unless the application is one referred to in paragraph (d)—\nwhether the quality, safety and efficacy of the goods for the\npurposes for which they are to be used have been\nsatisfactorily established; and\n(d) for an application for provisional registration of a medicine:\n(i) whether, based on preliminary clinical data, the safety\nand efficacy of the medicine for the purposes for which\nit is to be used have been satisfactorily established; and\n(ii) whether the quality of the medicine for the purposes for\nwhich it is to be used has been satisfactorily established;\nand\n(iii) if subsection 23AA(1) applies in relation to the\napplication—whether, if the Secretary were to register\nthe medicine, the Secretary is satisfied with the\napplicant’s plan to submit comprehensive clinical data\non the safety and efficacy of the medicine before the\nend of the 6 years that would start on the day that\nregistration would commence; and\n(da) if:\n(i) the applicant is applying for the registration of restricted\nmedicine; or\n(ii) the applicant is applying for the registration of medicine\n(other than restricted medicine) and the applicant has\nbeen given a notice in writing by the Secretary requiring\nthe applicant to give to the Secretary product\ninformation, in relation to the medicine, that is in the\nform approved under section 7D in relation to the\nmedicine;\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-25-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-25"
      },
