    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26 Listing of therapeutic goods",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-26"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.160",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where:\n(a) an application is made for the listing of therapeutic goods in\nrelation to a person under section 23; and\n(aaa) the application complies with section 23C; and\n(aa) the application is accompanied by either:\n(i) the certificate required under subsection 26B(1); or\n(ii) a notice (in accordance with a form approved, in\nwriting, by the Secretary) that a certificate under that\nsubsection is not required in relation to the application;\nand\n(b) the person has complied with any requirements made by the\nSecretary under section 31 in relation to the goods; and\n(ba) the goods are not goods which may be listed under\nsection 26A or 26AE;\nthen, subject to this section, the Secretary is not to refuse to list the\ngoods in relation to the person except where the Secretary is\nsatisfied that:\n(c) the goods are not eligible for listing; or\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 26\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(d) the goods are not safe for the purposes for which they are to\nbe used; or\n(e) the presentation of the goods is unacceptable; or\n(f) the goods do not conform to a standard applicable to the\ngoods; or\n(fa) either of the following has not been complied with in relation\nto the goods:\n(i) an applicable provision of the Therapeutic Goods\nAdvertising Code;\n(ii) any other requirement relating to advertising applicable\nunder Part 5-1 or the regulations; or\n(g) if a step in the manufacture of the goods has been carried out\noutside Australia—the manufacturing and quality control\nprocedures used in the manufacture of the goods are not\nacceptable; or\n(h) if the goods have been manufactured in Australia—the goods\nhave been manufactured contrary to Part 3-3; or\n(j) if the goods have been manufactured in Australia, or\nimported into Australia, solely for export—a relevant\nauthority of the country to which the goods are to be\nexported has not confirmed its willingness to accept the\ngoods and:\n(i) the goods have been refused registration or listing for\nsupply in Australia; or\n(ii) the Secretary requires such a confirmation for a reason\nother than because the goods have been refused\nregistration or listing; or\n(k) the goods do not comply with prescribed quality or safety\ncriteria; or\n(l) if there are one or more absolute prohibitions in force for the\npurposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3)—imports into Australia,\nexports from Australia or supplies in Australia of the goods\nwould contravene one or more of those prohibitions; or\n(la) if there are one or more prohibitions in force for the purposes\nof subsection 9K(1) or (3) that are subject to conditions—\nimports into Australia, exports from Australia or supplies in\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where:\n(a) an application is made for the listing of therapeutic goods in\nrelation to a person under section 23; and\n(aaa) the application complies with section 23C; and\n(aa) the application is accompanied by either:\n(i) the certificate required under subsection 26B(1); or\n(ii) a notice (in accordance with a form approved, in\nwriting, by the Secretary) that a certificate under that\nsubsection is not required in relation to the application;\nand\n(b) the person has complied with any requirements made by the\nSecretary under section 31 in relation to the goods; and\n(ba) the goods are not goods which may be listed under\nsection 26A or 26AE;\nthen, subject to this section, the Secretary is not to refuse to list the\ngoods in relation to the person except where the Secretary is\nsatisfied that:\n(c) the goods are not eligible for listing; or\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 26\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(d) the goods are not safe for the purposes for which they are to\nbe used; or\n(e) the presentation of the goods is unacceptable; or\n(f) the goods do not conform to a standard applicable to the\ngoods; or\n(fa) either of the following has not been complied with in relation\nto the goods:\n(i) an applicable provision of the Therapeutic Goods\nAdvertising Code;\n(ii) any other requirement relating to advertising applicable\nunder Part 5-1 or the regulations; or\n(g) if a step in the manufacture of the goods has been carried out\noutside Australia—the manufacturing and quality control\nprocedures used in the manufacture of the goods are not\nacceptable; or\n(h) if the goods have been manufactured in Australia—the goods\nhave been manufactured contrary to Part 3-3; or\n(j) if the goods have been manufactured in Australia, or\nimported into Australia, solely for export—a relevant\nauthority of the country to which the goods",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "44c0529b7264dced4a0ece3601f18204662a12e4409cf6c5f0ffe7966ed228e2",
      "skos:note": "Listing of therapeutic goods"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-26",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26 Listing of therapeutic goods",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 160,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where:\n(a) an application is made for the listing of therapeutic goods in\nrelation to a person under section 23; and\n(aaa) the application complies with section 23C; and\n(aa) the application is accompanied by either:\n(i) the certificate required under subsection 26B(1); or\n(ii) a notice (in accordance with a form approved, in\nwriting, by the Secretary) that a certificate under that\nsubsection is not required in relation to the application;\nand\n(b) the person has complied with any requirements made by the\nSecretary under section 31 in relation to the goods; and\n(ba) the goods are not goods which may be listed under\nsection 26A or 26AE;\nthen, subject to this section, the Secretary is not to refuse to list the\ngoods in relation to the person except where the Secretary is\nsatisfied that:\n(c) the goods are not eligible for listing; or\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 26\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(d) the goods are not safe for the purposes for which they are to\nbe used; or\n(e) the presentation of the goods is unacceptable; or\n(f) the goods do not conform to a standard applicable to the\ngoods; or\n(fa) either of the following has not been complied with in relation\nto the goods:\n(i) an applicable provision of the Therapeutic Goods\nAdvertising Code;\n(ii) any other requirement relating to advertising applicable\nunder Part 5-1 or the regulations; or\n(g) if a step in the manufacture of the goods has been carried out\noutside Australia—the manufacturing and quality control\nprocedures used in the manufacture of the goods are not\nacceptable; or\n(h) if the goods have been manufactured in Australia—the goods\nhave been manufactured contrary to Part 3-3; or\n(j) if the goods have been manufactured in Australia, or\nimported into Australia, solely for export—a relevant\nauthority of the country to which the goods are to be\nexported has not confirmed its willingness to accept the\ngoods and:\n(i) the goods have been refused registration or listing for\nsupply in Australia; or\n(ii) the Secretary requires such a confirmation for a reason\nother than because the goods have been refused\nregistration or listing; or\n(k) the goods do not comply with prescribed quality or safety\ncriteria; or\n(l) if there are one or more absolute prohibitions in force for the\npurposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3)—imports into Australia,\nexports from Australia or supplies in Australia of the goods\nwould contravene one or more of those prohibitions; or\n(la) if there are one or more prohibitions in force for the purposes\nof subsection 9K(1) or (3) that are subject to conditions—\nimports into Australia, exports from Australia or supplies in\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
