      "values:originalText": "(5) If:\n(a) an application is made under section 23 in relation to a\nmedicine for listing under section 26AE; and\n(b) the applicant has paid the whole of the evaluation fee; and\n(c) regulations made for the purposes of paragraph 63(2)(daaaa)\nprescribe a period within which evaluations under\nsection 26AE in relation to the medicine must be completed;\nand\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If:\n(a) an application is made under section 23 in relation to a\nmedicine for listing under section 26AE; and\n(b) the applicant has paid the whole of the evaluation fee; and\n(c) regulations made for the purposes of paragraph 63(2)(daaaa)\nprescribe a period within which evaluations under\nsection 26AE in relation to the medicine must be completed;\nand\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ac"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ac-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ac-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1d01f11d5556c8a7d7b129bb4dbce2c96fc117499c1977db49193d905b960050",
      "skos:note": "Pay evaluation fee before listing medicine under section 26AE"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-26ac-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26AC(5) Evaluation fees for listing of medicine under section 26AE",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 173,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If:\n(a) an application is made under section 23 in relation to a\nmedicine for listing under section 26AE; and\n(b) the applicant has paid the whole of the evaluation fee; and\n(c) regulations made for the purposes of paragraph 63(2)(daaaa)\nprescribe a period within which evaluations under\nsection 26AE in relation to the medicine must be completed;\nand\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ac-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ac-ss-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ac-ss-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must pay evaluation fee",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ad",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26AD Lapsing and deemed refusal of applications for listing of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-26ad"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.174",
      "values:originalText": "medicine under section 26AE\nLapsing of applications\n(1) An application for the listing of a medicine under section 26AE\nlapses if:\n(a) any part of the evaluation fee referred to in section 26AC\nremains unpaid at the end of 28 days after the day on which\nthe amount became due and payable; or\n(b) the application contains information that is inaccurate or\nmisleading in a material particular; or\n(c) information given to the Secretary by, or on behalf of, the\napplicant in connection with the application is inaccurate or\nmisleading in a material particular.\nDeemed refusal of applications\n(2) If:\n(a) regulations made for the purposes of paragraph 63(2)(daaaa)\nprescribe a period within which evaluations under\nsection 26AE in relation to the medicine must be completed;\nand\n(b) at the end of that period, the evaluation has not been\ncompleted;\nthe applicant may give the Secretary written notice that the\napplicant wishes to treat the application as having been refused.\n(3) A notice under subsection (2) may be given at any time before the\nevaluation is completed.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 26AE\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(4) If a notice has been given, this Act (except subsection 60(5)) has\neffect as if:\n(a) the Secretary had decided not to list the medicine which is\nthe subject of the application; and\n(b) the Minister had made a decision under subsection 60(3)\nconfirming the decision of the Secretary; and\n(c) the Minister’s decision had been made on the day on which\nnotice was given to the Secretary under subsection (2).",
      "skos:definition": "medicine under section 26AE\nLapsing of applications\n(1) An application for the listing of a medicine under section 26AE\nlapses if:\n(a) any part of the evaluation fee referred to in section 26AC\nremains unpaid at the end of 28 days after the day on which\nthe amount became due and payable; or\n(b) the application contains information that is inaccurate or\nmisleading in a material particular; or\n(c) information given to the Secretary by, or on behalf of, the\napplicant in connection with the application is inaccurate or\nmisleading in a material particular.\nDeemed refusal of applications\n(2) If:\n(a) regulations made for the purposes of paragraph 63(2)(daaaa)\nprescribe a period within which evaluations under\nsection 26AE in relation to the medicine must be completed;\nand\n(b) at the end of that period, the evaluation has not been\ncompleted;\nthe applicant may give the Secretary written notice that the\napplicant wishes to treat the application as having been refused.\n(3) A notice under subsection (2) may be given at any time before the\nevaluation is completed.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 26AE\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(4) If a notice has been given, this Act (except subsection 60(5)) has\neffect as if:\n(a) the Secretary had decided not to list the medicine which is\nthe subject of the application; and\n(b) the Minister had made a decision under subsection 60(3)\nconfirming the decision of the Secretary; and\n(c) the Minister’s decision had been made on the day on which\nnotice was given to the Secretary under subsection (2).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ad-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ad-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ad-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ad-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "68f39f5b384d9e42a9e3cb3607877a04c5a02447c47a83d8f1956cb38f3ba234"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-26ad",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26AD Lapsing and deemed refusal of applications for listing of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 174,
      "values:originalText": "medicine under section 26AE\nLapsing of applications\n(1) An application for the listing of a medicine under section 26AE\nlapses if:\n(a) any part of the evaluation fee referred to in section 26AC\nremains unpaid at the end of 28 days after the day on which\nthe amount became due and payable; or\n(b) the application contains information that is inaccurate or\nmisleading in a material particular; or\n(c) information given to the Secretary by, or on behalf of, the\napplicant in connection with the application is inaccurate or\nmisleading in a material particular.\nDeemed refusal of applications\n(2) If:\n(a) regulations made for the purposes of paragraph 63(2)(daaaa)\nprescribe a period within which evaluations under\nsection 26AE in relation to the medicine must be completed;\nand\n(b) at the end of that period, the evaluation has not been\ncompleted;\nthe applicant may give the Secretary written notice that the\napplicant wishes to treat the application as having been refused.\n(3) A notice under subsection (2) may be given at any time before the\nevaluation is completed.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 26AE\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(4) If a notice has been given, this Act (except subsection 60(5)) has\neffect as if:\n(a) the Secretary had decided not to list the medicine which is\nthe subject of the application; and\n(b) the Minister had made a decision under subsection 60(3)\nconfirming the decision of the Secretary; and\n(c) the Minister’s decision had been made on the day on which\nnotice was given to the Secretary under subsection (2)."
    },
