      "cml:premiseText": "(4) If a notice has been given"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ae",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26AE Evaluation and listing of certain medicines",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-26ae"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.175",
      "values:originalText": "Evaluation\n(1) If:\n(a) an application is made under section 23 for the listing of a\nmedicine in relation to a person under this section; and\n(b) the application has passed preliminary assessment;\nthe Secretary must evaluate the medicine having regard to:\n\n(c) whether the efficacy of the medicine for the purposes for\nwhich it is to be used has been satisfactorily established; and\n(d) such other matters (if any) as the Secretary considers\nrelevant.\nNote:\nThe Secretary must not use restricted information when evaluating the\nmedicine for listing: see section 26AF.\n(2) If a period in relation to which an evaluation under this section\nmust be completed has been prescribed under\nparagraph 63(2)(daaaa), the evaluation must be completed within\nthat period.\nSecretary must decide whether to list medicine\n(3) After an evaluation under this section of goods has been\ncompleted, the Secretary must decide:\n(a) to list the medicine; or\n(b) not to list the medicine.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "Evaluation\n(1) If:\n(a) an application is made under section 23 for the listing of a\nmedicine in relation to a person under this section; and\n(b) the application has passed preliminary assessment;\nthe Secretary must evaluate the medicine having regard to:\n\n(c) whether the efficacy of the medicine for the purposes for\nwhich it is to be used has been satisfactorily established; and\n(d) such other matters (if any) as the Secretary considers\nrelevant.\nNote:\nThe Secretary must not use restricted information when evaluating the\nmedicine for listing: see section 26AF.\n(2) If a period in relation to which an evaluation under this section\nmust be completed has been prescribed under\nparagraph 63(2)(daaaa), the evaluation must be completed within\nthat period.\nSecretary must decide whether to list medicine\n(3) After an evaluation under this section of goods has been\ncompleted, the Secretary must decide:\n(a) to list the medicine; or\n(b) not to list the medicine.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ae-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ae-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ae-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "163e44b102626149bbbfb058eee4fcfa7748b40949629e0a1a4ff058f3bb548b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-26ae",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26AE Evaluation and listing of certain medicines",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 175,
      "values:originalText": "Evaluation\n(1) If:\n(a) an application is made under section 23 for the listing of a\nmedicine in relation to a person under this section; and\n(b) the application has passed preliminary assessment;\nthe Secretary must evaluate the medicine having regard to:\n\n(c) whether the efficacy of the medicine for the purposes for\nwhich it is to be used has been satisfactorily established; and\n(d) such other matters (if any) as the Secretary considers\nrelevant.\nNote:\nThe Secretary must not use restricted information when evaluating the\nmedicine for listing: see section 26AF.\n(2) If a period in relation to which an evaluation under this section\nmust be completed has been prescribed under\nparagraph 63(2)(daaaa), the evaluation must be completed within\nthat period.\nSecretary must decide whether to list medicine\n(3) After an evaluation under this section of goods has been\ncompleted, the Secretary must decide:\n(a) to list the medicine; or\n(b) not to list the medicine.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
