    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26bd-ss-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26BD(9) Requirements relating to an application for variation of a",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-26bd-ss-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.182",
      "values:originalText": "(9) The Secretary may, by legislative instrument, determine a form of\ninformation for the purposes of subparagraph (3)(e)(ii).\n26BDA  Lapsing of application for variation of a section 26BB\ndetermination\nIf an application made under subsection 26BD(1) has passed\npreliminary assessment, the application lapses if:\n(a) the application contains information that is inaccurate or\nmisleading in a material particular; or\n(b) information given to the Secretary by, or on behalf of, the\napplicant in connection with the application is inaccurate or\nmisleading in a material particular; or\n(c) the evaluation fee prescribed for the purposes of\nparagraph 26BE(3)(b) has not been paid before the end of the\nperiod worked out in accordance with the regulations.",
      "skos:definition": "(9) The Secretary may, by legislative instrument, determine a form of\ninformation for the purposes of subparagraph (3)(e)(ii).\n26BDA  Lapsing of application for variation of a section 26BB\ndetermination\nIf an application made under subsection 26BD(1) has passed\npreliminary assessment, the application lapses if:\n(a) the application contains information that is inaccurate or\nmisleading in a material particular; or\n(b) information given to the Secretary by, or on behalf of, the\napplicant in connection with the application is inaccurate or\nmisleading in a material particular; or\n(c) the evaluation fee prescribed for the purposes of\nparagraph 26BE(3)(b) has not been paid before the end of the\nperiod worked out in accordance with the regulations.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26bd"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26bd-ss-9-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26bd-ss-9-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ac3e3500ed495d6adcf72e74f38f7a60de5690ffeb14ebf85d01088b6565ee37",
      "skos:note": "Application lapse due to inaccurate or misleading information"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-26bd-ss-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26BD(9) Requirements relating to an application for variation of a",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 182,
      "values:originalText": "(9) The Secretary may, by legislative instrument, determine a form of\ninformation for the purposes of subparagraph (3)(e)(ii).\n26BDA  Lapsing of application for variation of a section 26BB\ndetermination\nIf an application made under subsection 26BD(1) has passed\npreliminary assessment, the application lapses if:\n(a) the application contains information that is inaccurate or\nmisleading in a material particular; or\n(b) information given to the Secretary by, or on behalf of, the\napplicant in connection with the application is inaccurate or\nmisleading in a material particular; or\n(c) the evaluation fee prescribed for the purposes of\nparagraph 26BE(3)(b) has not been paid before the end of the\nperiod worked out in accordance with the regulations."
    },
    {
