    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26bf-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26BF(2) Permissible indications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-26bf-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.186",
      "values:originalText": "(2) In deciding whether to make a determination under subsection (1)\nin relation to a particular indication, the Minister may have regard\nto whether the indication is a therapeutic use that relates to one or\nmore of the following:\n(a) maintaining health;\n(b) enhancing health;\n(c) preventing a dietary deficiency;\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 26BG\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(d) a disease, ailment, defect or injury, other than a serious form\nof the disease, ailment, defect or injury.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) In deciding whether to make a determination under subsection (1)\nin relation to a particular indication, the Minister may have regard\nto whether the indication is a therapeutic use that relates to one or\nmore of the following:\n(a) maintaining health;\n(b) enhancing health;\n(c) preventing a dietary deficiency;\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 26BG\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(d) a disease, ailment, defect or injury, other than a serious form\nof the disease, ailment, defect or injury.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26bf"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26bf-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9c2e6715f958e751000f9ebe6f459a5525c44b6c49a03c73db2e96a5849dcc66",
      "skos:note": "The Minister may consider therapeutic uses of a substance when making a determination."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-26bf-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26BF(2) Permissible indications",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 186,
      "values:originalText": "(2) In deciding whether to make a determination under subsection (1)\nin relation to a particular indication, the Minister may have regard\nto whether the indication is a therapeutic use that relates to one or\nmore of the following:\n(a) maintaining health;\n(b) enhancing health;\n(c) preventing a dietary deficiency;\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 26BG\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(d) a disease, ailment, defect or injury, other than a serious form\nof the disease, ailment, defect or injury."
    },
