      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 207,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The information with which subsection (1) is concerned is\ninformation of the following kinds:\n(a) information that contradicts information already given by the\nperson under this Act;\n(b) information that indicates that the use of the goods in\naccordance with the recommendations for their use may have\nan unintended harmful effect;\n(c) information that indicates that the goods, when used in\naccordance with the recommendations for their use, may not\nbe as effective as the application for registration or listing of\nthe goods or information already given by the person under\nthis Act suggests;\n(d) information that indicates that the quality, safety or efficacy\nof the goods is unacceptable."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-29aa-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-29aa-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-29aa-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits failing to notify adverse effects of goods.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person under this Act must provide information about adverse effects.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Failing to do so is a civil penalty."
    },
    {
