    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-29c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29C Civil penalties for failing to notify adverse effects etc. where",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-29c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.208",
      "values:originalText": "application withdrawn or lapses\nCivil penalty for failing to comply with requirements of a notice\n(1) A person contravenes this subsection if the person does not comply\nwith the requirements of a notice under subsection 29B(1) within\n30 days after the day on which the notice is given to the person.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—3,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—30,000 penalty units.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 29D\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nCivil penalty for giving false or misleading information in\npurported compliance with requirements of a notice\n(2) A person contravenes this subsection if the person, in purported\ncompliance with a notice under subsection 29B(1), gives\ninformation that is false or misleading in a material particular.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—3,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—30,000 penalty units.",
      "skos:definition": "application withdrawn or lapses\nCivil penalty for failing to comply with requirements of a notice\n(1) A person contravenes this subsection if the person does not comply\nwith the requirements of a notice under subsection 29B(1) within\n30 days after the day on which the notice is given to the person.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—3,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—30,000 penalty units.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 29D\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nCivil penalty for giving false or misleading information in\npurported compliance with requirements of a notice\n(2) A person contravenes this subsection if the person, in purported\ncompliance with a notice under subsection 29B(1), gives\ninformation that is false or misleading in a material particular.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—3,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—30,000 penalty units.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-29c-ss-1"
        },
