    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-29f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29F Revocation of suspension",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-29f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.211",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary must revoke a suspension under section 29D, by\nwritten notice given to the person in relation to whom the\ntherapeutic goods are included in the Register, if the Secretary is\nsatisfied that:\n(a) the ground on which the registration or listing of the\ntherapeutic goods was suspended no longer applies; and\n(b) there are no other grounds for suspending the registration or\nlisting of the therapeutic goods.\n(2) The Secretary’s power to revoke the suspension may be exercised:\n(a) if the person in relation to whom the therapeutic goods are\nincluded in the Register applies in writing to the Secretary; or\n(b) on the Secretary’s own initiative.\nPublication\n(3) As soon as practicable after giving a notice under subsection (1),\nthe Secretary must cause to be published in the Gazette or on the\nDepartment’s website a notice setting out particulars of the\nrevocation.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary must revoke a suspension under section 29D, by\nwritten notice given to the person in relation to whom the\ntherapeutic goods are included in the Register, if the Secretary is\nsatisfied that:\n(a) the ground on which the registration or listing of the\ntherapeutic goods was suspended no longer applies; and\n(b) there are no other grounds for suspending the registration or\nlisting of the therapeutic goods.\n(2) The Secretary’s power to revoke the suspension may be exercised:\n(a) if the person in relation to whom the therapeutic goods are\nincluded in the Register applies in writing to the Secretary; or\n(b) on the Secretary’s own initiative.\nPublication\n(3) As soon as practicable after giving a notice under subsection (1),\nthe Secretary must cause to be published in the Gazette or on the\nDepartment’s website a notice setting out particulars of the\nrevocation.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-29f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-29f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-29f-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "74e82e7bf30fea15b41c7611eeaf0a17121a666c1f6ddc1e1052f6b06ef06589"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-29f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29F Revocation of suspension",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 211,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary must revoke a suspension under section 29D, by\nwritten notice given to the person in relation to whom the\ntherapeutic goods are included in the Register, if the Secretary is\nsatisfied that:\n(a) the ground on which the registration or listing of the\ntherapeutic goods was suspended no longer applies; and\n(b) there are no other grounds for suspending the registration or\nlisting of the therapeutic goods.\n(2) The Secretary’s power to revoke the suspension may be exercised:\n(a) if the person in relation to whom the therapeutic goods are\nincluded in the Register applies in writing to the Secretary; or\n(b) on the Secretary’s own initiative.\nPublication\n(3) As soon as practicable after giving a notice under subsection (1),\nthe Secretary must cause to be published in the Gazette or on the\nDepartment’s website a notice setting out particulars of the\nrevocation.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
