    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30aa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30AA Revocation of cancellation of registration or listing—payment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-30aa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.218",
      "values:originalText": "of annual registration or listing charge\n(1) If:\n(a) the Secretary cancels the registration or listing of therapeutic\ngoods because the annual registration or listing charge was\nnot paid within 28 days after it became payable (see\nparagraph 30(1)(h)); and\n(b) before the end of the period of 90 days beginning on the day\nthe goods ceased to be registered or listed, the person\nrequests, in writing, the Secretary to revoke the cancellation;\nand\n(c) the annual registration or listing charge has been paid; and\n(d) the request is accompanied by the prescribed application fee;\nthe Secretary may, by notice in writing given to the person, revoke\nthe cancellation.\n(2) If the cancellation is revoked, the cancellation is taken never to\nhave occurred.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 30B\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "of annual registration or listing charge\n(1) If:\n(a) the Secretary cancels the registration or listing of therapeutic\ngoods because the annual registration or listing charge was\nnot paid within 28 days after it became payable (see\nparagraph 30(1)(h)); and\n(b) before the end of the period of 90 days beginning on the day\nthe goods ceased to be registered or listed, the person\nrequests, in writing, the Secretary to revoke the cancellation;\nand\n(c) the annual registration or listing charge has been paid; and\n(d) the request is accompanied by the prescribed application fee;\nthe Secretary may, by notice in writing given to the person, revoke\nthe cancellation.\n(2) If the cancellation is revoked, the cancellation is taken never to\nhave occurred.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nRegistration and listing  Division 2\nSection 30B\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
