    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30el",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30EL Substitution of prescription medicine by pharmacists",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-30el"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.237",
      "values:originalText": "If:\n(a) an instrument is in force under subsection 30EK(1); and\n(b) under a law of a State or Territory, a pharmacist is authorised\nto dispense medicine (the scarce medicine) covered by\nparagraph 30EK(1)(a) to a person;\nthen, despite any law of a State or Territory, the pharmacist may\ndispense medicine covered by paragraph 30EK(1)(b) to that person\nin substitution for the scarce medicine, provided that the\nsubstitution is in the circumstances specified in the instrument\nunder subsection 30EK(1).\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "If:\n(a) an instrument is in force under subsection 30EK(1); and\n(b) under a law of a State or Territory, a pharmacist is authorised\nto dispense medicine (the scarce medicine) covered by\nparagraph 30EK(1)(a) to a person;\nthen, despite any law of a State or Territory, the pharmacist may\ndispense medicine covered by paragraph 30EK(1)(b) to that person\nin substitution for the scarce medicine, provided that the\nsubstitution is in the circumstances specified in the instrument\nunder subsection 30EK(1).\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30el-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30el-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c1d84a9818ab11e0b4164982262f55745a49c3189648d669af73769211591214",
      "skos:note": "Pharmacist may dispense scarce medicine in substitution for another"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-30el",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "30EL Substitution of prescription medicine by pharmacists",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 237,
      "values:originalText": "If:\n(a) an instrument is in force under subsection 30EK(1); and\n(b) under a law of a State or Territory, a pharmacist is authorised\nto dispense medicine (the scarce medicine) covered by\nparagraph 30EK(1)(a) to a person;\nthen, despite any law of a State or Territory, the pharmacist may\ndispense medicine covered by paragraph 30EK(1)(b) to that person\nin substitution for the scarce medicine, provided that the\nsubstitution is in the circumstances specified in the instrument\nunder subsection 30EK(1).\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30el-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30el"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30el-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permission to dispense",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30F Criminal offences for goods exempt under section 18A not",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-30f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.238",
      "values:originalText": "conforming to standards etc.\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) therapeutic goods of a particular kind are exempt under\nsection 18A; and\n(b) a person supplies a batch of goods of that kind; and\n(c) the Secretary is satisfied that the goods included in that\nbatch:\n(i) do not conform to a standard applicable to goods of that\nkind; or\n(ii) are otherwise not fit to be used for their intended\npurposes.\n(2) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the person, require\nthe person to take steps to recall the goods included in that batch\n(except any of those goods that cannot be recalled because they\nhave been administered to, or applied in the treatment of, a person).\n(3) The notice may specify one or more of the following requirements:\n(a) the steps to be taken to recall the goods;\n(b) the manner in which the steps are to be taken;\n(c) a reasonable period within which the steps are to be taken.\n(4) The Secretary must, as soon as practicable after giving the notice,\ncause particulars of it to be published in the Gazette or on the\nDepartment’s website.\nWritten notice is not a legislative instrument\n(4A) A written notice given to a person by the Secretary under this\nsection is not a legislative instrument.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nGeneral  Division 3\nSection 30F\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nOffences\n(4B) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the Secretary gives a notice to the person under\nsubsection (2); and\n(b) the notice specifies a particular requirement mentioned in\nsubsection (3); and\n(c) the person fails to comply with that requirement; and\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of the goods has resulted in, will result in, or is\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the goods, if the goods were used, would\nresult in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury\nto any person; and\n(e) the harm or injury has resulted, will result, is likely to result,\nwould result, or would be likely to result, because the person\nfailed to comply with that requirement.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (5) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the Secretary gives a notice to the person under\nsubsection (2); and\n(b) the notice specifies a particular requirement mentioned in\nsubsection (3); and\n(c) the person fails to comply with that requirement.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(6) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the Secretary gives a notice to the person under\nsubsection (2); and\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "conforming to standards etc.\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) therapeutic goods of a particular kind are exempt under\nsection 18A; and\n(b) a person supplies a batch of goods of that kind; and\n(c) the Secretary is satisfied that the goods included in that\nbatch:\n(i) do not conform to a standard applicable to goods of that\nkind; or\n(ii) are otherwise not fit to be used for their intended\npurposes.\n(2) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the person, require\nthe person to take steps to recall the goods included in that batch\n(except any of those goods that cannot be recalled because they\nhave been administered to, or applied in the treatment of, a person).\n(3) The notice may specify one or more of the following requirements:\n(a) the steps to be taken to recall the goods;\n(b) the manner in which the steps are to be taken;\n(c) a reasonable period within which the steps are to be taken.\n(4) The Secretary must, as soon as practicable after giving the notice,\ncause particulars of it to be published in the Gazette or on the\nDepartment’s website.\nWritten notice is not a legislative instrument\n(4A) A written notice given to a person by the Secretary under this\nsection is not a legislative instrument.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nGeneral  Division 3\nSection 30F\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nOffences\n(4B) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the Secretary gives a notice to the person under\nsubsection (2); and\n(b) the notice specifies a particular requirement mentioned in\nsubsection (3); and\n(c) the person fails to comply with that requirement; and\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of the goods has resulted in, will result in, or is\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the goods, if the goods were used, would\nresult in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury\nto any person; and\n(e) the harm or injury has resulte",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-4a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-4b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-5"
        },
