    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-4a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30F(4A) Criminal offences for goods exempt under section 18A not",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-30f-ss-4a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.238",
      "values:originalText": "(4A) A written notice given to a person by the Secretary under this\nsection is not a legislative instrument.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nGeneral  Division 3\nSection 30F\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nOffences",
      "skos:definition": "(4A) A written notice given to a person by the Secretary under this\nsection is not a legislative instrument.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nGeneral  Division 3\nSection 30F\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nOffences",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-4a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-4a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7ebd8475f22eec6693df87720bc9abe216cfe210b3f07867ef38be915a8f5704",
      "skos:note": "A written notice given to a person by the Secretary under this section is not a legislative instrument."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-30f-ss-4a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "30F(4A) Criminal offences for goods exempt under section 18A not",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 238,
      "values:originalText": "(4A) A written notice given to a person by the Secretary under this\nsection is not a legislative instrument.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nGeneral  Division 3\nSection 30F\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nOffences"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-4a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-4a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-4a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits notices from being considered legislative instruments.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "None",
      "cml:conclusionText": "None"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-4b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30F(4B) Criminal offences for goods exempt under section 18A not",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-30f-ss-4b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.238",
      "values:originalText": "(4B) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the Secretary gives a notice to the person under\nsubsection (2); and\n(b) the notice specifies a particular requirement mentioned in\nsubsection (3); and\n(c) the person fails to comply with that requirement; and\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of the goods has resulted in, will result in, or is\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the goods, if the goods were used, would\nresult in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury\nto any person; and\n(e) the harm or injury has resulted, will result, is likely to result,\nwould result, or would be likely to result, because the person\nfailed to comply with that requirement.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (5) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.",
      "skos:definition": "(4B) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the Secretary gives a notice to the person under\nsubsection (2); and\n(b) the notice specifies a particular requirement mentioned in\nsubsection (3); and\n(c) the person fails to comply with that requirement; and\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of the goods has resulted in, will result in, or is\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the goods, if the goods were used, would\nresult in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury\nto any person; and\n(e) the harm or injury has resulted, will result, is likely to result,\nwould result, or would be likely to result, because the person\nfailed to comply with that requirement.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (5) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-4b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-4b-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-4b-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-4b-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-4b-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30f-ss-4b-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0adfcc10519709f44bf4af8223516387f5bf4613d270c5d6ec9bbf75c440dbcd",
      "skos:note": "Failure to comply with a notice results in harm or injury."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-30f-ss-4b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "30F(4B) Criminal offences for goods exempt under section 18A not",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 238,
      "values:originalText": "(4B) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the Secretary gives a notice to the person under\nsubsection (2); and\n(b) the notice specifies a particular requirement mentioned in\nsubsection (3); and\n(c) the person fails to comply with that requirement; and\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of the goods has resulted in, will result in, or is\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the goods, if the goods were used, would\nresult in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury\nto any person; and\n(e) the harm or injury has resulted, will result, is likely to result,\nwould result, or would be likely to result, because the person\nfailed to comply with that requirement.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (5) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA."
    },
    {
