      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Notice specifies requirement",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Non-compliance is prohibited"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30G Disposal of unused goods exempt under section 18A",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-30g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.240",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to particular therapeutic goods if:\n(a) an exemption in relation to those goods under section 18A\nceases to have effect otherwise than because those goods\nhave become registered goods or listed goods (see\nparagraph 18A(5)(a)); and\n(b) those goods have not been used before the exemption so\nceases to have effect.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nGeneral  Division 3\nSection 30H\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(2) The Secretary may arrange for the disposal of any of those goods\nin accordance with the regulations.\n(3) Regulations made for the purposes of subsection (2) may set out\nthe methods by which those goods are to be stored, supplied,\ndestroyed, exported or otherwise disposed of.\n(4) A method set out in the regulations under subsection (3) must not\nenable or permit any benefit to be conferred on a person (including\nthe Commonwealth) other than the owner of those goods.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to particular therapeutic goods if:\n(a) an exemption in relation to those goods under section 18A\nceases to have effect otherwise than because those goods\nhave become registered goods or listed goods (see\nparagraph 18A(5)(a)); and\n(b) those goods have not been used before the exemption so\nceases to have effect.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nGeneral  Division 3\nSection 30H\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(2) The Secretary may arrange for the disposal of any of those goods\nin accordance with the regulations.\n(3) Regulations made for the purposes of subsection (2) may set out\nthe methods by which those goods are to be stored, supplied,\ndestroyed, exported or otherwise disposed of.\n(4) A method set out in the regulations under subsection (3) must not\nenable or permit any benefit to be conferred on a person (including\nthe Commonwealth) other than the owner of those goods.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30g-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30g-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30g-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30g-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "45ff15ef881a4e851ca91e68bc2e683c331cdfd2cc5574bdf871b67018649bf7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-30g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "30G Disposal of unused goods exempt under section 18A",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 240,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to particular therapeutic goods if:\n(a) an exemption in relation to those goods under section 18A\nceases to have effect otherwise than because those goods\nhave become registered goods or listed goods (see\nparagraph 18A(5)(a)); and\n(b) those goods have not been used before the exemption so\nceases to have effect.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nGeneral  Division 3\nSection 30H\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(2) The Secretary may arrange for the disposal of any of those goods\nin accordance with the regulations.\n(3) Regulations made for the purposes of subsection (2) may set out\nthe methods by which those goods are to be stored, supplied,\ndestroyed, exported or otherwise disposed of.\n(4) A method set out in the regulations under subsection (3) must not\nenable or permit any benefit to be conferred on a person (including\nthe Commonwealth) other than the owner of those goods."
    },
