    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30H Record for goods exempt under section 18A",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-30h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.241",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) there are therapeutic goods that are exempt under\nsection 18A; and\n(b) a condition of the exemption:\n(i) requires the person to keep a record about those goods;\nor\n(ii) specifies the manner in which the person must keep the\nrecord; and\n(c) the person does an act or omits to do an act in relation to\nthose goods; and\n(d) the act or omission results in the breach of that condition of\nthe exemption.\nPenalty: 240 penalty units.\n(2) Strict liability applies to paragraph (1)(b).\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) there are therapeutic goods that are exempt under\nsection 18A; and\n(b) a condition of the exemption:\n(i) requires the person to keep a record about those goods;\nor\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) there are therapeutic goods that are exempt under\nsection 18A; and\n(b) a condition of the exemption:\n(i) requires the person to keep a record about those goods;\nor\n(ii) specifies the manner in which the person must keep the\nrecord; and\n(c) the person does an act or omits to do an act in relation to\nthose goods; and\n(d) the act or omission results in the breach of that condition of\nthe exemption.\nPenalty: 240 penalty units.\n(2) Strict liability applies to paragraph (1)(b).\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) there are therapeutic goods that are exempt under\nsection 18A; and\n(b) a condition of the exemption:\n(i) requires the person to keep a record about those goods;\nor\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30h-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30h-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "40c27e916eaa50d59579a66ca8e29a74b0b5610d2f88ef1fa4a5709a40dcdb78"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-30h",
