    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-31c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31C Criminal offences for failing to give information or documents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-31c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.254",
      "values:originalText": "sought under section 31A, 31AA, 31B or 31BA\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 31A, 31AA, 31B or\n31BA; and\n(b) the person fails to comply with the notice.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nGeneral  Division 3\nSection 31D\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nPenalty: 400 penalty units.\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 31A, 31AA, 31B or\n31BA; and\n(b) the person fails to comply with the notice.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(3) An offence against subsection (2) is an offence of strict liability.",
      "skos:definition": "sought under section 31A, 31AA, 31B or 31BA\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 31A, 31AA, 31B or\n31BA; and\n(b) the person fails to comply with the notice.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nGeneral  Division 3\nSection 31D\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nPenalty: 400 penalty units.\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 31A, 31AA, 31B or\n31BA; and\n(b) the person fails to comply with the notice.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(3) An offence against subsection (2) is an offence of strict liability.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-31c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-31c-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-31c-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a79e4cc5ec0d8659396307f90adb4e677b5b3cf6d2130ca8cdc48ad1956fe850"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-31c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31C Criminal offences for failing to give information or documents",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 254,
      "values:originalText": "sought under section 31A, 31AA, 31B or 31BA\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 31A, 31AA, 31B or\n31BA; and\n(b) the person fails to comply with the notice.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nGeneral  Division 3\nSection 31D\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nPenalty: 400 penalty units.\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 31A, 31AA, 31B or\n31BA; and\n(b) the person fails to comply with the notice.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(3) An offence against subsection (2) is an offence of strict liability."
    },
