      "cml:logicSummary": "Specifies the temporal interval for giving false or misleading information as after receiving a notice.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person gives information to the Secretary in compliance or purported compliance with the notice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-31d-ss-1a-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits omitting any matter or thing without which the information is misleading.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The information omits any matter or thing without which it is misleading."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-31d-ss-1a-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imposes an obligation on the person to provide accurate information that includes all necessary matters and things.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The information must include all matter and thing without which it is misleading."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-31e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31E False or misleading documents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-31e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.256",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person produces a document to the Secretary; and\n(b) the person does so knowing that the document is false or\nmisleading; and\n(c) the document is produced in compliance or purported\ncompliance with a notice given under section 31A, 31AA,\n31B or 31BA.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(1A) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person produces a document to the Secretary; and\n(b) the document is false or misleading; and\n(c) the document is produced in compliance or purported\ncompliance with a notice given under section 31A, 31AA,\n31B or 31BA.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nGeneral  Division 3\nSection 31F\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(1B) An offence against subsection (1A) is an offence of strict liability.\n(2) Subsection (1) or (1A) does not apply if the document is not false\nor misleading in a material particular.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\n(3) Subsection (1) or (1A) does not apply to a person who produces a\ndocument if the document is accompanied by a written statement\nsigned by the person or, in the case of a body corporate, by a\ncompetent officer of the body corporate:\n(a) stating that the document is, to the knowledge of the\nfirst-mentioned person, false or misleading in a material\nparticular; and\n(b) setting out, or referring to, the material particular in which\nthe document is, to the knowledge of the first-mentioned\nperson, false or misleading.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (3): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person produces a document to the Secretary; and\n(b) the person does so knowing that the document is false or\nmisleading; and\n(c) the document is produced in compliance or purported\ncompliance with a notice given under section 31A, 31AA,\n31B or 31BA.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(1A) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person produces a document to the Secretary; and\n(b) the document is false or misleading; and\n(c) the document is produced in compliance or purported\ncompliance with a notice given under section 31A, 31AA,\n31B or 31BA.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nRegistration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2\nGeneral  Division 3\nSection 31F\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(1B) An offence against subsection (1A) is an offence of strict liability.\n(2) Subsection (1) or (1A) does not apply if the document is not false\nor misleading in a material particular.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\n(3) Subsection (1) or (1A) does not apply to a person who produces a\ndocument if the document is accompanied by a written statement\nsigned by the person or, in the case of a body corporate, by a\ncompetent officer of the body corporate:\n(a) stating that the document is, to the knowledge of the\nfirst-mentioned person, false or misleading in a material\nparticular; and\n(b) setting out, or referring to, the material particular in which\nthe document is, to the knowledge of the first-mentioned\nperson, false or misleading.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (3): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-31e-ss-1"
        },
