    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-31e-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31E(3) False or misleading documents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-31e-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.256",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Subsection (1) or (1A) does not apply to a person who produces a\ndocument if the document is accompanied by a written statement\nsigned by the person or, in the case of a body corporate, by a\ncompetent officer of the body corporate:\n(a) stating that the document is, to the knowledge of the\nfirst-mentioned person, false or misleading in a material\nparticular; and\n(b) setting out, or referring to, the material particular in which\nthe document is, to the knowledge of the first-mentioned\nperson, false or misleading.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (3): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Subsection (1) or (1A) does not apply to a person who produces a\ndocument if the document is accompanied by a written statement\nsigned by the person or, in the case of a body corporate, by a\ncompetent officer of the body corporate:\n(a) stating that the document is, to the knowledge of the\nfirst-mentioned person, false or misleading in a material\nparticular; and\n(b) setting out, or referring to, the material particular in which\nthe document is, to the knowledge of the first-mentioned\nperson, false or misleading.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (3): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-31e"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-31e-ss-3-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e9336a74b01a2846118c1e33ea5bf36b037f1e7cc68e8ca2d19d0bae7640dffc",
      "skos:note": "Exemption from subsection (1) or (1A) for documents accompanied by a written statement"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-31e-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31E(3) False or misleading documents",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 256,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Subsection (1) or (1A) does not apply to a person who produces a\ndocument if the document is accompanied by a written statement\nsigned by the person or, in the case of a body corporate, by a\ncompetent officer of the body corporate:\n(a) stating that the document is, to the knowledge of the\nfirst-mentioned person, false or misleading in a material\nparticular; and\n(b) setting out, or referring to, the material particular in which\nthe document is, to the knowledge of the first-mentioned\nperson, false or misleading.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (3): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code."
    },
