    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32A Meaning of biological",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.259",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (3), a biological is a thing that:\n(a) either:\n(i) comprises, contains or is derived from human cells or\nhuman tissues; or\n(ii) is specified under subsection (2); and\n(b) is represented in any way to be, or is, whether because of the\nway in which it is presented or for any other reason, likely to\nbe taken to be:\n(i) for use in the treatment or prevention of a disease,\nailment, defect or injury affecting persons; or\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (3), a biological is a thing that:\n(a) either:\n(i) comprises, contains or is derived from human cells or\nhuman tissues; or\n(ii) is specified under subsection (2); and\n(b) is represented in any way to be, or is, whether because of the\nway in which it is presented or for any other reason, likely to\nbe taken to be:\n(i) for use in the treatment or prevention of a disease,\nailment, defect or injury affecting persons; or\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32a-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "688e347afe658c99d9c5d23183a0f1bd1dc0fe12bcbdceacc38180dda8ad2b58",
      "skos:note": "Defines what constitutes a biological."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32A Meaning of biological",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 259,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (3), a biological is a thing that:\n(a) either:\n(i) comprises, contains or is derived from human cells or\nhuman tissues; or\n(ii) is specified under subsection (2); and\n(b) is represented in any way to be, or is, whether because of the\nway in which it is presented or for any other reason, likely to\nbe taken to be:\n(i) for use in the treatment or prevention of a disease,\nailment, defect or injury affecting persons; or\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32a"
