      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32aa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32AA Biological classes",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32aa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.260",
      "values:originalText": "The regulations may prescribe different classes of biologicals.\nNote 1:\nThe regulations may prescribe the circumstances in which a biological\nincluded in a class of biologicals is separate and distinct from other\nbiologicals: see section 32AB.\nNote 2:\nThe Secretary may approve different application forms for different\nclasses of biologicals: see section 32DDA.\n32AB  When biologicals are separate and distinct from other\nbiologicals\n(1) The regulations may prescribe the circumstances in which a\nbiological included in a specified class of biologicals is separate\nand distinct from other biologicals.\n(2) The regulations may make different provision in relation to\ndifferent classes of biologicals that are prescribed by the\nregulations for the purposes of section 32AA.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nPreliminary  Division 1\nSection 32AB\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nNote:\nThe Secretary may cancel the entry of a biological from the Register if\nthe biological has changed so that it has become separate and distinct\nfrom the biological as so included: see subsection 32GC(1).\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "The regulations may prescribe different classes of biologicals.\nNote 1:\nThe regulations may prescribe the circumstances in which a biological\nincluded in a class of biologicals is separate and distinct from other\nbiologicals: see section 32AB.\nNote 2:\nThe Secretary may approve different application forms for different\nclasses of biologicals: see section 32DDA.\n32AB  When biologicals are separate and distinct from other\nbiologicals\n(1) The regulations may prescribe the circumstances in which a\nbiological included in a specified class of biologicals is separate\nand distinct from other biologicals.\n(2) The regulations may make different provision in relation to\ndifferent classes of biologicals that are prescribed by the\nregulations for the purposes of section 32AA.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nPreliminary  Division 1\nSection 32AB\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nNote:\nThe Secretary may cancel the entry of a biological from the Register if\nthe biological has changed so that it has become separate and distinct\nfrom the biological as so included: see subsection 32GC(1).\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32aa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32aa-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5351deba72f85072074e55b47a197b99059c1f3308d53b3d552e7a0124d0bc6c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32aa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32AA Biological classes",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 260,
      "values:originalText": "The regulations may prescribe different classes of biologicals.\nNote 1:\nThe regulations may prescribe the circumstances in which a biological\nincluded in a class of biologicals is separate and distinct from other\nbiologicals: see section 32AB.\nNote 2:\nThe Secretary may approve different application forms for different\nclasses of biologicals: see section 32DDA.\n32AB  When biologicals are separate and distinct from other\nbiologicals\n(1) The regulations may prescribe the circumstances in which a\nbiological included in a specified class of biologicals is separate\nand distinct from other biologicals.\n(2) The regulations may make different provision in relation to\ndifferent classes of biologicals that are prescribed by the\nregulations for the purposes of section 32AA.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nPreliminary  Division 1\nSection 32AB\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nNote:\nThe Secretary may cancel the entry of a biological from the Register if\nthe biological has changed so that it has become separate and distinct\nfrom the biological as so included: see subsection 32GC(1).\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
