    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32bb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32BB Criminal offences for exporting a biological",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32bb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.265",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person exports from Australia a biological for use in\nhumans; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies:\n(i) the biological is included in the Register in relation to\nthe person;\n(ii) the person is exempt under subsection 32CA(1) in\nrelation to the biological or the biological is exempt\nunder subsection 32CA(2);\n(iii) the biological is exempt under section 32CB;\n(iv) the biological is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CK(1) that is held by the person, being an\napproval covering the exportation from Australia of the\nbiological; and\n(c) either:\n(i) the use of the biological has resulted in, will result in, or\nis likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the biological, if the biological were used,\nwould result in, or would be likely to result in, harm or\ninjury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person exports from Australia a biological for use in\nhumans; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies:\n(i) the biological is included in the Register in relation to\nthe person;\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person exports from Australia a biological for use in\nhumans; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies:\n(i) the biological is included in the Register in relation to\nthe person;\n(ii) the person is exempt under subsection 32CA(1) in\nrelation to the biological or the biological is exempt\nunder subsection 32CA(2);\n(iii) the biological is exempt under section 32CB;\n(iv) the biological is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CK(1) that is held by the person, being an\napproval covering the exportation from Australia of the\nbiological; and\n(c) either:\n(i) the use of the biological has resulted in, will result in, or\nis likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the biological, if the biological were used,\nwould result in, or would be likely to result in, harm or\ninjury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person exports from Australia a biological for use in\nhumans; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies:\n(i) the biological is included in the Register in relation to\nthe person;\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32bb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32bb-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0d05543a60d54159bc0672ad0aec107894bc6e0f93628c2b37508a1a5a461618"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32bb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32BB Criminal offences for exporting a biological",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 265,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person exports from Australia a biological for use in\nhumans; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies:\n(i) the biological is included in the Register in relation to\nthe person;\n(ii) the person is exempt under subsection 32CA(1) in\nrelation to the biological or the biological is exempt\nunder subsection 32CA(2);\n(iii) the biological is exempt under section 32CB;\n(iv) the biological is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CK(1) that is held by the person, being an\napproval covering the exportation from Australia of the\nbiological; and\n(c) either:\n(i) the use of the biological has resulted in, will result in, or\nis likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the biological, if the biological were used,\nwould result in, or would be likely to result in, harm or\ninjury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person exports from Australia a biological for use in\nhumans; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies:\n(i) the biological is included in the Register in relation to\nthe person;\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
    {
