    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32bf",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32BF Civil penalties for importing, exporting, manufacturing or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32bf"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.275",
      "values:originalText": "supplying a biological\nImporting a biological for use in humans\n(1) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n(a) the person imports into Australia a biological for use in\nhumans; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies:\n(i) the biological is included in the Register in relation to\nthe person;\n(ii) the person is exempt under subsection 32CA(1) in\nrelation to the biological or the biological is exempt\nunder subsection 32CA(2);\n(iii) the biological is exempt under section 32CB;\n(iv) the biological is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CK(1) that is held by the person, being an\napproval covering the importation into Australia of the\nbiological;\n(v) the biological is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CO(1), (1A) or (2) that is held by the\nperson.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—5,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—50,000 penalty units.\nExporting a biological for use in humans\n(2) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n(a) the person exports from Australia a biological for use in\nhumans; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies:\n(i) the biological is included in the Register in relation to\nthe person;\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "supplying a biological\nImporting a biological for use in humans\n(1) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n(a) the person imports into Australia a biological for use in\nhumans; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies:\n(i) the biological is included in the Register in relation to\nthe person;\n(ii) the person is exempt under subsection 32CA(1) in\nrelation to the biological or the biological is exempt\nunder subsection 32CA(2);\n(iii) the biological is exempt under section 32CB;\n(iv) the biological is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CK(1) that is held by the person, being an\napproval covering the importation into Australia of the\nbiological;\n(v) the biological is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CO(1), (1A) or (2) that is held by the\nperson.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—5,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—50,000 penalty units.\nExporting a biological for use in humans\n(2) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n(a) the person exports from Australia a biological for use in\nhumans; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies:\n(i) the biological is included in the Register in relation to\nthe person;\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32bf-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32bf-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0677747650a09431b56b23a3cfcf39c06feec3ef42ac2c67dd31bc9f3ca5873c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32bf",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32BF Civil penalties for importing, exporting, manufacturing or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 275,
      "values:originalText": "supplying a biological\nImporting a biological for use in humans\n(1) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n(a) the person imports into Australia a biological for use in\nhumans; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies:\n(i) the biological is included in the Register in relation to\nthe person;\n(ii) the person is exempt under subsection 32CA(1) in\nrelation to the biological or the biological is exempt\nunder subsection 32CA(2);\n(iii) the biological is exempt under section 32CB;\n(iv) the biological is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CK(1) that is held by the person, being an\napproval covering the importation into Australia of the\nbiological;\n(v) the biological is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CO(1), (1A) or (2) that is held by the\nperson.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—5,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—50,000 penalty units.\nExporting a biological for use in humans\n(2) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n(a) the person exports from Australia a biological for use in\nhumans; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies:\n(i) the biological is included in the Register in relation to\nthe person;\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
