    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32bg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32BG Criminal offences and civil penalty relating to a failure to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32bg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.279",
      "values:originalText": "notify the Secretary about manufacturing\nCriminal offences\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports a biological into Australia for use in humans; or\n(ii) exports a biological from Australia for use in humans;\nor\n(iii) manufactures a biological in Australia for use in\nhumans; or\n(iv) supplies a biological in Australia for use in humans; and\n(b) the person is the sponsor of the biological; and\n(c) the person is not exempt under subsection 32CA(1) in\nrelation to the biological and the biological is not exempt\nunder subsection 32CA(2); and\n(d) the person has not, at or before the time of the importation,\nexportation, manufacture or supply, properly notified to the\nSecretary either or both of the following:\n(i) the manufacturer of the biological;\n(ii) the premises used in the manufacture of the biological.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(1A) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports a biological into Australia for use in humans; or\n(ii) exports a biological from Australia for use in humans;\nor\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "notify the Secretary about manufacturing\nCriminal offences\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports a biological into Australia for use in humans; or\n(ii) exports a biological from Australia for use in humans;\nor\n(iii) manufactures a biological in Australia for use in\nhumans; or\n(iv) supplies a biological in Australia for use in humans; and\n(b) the person is the sponsor of the biological; and\n(c) the person is not exempt under subsection 32CA(1) in\nrelation to the biological and the biological is not exempt\nunder subsection 32CA(2); and\n(d) the person has not, at or before the time of the importation,\nexportation, manufacture or supply, properly notified to the\nSecretary either or both of the following:\n(i) the manufacturer of the biological;\n(ii) the premises used in the manufacture of the biological.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(1A) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports a biological into Australia for use in humans; or\n(ii) exports a biological from Australia for use in humans;\nor\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32bg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32bg-ss-1a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dd0fec9e174dd72cf2617f620da7b466f0c8086f4c0d38048ed657f6b0617646"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32bg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32BG Criminal offences and civil penalty relating to a failure to",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 279,
      "values:originalText": "notify the Secretary about manufacturing\nCriminal offences\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports a biological into Australia for use in humans; or\n(ii) exports a biological from Australia for use in humans;\nor\n(iii) manufactures a biological in Australia for use in\nhumans; or\n(iv) supplies a biological in Australia for use in humans; and\n(b) the person is the sponsor of the biological; and\n(c) the person is not exempt under subsection 32CA(1) in\nrelation to the biological and the biological is not exempt\nunder subsection 32CA(2); and\n(d) the person has not, at or before the time of the importation,\nexportation, manufacture or supply, properly notified to the\nSecretary either or both of the following:\n(i) the manufacturer of the biological;\n(ii) the premises used in the manufacture of the biological.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(1A) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports a biological into Australia for use in humans; or\n(ii) exports a biological from Australia for use in humans;\nor\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
