    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32bl",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32BL Civil penalty for advertising biological for an indication",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32bl"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.287",
      "values:originalText": "A person contravenes this section if:\n(a) the person, by any means, advertises a biological for an\nindication; and\n(b) the biological is included in the Register; and\n(c) the indication is not an indication accepted in relation to that\ninclusion.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—5,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—50,000 penalty units.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "A person contravenes this section if:\n(a) the person, by any means, advertises a biological for an\nindication; and\n(b) the biological is included in the Register; and\n(c) the indication is not an indication accepted in relation to that\ninclusion.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—5,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—50,000 penalty units.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32bl-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32bl-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32bl-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3f0e9dca5ed0e450272c4a41587cee91108d4449fdc09162998d0291c7947e38",
      "skos:note": "Advertising biological for an indication without proper registration is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32bl",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32BL Civil penalty for advertising biological for an indication",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 287,
      "values:originalText": "A person contravenes this section if:\n(a) the person, by any means, advertises a biological for an\nindication; and\n(b) the biological is included in the Register; and\n(c) the indication is not an indication accepted in relation to that\ninclusion.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—5,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—50,000 penalty units.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32bl-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32bl"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32bl-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits advertising biological for an indication without proper registration.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32bl-logic-descriptionlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Classify",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Classifies advertisements as prohibited if they include unregistered biologicals.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32C What this Division is about",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.288",
      "values:originalText": "There are 4 kinds of exemptions in relation to biologicals:\n(a)\nexemptions of biologicals under the regulations; and\n(b)\nexemptions of biologicals to deal with emergencies; and\n(c)\nexemptions of biologicals for special and experimental\nuses; and\n(d)\nexemptions of biologicals where substitutes are\nunavailable.\nSubdivision B—Exempting biologicals under the regulations",
      "skos:definition": "There are 4 kinds of exemptions in relation to biologicals:\n(a)\nexemptions of biologicals under the regulations; and\n(b)\nexemptions of biologicals to deal with emergencies; and\n(c)\nexemptions of biologicals for special and experimental\nuses; and\n(d)\nexemptions of biologicals where substitutes are\nunavailable.\nSubdivision B—Exempting biologicals under the regulations",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32c-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c38bc359a91a2207e4a55da9309d6818217b55e4c65f0ef58a706fed4adb366f",
      "skos:note": "Exemptions of biologicals under regulations, emergencies, special and experimental uses, and substitutes unavailable."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32C What this Division is about",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 288,
      "values:originalText": "There are 4 kinds of exemptions in relation to biologicals:\n(a)\nexemptions of biologicals under the regulations; and\n(b)\nexemptions of biologicals to deal with emergencies; and\n(c)\nexemptions of biologicals for special and experimental\nuses; and\n(d)\nexemptions of biologicals where substitutes are\nunavailable.\nSubdivision B—Exempting biologicals under the regulations"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32c-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32c"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ca",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32CA Exempt biologicals",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32ca"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.288",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may exempt specified persons from the operation\nof Division 4 in relation to specified biologicals.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n(2) The regulations may exempt specified biologicals from the\noperation of Division 4.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n(3) An exemption under this section may be subject to conditions that\nare prescribed in the regulations.\nNote:\nThere are criminal offences and a civil penalty related to the breach of\na condition of an exemption: see sections 32CP and 32CQ.\n(5) If the regulations revoke an exemption, the revocation takes effect\non the day specified in the regulations. The day must not be earlier\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nExemptions  Division 3\nSection 32CB\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nthan 28 days after the day on which the regulations revoking the\nexemption take effect.\nSubdivision C—Exempting biologicals to deal with emergencies",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The regulations may exempt specified persons from the operation\nof Division 4 in relation to specified biologicals.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n(2) The regulations may exempt specified biologicals from the\noperation of Division 4.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n(3) An exemption under this section may be subject to conditions that\nare prescribed in the regulations.\nNote:\nThere are criminal offences and a civil penalty related to the breach of\na condition of an exemption: see sections 32CP and 32CQ.\n(5) If the regulations revoke an exemption, the revocation takes effect\non the day specified in the regulations. The day must not be earlier\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nExemptions  Division 3\nSection 32CB\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nthan 28 days after the day on which the regulations revoking the\nexemption take effect.\nSubdivision C—Exempting biologicals to deal with emergencies",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ca-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ca-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ca-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ca-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "db82edd594c1204b50881db698f8ea10f8b6ff23fcb840bb2fcc00072c71b7b6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32ca",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32CA Exempt biologicals",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 288,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may exempt specified persons from the operation\nof Division 4 in relation to specified biologicals.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n(2) The regulations may exempt specified biologicals from the\noperation of Division 4.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n(3) An exemption under this section may be subject to conditions that\nare prescribed in the regulations.\nNote:\nThere are criminal offences and a civil penalty related to the breach of\na condition of an exemption: see sections 32CP and 32CQ.\n(5) If the regulations revoke an exemption, the revocation takes effect\non the day specified in the regulations. The day must not be earlier\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nExemptions  Division 3\nSection 32CB\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nthan 28 days after the day on which the regulations revoking the\nexemption take effect.\nSubdivision C—Exempting biologicals to deal with emergencies"
    },
