      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cb-ss-1a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cb-ss-1a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fc5de5e42117aadbd69848069a4b5d9b3d6d2a5644eb3c1a7a7d76d1acbadecf",
      "skos:note": "Minister must make exemption under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32cb-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32CB(1A) Minister may make exemptions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 289,
      "values:originalText": "(1A) The Minister may make an exemption under subsection (1) only if\nthe Minister is satisfied of the matter in subsection (2) or (2A)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cb-ss-1a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cb-ss-1a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cb-ss-1a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to make exemption",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Minister is satisfied of the matter in subsection (2) or (2A)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Exemption must be made"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cb-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32CB(2) Minister may make exemptions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32cb-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.289",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The matter in this subsection is that in the national interest, the\nexemption should be made so that:\n(a) the biologicals may be stockpiled as quickly as possible in\norder to create a preparedness to deal with a potential threat\nto public health that may be caused by a possible future\nemergency; or\n(b) the biologicals can be made available urgently in Australia in\norder to deal with an actual threat to public health caused by\nan emergency that has occurred.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The matter in this subsection is that in the national interest, the\nexemption should be made so that:\n(a) the biologicals may be stockpiled as quickly as possible in\norder to create a preparedness to deal with a potential threat\nto public health that may be caused by a possible future\nemergency; or\n(b) the biologicals can be made available urgently in Australia in\norder to deal with an actual threat to public health caused by\nan emergency that has occurred.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cb"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cb-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cb-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b05959bf8079b221dc670546ec6ce03432a39d57646c600eddb0ccbefca70def",
      "skos:note": "Minister may make exemptions in national interest."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32cb-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32CB(2) Minister may make exemptions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 289,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The matter in this subsection is that in the national interest, the\nexemption should be made so that:\n(a) the biologicals may be stockpiled as quickly as possible in\norder to create a preparedness to deal with a potential threat\nto public health that may be caused by a possible future\nemergency; or\n(b) the biologicals can be made available urgently in Australia in\norder to deal with an actual threat to public health caused by\nan emergency that has occurred."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cb-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cb-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
