      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cb-ss-2a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32CB(2A) Minister may make exemptions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32cb-ss-2a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.289",
      "values:originalText": "(2A) The matter in this subsection is that:\n(a) a national emergency declaration is in force; and\n(b) either of the following apply:\n(i) the exemption should be made so that the biologicals\nmay be stockpiled to deal with a potential threat to\npublic health that may be caused by the emergency to\nwhich the national emergency declaration relates;\n(ii) the exemption should be made so that the biologicals\ncan be made available urgently in Australia in order to\ndeal with an actual threat to public health caused by the\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(2A) The matter in this subsection is that:\n(a) a national emergency declaration is in force; and\n(b) either of the following apply:\n(i) the exemption should be made so that the biologicals\nmay be stockpiled to deal with a potential threat to\npublic health that may be caused by the emergency to\nwhich the national emergency declaration relates;\n(ii) the exemption should be made so that the biologicals\ncan be made available urgently in Australia in order to\ndeal with an actual threat to public health caused by the\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cb"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cb-ss-2a-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ff8a0ded51bb92009ddf22609c12fad77d7071c77e323f785ecd3e09ff211fd8",
      "skos:note": "Minister may make exemptions under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32cb-ss-2a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32CB(2A) Minister may make exemptions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 289,
      "values:originalText": "(2A) The matter in this subsection is that:\n(a) a national emergency declaration is in force; and\n(b) either of the following apply:\n(i) the exemption should be made so that the biologicals\nmay be stockpiled to deal with a potential threat to\npublic health that may be caused by the emergency to\nwhich the national emergency declaration relates;\n(ii) the exemption should be made so that the biologicals\ncan be made available urgently in Australia in order to\ndeal with an actual threat to public health caused by the\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cb-ss-2a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cb-ss-2a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32CC Conditions of exemptions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32cc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.290",
      "values:originalText": "An exemption under section 32CB is subject to conditions\nspecified in the exemption about any of the following:\n(a) the quantity of biologicals that are exempt;\n(b) the source of those biologicals;\n(c) the persons or class of persons who may import, export,\nmanufacture or supply those biologicals;\n(d) the supply of those biologicals (including the persons or class\nof persons to whom biologicals may be supplied for use and\nthe circumstances under which a stockpile of biologicals may\nbe supplied for use);\n(e) the storage and security of those biologicals;\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nExemptions  Division 3\nSection 32CD\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(f) the keeping and disclosure of, and access to, records about\nthose biologicals;\n(g) the disposal of those biologicals;\n(h) the manner in which any of those biologicals is to be dealt\nwith if a condition of the exemption is breached;\n(i) any other matters that the Minister thinks appropriate.\nWhether or not biologicals are exempt under section 32CB is not\naffected by whether or not there is a breach of a condition under\nthis section in relation to those biologicals.\nNote 1:\nThere are criminal offences and civil penalties related to the breach of\na condition of an exemption: see sections 32CP and 32CQ.\nNote 2:\nSection 32CD deals with variation and revocation of the conditions.",
      "skos:definition": "An exemption under section 32CB is subject to conditions\nspecified in the exemption about any of the following:\n(a) the quantity of biologicals that are exempt;\n(b) the source of those biologicals;\n(c) the persons or class of persons who may import, export,\nmanufacture or supply those biologicals;\n(d) the supply of those biologicals (including the persons or class\nof persons to whom biologicals may be supplied for use and\nthe circumstances under which a stockpile of biologicals may\nbe supplied for use);\n(e) the storage and security of those biologicals;\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nExemptions  Division 3\nSection 32CD\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(f) the keeping and disclosure of, and access to, records about\nthose biologicals;\n(g) the disposal of those biologicals;\n(h) the manner in which any of those biologicals is to be dealt\nwith if a condition of the exemption is breached;\n(i) any other matters that the Minister thinks appropriate.\nWhether or not biologicals are exempt under section 32CB is not\naffected by whether or not there is a breach of a condition under\nthis section in relation to those biologicals.\nNote 1:\nThere are criminal offences and civil penalties related to the breach of\na condition of an exemption: see sections 32CP and 32CQ.\nNote 2:\nSection 32CD deals with variation and revocation of the conditions.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cc-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cc-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cc-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c7b1c460731585fbba3a42855f586235f97ca637206d026d81d8378972880350",
      "skos:note": "Conditions for exemptions under section 32CB"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32cc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32CC Conditions of exemptions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 290,
      "values:originalText": "An exemption under section 32CB is subject to conditions\nspecified in the exemption about any of the following:\n(a) the quantity of biologicals that are exempt;\n(b) the source of those biologicals;\n(c) the persons or class of persons who may import, export,\nmanufacture or supply those biologicals;\n(d) the supply of those biologicals (including the persons or class\nof persons to whom biologicals may be supplied for use and\nthe circumstances under which a stockpile of biologicals may\nbe supplied for use);\n(e) the storage and security of those biologicals;\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nExemptions  Division 3\nSection 32CD\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(f) the keeping and disclosure of, and access to, records about\nthose biologicals;\n(g) the disposal of those biologicals;\n(h) the manner in which any of those biologicals is to be dealt\nwith if a condition of the exemption is breached;\n(i) any other matters that the Minister thinks appropriate.\nWhether or not biologicals are exempt under section 32CB is not\naffected by whether or not there is a breach of a condition under\nthis section in relation to those biologicals.\nNote 1:\nThere are criminal offences and civil penalties related to the breach of\na condition of an exemption: see sections 32CP and 32CQ.\nNote 2:\nSection 32CD deals with variation and revocation of the conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cc-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cc"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cc-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Conditions for exemptions",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
