    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cj-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32CJ(6) Criminal offences and civil penalty for biologicals not",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32cj-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.294",
      "values:originalText": "(6) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the Secretary gives a notice to the person under\nsubsection (2); and\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nExemptions  Division 3\nSection 32CJ\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) the notice specifies a particular requirement mentioned in\nsubsection (3); and\n(c) the person fails to comply with that requirement; and\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of any of the biologicals has resulted in, will\nresult in, or is likely to result in, harm or injury to any\nperson; or\n(ii) the use of any of the biologicals, if any of the\nbiologicals were used, would result in, or would be\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person; and\n(e) the harm or injury has resulted, will result, is likely to result,\nwould result, or would be likely to result, because the person\nfailed to comply with that requirement.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the Secretary gives a notice to the person under\nsubsection (2); and\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nExemptions  Division 3\nSection 32CJ\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) the notice specifies a particular requirement mentioned in\nsubsection (3); and\n(c) the person fails to comply with that requirement; and\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of any of the biologicals has resulted in, will\nresult in, or is likely to result in, harm or injury to any\nperson; or\n(ii) the use of any of the biologicals, if any of the\nbiologicals were used, would result in, or would be\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person; and\n(e) the harm or injury has resulted, will result, is likely to result,\nwould result, or would be likely to result, because the person\nfailed to comply with that requirement.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cj"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cj-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cj-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cj-ss-6-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cj-ss-6-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cj-ss-6-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cj-ss-6-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "78ab3acffacaca9381df72ef1e04017c8bcc0f3ab56d64213beb686bf8eb2153",
      "skos:note": "Failure to comply with notice requirement results in harm or injury."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32cj-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32CJ(6) Criminal offences and civil penalty for biologicals not",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 294,
      "values:originalText": "(6) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the Secretary gives a notice to the person under\nsubsection (2); and\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nExemptions  Division 3\nSection 32CJ\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) the notice specifies a particular requirement mentioned in\nsubsection (3); and\n(c) the person fails to comply with that requirement; and\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of any of the biologicals has resulted in, will\nresult in, or is likely to result in, harm or injury to any\nperson; or\n(ii) the use of any of the biologicals, if any of the\nbiologicals were used, would result in, or would be\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person; and\n(e) the harm or injury has resulted, will result, is likely to result,\nwould result, or would be likely to result, because the person\nfailed to comply with that requirement.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cj-ss-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cj-ss-6"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
