      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.296",
      "values:originalText": "(4) An application for an approval for use of the kind referred to in\nparagraph (1)(e) must:\n(a) be made to the Secretary; and\n(b) be in a form (if any) approved, in writing, by the Secretary;\nand\n(c) be accompanied by such information relating to the\nbiological the subject of the application as is required by the\nSecretary; and\n(d) be accompanied by the prescribed evaluation fee.\nSecretary’s decision",
      "skos:definition": "(4) An application for an approval for use of the kind referred to in\nparagraph (1)(e) must:\n(a) be made to the Secretary; and\n(b) be in a form (if any) approved, in writing, by the Secretary;\nand\n(c) be accompanied by such information relating to the\nbiological the subject of the application as is required by the\nSecretary; and\n(d) be accompanied by the prescribed evaluation fee.\nSecretary’s decision",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ck"
      },
