    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32CM Authorities for health practitioners",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32cm"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.300",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may, in writing, authorise a specified medical\npractitioner to supply a specified biological, for use in the\ntreatment of humans, to the class or classes of recipients specified\nin the authority.\nNote:\nSection 32CN contains criminal offences relating to the giving an\nauthority to a medical practitioner.\n(1A) An application for an authority under subsection (1) must be in a\nform (if any) approved, in writing, by the Secretary.\n(2) The Secretary may give an authority under subsection (1) subject\nto any conditions that are specified in the authority.\nNote:\nThere are criminal offences and a civil penalty related to the breach of\na condition of an authority: see sections 32CP and 32CQ.\n(3) The Secretary may impose conditions (or further conditions) on an\nauthority given to a person under subsection (1) by giving to the\nperson written notice of the conditions (or further conditions).\nNote:\nThere are criminal offences and a civil penalty related to the breach of\na condition of an authority: see sections 32CP and 32CQ.\n(4) An authority under subsection (1) may only be given to a medical\npractitioner:\n(a) who is included in a class of medical practitioners prescribed\nby the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph; and\n(b) who has the approval of an ethics committee to supply the\nspecified biological.\nParagraph (b) does not apply in the circumstances (if any)\nprescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this subsection.\n(5) An authority under subsection (1) may only be given in relation to\na class or classes of recipients prescribed by the regulations for the\npurposes of this subsection.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nExemptions  Division 3\nSection 32CM\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(6) The regulations may prescribe the circumstances in which a\nbiological may be supplied under an authority under subsection (1).\n(7) An authority under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument.\n(7A) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules\nauthorising any health practitioner who is included in a specified\nclass of health practitioners to supply a specified biological, for use\nin the treatment of humans, to the class or classes of recipients\nspecified in those rules, so long as:\n(a) the biological is supplied in the circumstances specified in\nthose rules; and\n(b) the conditions (if any) specified in those rules are satisfied.\n(7B) In making rules under subsection (7A), the Minister must comply\nwith:\n(a) such requirements (if any) as are prescribed by the\nregulations; and\n(b) such restrictions (if any) as are prescribed by the regulations;\nand\n(c) such limitations (if any) as are prescribed by the regulations.\n(7C) If:\n(a) a person is authorised, by subsection (7A) rules, to supply a\nbiological; and\n(b) the person supplies the biological in accordance with those\nrules;\nthe person must:\n(c) notify the supply to the Secretary; and\n(d) do so within 28 days after the supply.\n(7D) A notification under subsection (7C) must:\n(a) be in accordance with a form that is approved, in writing, by\nthe Secretary; and\n(b) contain such information as is prescribed by the regulations.\n(7E) An approval of a form may require or permit information to be\ngiven in accordance with specified software requirements:\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary may, in writing, authorise a specified medical\npractitioner to supply a specified biological, for use in the\ntreatment of humans, to the class or classes of recipients specified\nin the authority.\nNote:\nSection 32CN contains criminal offences relating to the giving an\nauthority to a medical practitioner.\n(1A) An application for an authority under subsection (1) must be in a\nform (if any) approved, in writing, by the Secretary.\n(2) The Secretary may give an authority under subsection (1) subject\nto any conditions that are specified in the authority.\nNote:\nThere are criminal offences and a civil penalty related to the breach of\na condition of an authority: see sections 32CP and 32CQ.\n(3) The Secretary may impose conditions (or further conditions) on an\nauthority given to a person under subsection (1) by giving to the\nperson written notice of the conditions (or further conditions).\nNote:\nThere are criminal offences and a civil penalty related to the breach of\na condition of an authority: see sections 32CP and 32CQ.\n(4) An authority under subsection (1) may only be given to a medical\npractitioner:\n(a) who is included in a class of medical practitioners prescribed\nby the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph; and\n(b) who has the approval of an ethics committee to supply the\nspecified biological.\nParagraph (b) does not apply in the circumstances (if any)\nprescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this subsection.\n(5) An authority under subsection (1) may only be given in relation to\na class or classes of recipients prescribed by the regulations for the\npurposes of this subsection.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nExemptions  Division 3\nSection 32CM\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(6) The regulations may prescribe the circumstances in which a\nbiological may be supplied under an authority under subsection (1).\n(7) An authority under subsection (1) is",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-7"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-7a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-7b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-7c"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-7d"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-7e"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7e1be9155054640ad5a3a5bc77097b953199b6cf32565b85458e77422d6ea3b2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32cm",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32CM Authorities for health practitioners",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 300,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may, in writing, authorise a specified medical\npractitioner to supply a specified biological, for use in the\ntreatment of humans, to the class or classes of recipients specified\nin the authority.\nNote:\nSection 32CN contains criminal offences relating to the giving an\nauthority to a medical practitioner.\n(1A) An application for an authority under subsection (1) must be in a\nform (if any) approved, in writing, by the Secretary.\n(2) The Secretary may give an authority under subsection (1) subject\nto any conditions that are specified in the authority.\nNote:\nThere are criminal offences and a civil penalty related to the breach of\na condition of an authority: see sections 32CP and 32CQ.\n(3) The Secretary may impose conditions (or further conditions) on an\nauthority given to a person under subsection (1) by giving to the\nperson written notice of the conditions (or further conditions).\nNote:\nThere are criminal offences and a civil penalty related to the breach of\na condition of an authority: see sections 32CP and 32CQ.\n(4) An authority under subsection (1) may only be given to a medical\npractitioner:\n(a) who is included in a class of medical practitioners prescribed\nby the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph; and\n(b) who has the approval of an ethics committee to supply the\nspecified biological.\nParagraph (b) does not apply in the circumstances (if any)\nprescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this subsection.\n(5) An authority under subsection (1) may only be given in relation to\na class or classes of recipients prescribed by the regulations for the\npurposes of this subsection.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nExemptions  Division 3\nSection 32CM\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(6) The regulations may prescribe the circumstances in which a\nbiological may be supplied under an authority under subsection (1).\n(7) An authority under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument.\n(7A) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules\nauthorising any health practitioner who is included in a specified\nclass of health practitioners to supply a specified biological, for use\nin the treatment of humans, to the class or classes of recipients\nspecified in those rules, so long as:\n(a) the biological is supplied in the circumstances specified in\nthose rules; and\n(b) the conditions (if any) specified in those rules are satisfied.\n(7B) In making rules under subsection (7A), the Minister must comply\nwith:\n(a) such requirements (if any) as are prescribed by the\nregulations; and\n(b) such restrictions (if any) as are prescribed by the regulations;\nand\n(c) such limitations (if any) as are prescribed by the regulations.\n(7C) If:\n(a) a person is authorised, by subsection (7A) rules, to supply a\nbiological; and\n(b) the person supplies the biological in accordance with those\nrules;\nthe person must:\n(c) notify the supply to the Secretary; and\n(d) do so within 28 days after the supply.\n(7D) A notification under subsection (7C) must:\n(a) be in accordance with a form that is approved, in writing, by\nthe Secretary; and\n(b) contain such information as is prescribed by the regulations.\n(7E) An approval of a form may require or permit information to be\ngiven in accordance with specified software requirements:\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
