    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32CM(3) Authorities for health practitioners",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32cm-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.300",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The Secretary may impose conditions (or further conditions) on an\nauthority given to a person under subsection (1) by giving to the\nperson written notice of the conditions (or further conditions).\nNote:\nThere are criminal offences and a civil penalty related to the breach of\na condition of an authority: see sections 32CP and 32CQ.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The Secretary may impose conditions (or further conditions) on an\nauthority given to a person under subsection (1) by giving to the\nperson written notice of the conditions (or further conditions).\nNote:\nThere are criminal offences and a civil penalty related to the breach of\na condition of an authority: see sections 32CP and 32CQ.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "95ca73c03a373e1fa34e1934febb8c07716d9d3c521f5c01b187a079608d7b43",
      "skos:note": "Secretary may impose conditions on an authority"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32cm-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32CM(3) Authorities for health practitioners",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 300,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The Secretary may impose conditions (or further conditions) on an\nauthority given to a person under subsection (1) by giving to the\nperson written notice of the conditions (or further conditions).\nNote:\nThere are criminal offences and a civil penalty related to the breach of\na condition of an authority: see sections 32CP and 32CQ."
    },
