          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-4-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-4-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cm-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b6e70e5ca9265ef50145bf766b83db88f392181cb25baadcf9aa6544b0d11b9b",
      "skos:note": "Authority for medical practitioners to supply specified biologicals."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32cm-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32CM(4) Authorities for health practitioners",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 300,
      "values:originalText": "(4) An authority under subsection (1) may only be given to a medical\npractitioner:\n(a) who is included in a class of medical practitioners prescribed\nby the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph; and\n(b) who has the approval of an ethics committee to supply the\nspecified biological.\nParagraph (b) does not apply in the circumstances (if any)\nprescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this subsection."
    },
