    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32db",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32DB Inclusion of Class 1 biological in the Register",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32db"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.315",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an application is made in accordance with section 32DA for a\nClass 1 biological to be included in the Register in relation to a\nperson, the Secretary must include the biological in the Register in\nrelation to the person.\nBiological number\n(2) If the Secretary includes the biological in the Register, the\nSecretary must assign a unique number to the biological. The\nnumber assigned may be any combination of numbers and either or\nboth of letters and symbols.\nNote:\nThe number assigned is the biological number of the biological.\nCertificate\n(3) As soon as practicable after the biological has been included in the\nRegister, the Secretary must give to the applicant a certificate of\nthe inclusion of the biological in the Register.\n(4) The certificate must:\n(a) specify the biological number of the biological; and\n(b) specify the day on which the inclusion of the biological in the\nRegister commences.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If an application is made in accordance with section 32DA for a\nClass 1 biological to be included in the Register in relation to a\nperson, the Secretary must include the biological in the Register in\nrelation to the person.\nBiological number\n(2) If the Secretary includes the biological in the Register, the\nSecretary must assign a unique number to the biological. The\nnumber assigned may be any combination of numbers and either or\nboth of letters and symbols.\nNote:\nThe number assigned is the biological number of the biological.\nCertificate\n(3) As soon as practicable after the biological has been included in the\nRegister, the Secretary must give to the applicant a certificate of\nthe inclusion of the biological in the Register.\n(4) The certificate must:\n(a) specify the biological number of the biological; and\n(b) specify the day on which the inclusion of the biological in the\nRegister commences.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32db-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32db-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32db-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32db-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "06c80de58824e7279ca69e35246c88e8b65bd6937e7b0ad8f6cd4c49a064930c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32db",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32DB Inclusion of Class 1 biological in the Register",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 315,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an application is made in accordance with section 32DA for a\nClass 1 biological to be included in the Register in relation to a\nperson, the Secretary must include the biological in the Register in\nrelation to the person.\nBiological number\n(2) If the Secretary includes the biological in the Register, the\nSecretary must assign a unique number to the biological. The\nnumber assigned may be any combination of numbers and either or\nboth of letters and symbols.\nNote:\nThe number assigned is the biological number of the biological.\nCertificate\n(3) As soon as practicable after the biological has been included in the\nRegister, the Secretary must give to the applicant a certificate of\nthe inclusion of the biological in the Register.\n(4) The certificate must:\n(a) specify the biological number of the biological; and\n(b) specify the day on which the inclusion of the biological in the\nRegister commences.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
