      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32df",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32DF Inclusion of biological in the Register",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32df"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.327",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n(a) an application is made under section 32DD for a biological to\nbe included in the Register in relation to a person; and\n(aa) the application has passed preliminary assessment; and\n(b) the Secretary decides that it is appropriate to include the\nbiological in the Register after an evaluation under\nsection 32DE; and\n(c) no part of an evaluation fee under section 32DI that is due\nand payable by the person remains unpaid;\nthe Secretary must include the biological in the Register in relation\nto the person.\nBiological number\n(2) If the Secretary includes the biological in the Register, the\nSecretary must assign a unique number to the biological. The\nnumber assigned may be any combination of numbers and either or\nboth of letters and symbols.\nNote:\nThe number assigned is the biological number of the biological.\nCertificate\n(3) As soon as practicable after the biological has been included in the\nRegister, the Secretary must give to the applicant a certificate of\nthe inclusion of the biological in the Register.\n(4) The certificate must:\n(a) specify the biological number of the biological; and\n(b) specify the day on which the inclusion of the biological in the\nRegister commences.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n(a) an application is made under section 32DD for a biological to\nbe included in the Register in relation to a person; and\n(aa) the application has passed preliminary assessment; and\n(b) the Secretary decides that it is appropriate to include the\nbiological in the Register after an evaluation under\nsection 32DE; and\n(c) no part of an evaluation fee under section 32DI that is due\nand payable by the person remains unpaid;\nthe Secretary must include the biological in the Register in relation\nto the person.\nBiological number\n(2) If the Secretary includes the biological in the Register, the\nSecretary must assign a unique number to the biological. The\nnumber assigned may be any combination of numbers and either or\nboth of letters and symbols.\nNote:\nThe number assigned is the biological number of the biological.\nCertificate\n(3) As soon as practicable after the biological has been included in the\nRegister, the Secretary must give to the applicant a certificate of\nthe inclusion of the biological in the Register.\n(4) The certificate must:\n(a) specify the biological number of the biological; and\n(b) specify the day on which the inclusion of the biological in the\nRegister commences.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32df-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32df-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32df-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32df-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a5bc10ca7ca70d469926602c1033e40986a58defe0e737a2622537d2e076cce3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32df",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32DF Inclusion of biological in the Register",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 327,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n(a) an application is made under section 32DD for a biological to\nbe included in the Register in relation to a person; and\n(aa) the application has passed preliminary assessment; and\n(b) the Secretary decides that it is appropriate to include the\nbiological in the Register after an evaluation under\nsection 32DE; and\n(c) no part of an evaluation fee under section 32DI that is due\nand payable by the person remains unpaid;\nthe Secretary must include the biological in the Register in relation\nto the person.\nBiological number\n(2) If the Secretary includes the biological in the Register, the\nSecretary must assign a unique number to the biological. The\nnumber assigned may be any combination of numbers and either or\nboth of letters and symbols.\nNote:\nThe number assigned is the biological number of the biological.\nCertificate\n(3) As soon as practicable after the biological has been included in the\nRegister, the Secretary must give to the applicant a certificate of\nthe inclusion of the biological in the Register.\n(4) The certificate must:\n(a) specify the biological number of the biological; and\n(b) specify the day on which the inclusion of the biological in the\nRegister commences.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
