    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32dh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32DH Lapsing of application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32dh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.328",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application under section 32DD for inclusion of a biological in\nthe Register lapses if:\n(a) any part of the evaluation fee payable in respect of the\nbiological remains unpaid at the end of the period of 42 days\nafter the day on which the part became due and payable; or\n(b) information given to the Secretary by, or on behalf of, the\napplicant in connection with the application, including\ninformation given for the purpose of a requirement under\nsection 32JA, is false or misleading in a material particular;\nor\n(c) the applicant fails to comply with a requirement under\nsection 32JA to give information consisting of patient data in\nrelation to the biological.\n(2) In this section:\npatient data, in relation to a biological, means information, derived\nfrom clinical trials, relating to individuals before, during and after\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nIncluding biologicals in the Register  Division 4\nSection 32DI\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nthe administration of the biological to those individuals, including,\nbut not limited to, demographic, biochemical and haematological\ninformation.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An application under section 32DD for inclusion of a biological in\nthe Register lapses if:\n(a) any part of the evaluation fee payable in respect of the\nbiological remains unpaid at the end of the period of 42 days\nafter the day on which the part became due and payable; or\n(b) information given to the Secretary by, or on behalf of, the\napplicant in connection with the application, including\ninformation given for the purpose of a requirement under\nsection 32JA, is false or misleading in a material particular;\nor\n(c) the applicant fails to comply with a requirement under\nsection 32JA to give information consisting of patient data in\nrelation to the biological.\n(2) In this section:\npatient data, in relation to a biological, means information, derived\nfrom clinical trials, relating to individuals before, during and after\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nIncluding biologicals in the Register  Division 4\nSection 32DI\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nthe administration of the biological to those individuals, including,\nbut not limited to, demographic, biochemical and haematological\ninformation.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32dh-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32dh-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "99246d20b94baafca32d8719d7c338d5fddb968bc8a1391224d3f1f695fd1142"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32dh",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32DH Lapsing of application",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 328,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application under section 32DD for inclusion of a biological in\nthe Register lapses if:\n(a) any part of the evaluation fee payable in respect of the\nbiological remains unpaid at the end of the period of 42 days\nafter the day on which the part became due and payable; or\n(b) information given to the Secretary by, or on behalf of, the\napplicant in connection with the application, including\ninformation given for the purpose of a requirement under\nsection 32JA, is false or misleading in a material particular;\nor\n(c) the applicant fails to comply with a requirement under\nsection 32JA to give information consisting of patient data in\nrelation to the biological.\n(2) In this section:\npatient data, in relation to a biological, means information, derived\nfrom clinical trials, relating to individuals before, during and after\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nIncluding biologicals in the Register  Division 4\nSection 32DI\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nthe administration of the biological to those individuals, including,\nbut not limited to, demographic, biochemical and haematological\ninformation."
    },
