    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32do",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32DO Criminal offences for false statements in applications for",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32do"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.334",
      "values:originalText": "including biologicals in the Register\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in, or in connection with, an\napplication for inclusion of a biological in the Register; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular;\nand\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of the biological has resulted in, will result in, or\nis likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the biological, if the biological were used,\nwould result in, or would be likely to result in, harm or\ninjury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in, or in connection with, an\napplication for inclusion of a biological in the Register; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nIncluding biologicals in the Register  Division 4\nSection 32DP\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in, or in connection with, an\napplication for inclusion of a biological in the Register; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(6) An offence against subsection (5) is an offence of strict liability.",
      "skos:definition": "including biologicals in the Register\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in, or in connection with, an\napplication for inclusion of a biological in the Register; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular;\nand\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of the biological has resulted in, will result in, or\nis likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the biological, if the biological were used,\nwould result in, or would be likely to result in, harm or\ninjury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in, or in connection with, an\napplication for inclusion of a biological in the Register; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nIncluding biologicals in the Register  Division 4\nSection 32DP\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in, or in connection with, an\napplication for inclusion of a biological in the Register; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(6) An offence against subsection (5) is an offence of strict liability.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32do-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32do-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32do-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32do-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "76894ee034b29d5f53608365656279a356af0f53ab78b8501ea4da7ea00c8034"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32do",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32DO Criminal offences for false statements in applications for",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 334,
      "values:originalText": "including biologicals in the Register\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in, or in connection with, an\napplication for inclusion of a biological in the Register; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular;\nand\n(d) either:\n(i) the use of the biological has resulted in, will result in, or\nis likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the biological, if the biological were used,\nwould result in, or would be likely to result in, harm or\ninjury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in, or in connection with, an\napplication for inclusion of a biological in the Register; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nIncluding biologicals in the Register  Division 4\nSection 32DP\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement; and\n(b) the statement is made in, or in connection with, an\napplication for inclusion of a biological in the Register; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(6) An offence against subsection (5) is an offence of strict liability."
    },
    {
