        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Secretary must inform the Gene Technology Regulator of the decision on the application.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Secretary must inform the Gene Technology Regulator of the decision on the application."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32E What this Division is about",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.341",
      "values:originalText": "Inclusions of biologicals in the Register are subject to certain\nautomatic conditions. The Minister and the Secretary may impose\nfurther conditions.",
      "skos:definition": "Inclusions of biologicals in the Register are subject to certain\nautomatic conditions. The Minister and the Secretary may impose\nfurther conditions.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32e-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "55c7893eefc5e4d3c641701e1c1f27f33d7a6e5f1d2c7bd23186a7663cda6f9f",
      "skos:note": "Exemptions from automatic conditions for inclusions of biologicals in the Register"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32E What this Division is about",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 341,
      "values:originalText": "Inclusions of biologicals in the Register are subject to certain\nautomatic conditions. The Minister and the Secretary may impose\nfurther conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32e-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32e"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ea",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32EA Conditions applying automatically",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32ea"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.341",
      "values:originalText": "Entry and inspection powers\n(1) The inclusion of a biological in the Register is subject to a\ncondition that the person in relation to whom the biological is\nincluded in the Register will:\n(a) allow an authorised person:\n(i) to enter, at any reasonable time, any premises (including\npremises outside Australia) at which that person or any\nother person deals with the biological, complies with\nrecord-keeping conditions under paragraph 32EC(2)(c)\nor keeps documents that relate to the biological; and\n(ii) while on those premises, to inspect those premises and\nany biological on those premises and to examine, take\nmeasurements of, conduct tests on or take samples of\nany biological on those premises or any thing on those\npremises that relates to any biological; and\n(iii) while on those premises, to make any still or moving\nimage or any recording of those premises or any thing\non those premises; and\n(iv) while on those premises, to inspect, and make copies of,\nany records kept in compliance with a condition under\nparagraph 32EC(2)(c); and\n(v) while on those premises, to inspect, and make copies of,\nany documents that relate to the biological; and\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "Entry and inspection powers\n(1) The inclusion of a biological in the Register is subject to a\ncondition that the person in relation to whom the biological is\nincluded in the Register will:\n(a) allow an authorised person:\n(i) to enter, at any reasonable time, any premises (including\npremises outside Australia) at which that person or any\nother person deals with the biological, complies with\nrecord-keeping conditions under paragraph 32EC(2)(c)\nor keeps documents that relate to the biological; and\n(ii) while on those premises, to inspect those premises and\nany biological on those premises and to examine, take\nmeasurements of, conduct tests on or take samples of\nany biological on those premises or any thing on those\npremises that relates to any biological; and\n(iii) while on those premises, to make any still or moving\nimage or any recording of those premises or any thing\non those premises; and\n(iv) while on those premises, to inspect, and make copies of,\nany records kept in compliance with a condition under\nparagraph 32EC(2)(c); and\n(v) while on those premises, to inspect, and make copies of,\nany documents that relate to the biological; and\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ea-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ea-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ea-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9a37c6652c9fa43f76135a5e1330bf7596828e100acc1afd10924f9758c91fdc",
      "skos:note": "Allow entry and inspection of premises for authorized persons."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32ea",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32EA Conditions applying automatically",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 341,
      "values:originalText": "Entry and inspection powers\n(1) The inclusion of a biological in the Register is subject to a\ncondition that the person in relation to whom the biological is\nincluded in the Register will:\n(a) allow an authorised person:\n(i) to enter, at any reasonable time, any premises (including\npremises outside Australia) at which that person or any\nother person deals with the biological, complies with\nrecord-keeping conditions under paragraph 32EC(2)(c)\nor keeps documents that relate to the biological; and\n(ii) while on those premises, to inspect those premises and\nany biological on those premises and to examine, take\nmeasurements of, conduct tests on or take samples of\nany biological on those premises or any thing on those\npremises that relates to any biological; and\n(iii) while on those premises, to make any still or moving\nimage or any recording of those premises or any thing\non those premises; and\n(iv) while on those premises, to inspect, and make copies of,\nany records kept in compliance with a condition under\nparagraph 32EC(2)(c); and\n(v) while on those premises, to inspect, and make copies of,\nany documents that relate to the biological; and\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ea-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ea"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ea-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Allow",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Grant permission for entry and inspection.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person in relation to whom the biological is included in the Register...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...to allow an authorised person to enter, inspect, and examine."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ea-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "During",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Entry is allowed during reasonable hours.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "at any reasonable time",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...to enter, inspect, and examine at any reasonable time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32eb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32EB Certification of manufacturing steps outside Australia",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32eb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.345",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The person in relation to whom a biological, other than a Class 1\nbiological, is included in the Register may apply to the Secretary\nfor a certification under this section of a step in the manufacture of\nthe biological that is to be carried out outside Australia.\n(2) If an application is made to the Secretary under this section, the\nSecretary may, by writing, certify that the manufacturing and\nquality control procedures used in that step are acceptable. The\nSecretary must give the person written notice of the certification.\n(3) In deciding whether to give the certification, subsections 25(2),\n(2E), (2F) and (2G) apply in a way corresponding to the way in\nwhich they apply for the purposes of paragraph 25(1)(g).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The person in relation to whom a biological, other than a Class 1\nbiological, is included in the Register may apply to the Secretary\nfor a certification under this section of a step in the manufacture of\nthe biological that is to be carried out outside Australia.\n(2) If an application is made to the Secretary under this section, the\nSecretary may, by writing, certify that the manufacturing and\nquality control procedures used in that step are acceptable. The\nSecretary must give the person written notice of the certification.\n(3) In deciding whether to give the certification, subsections 25(2),\n(2E), (2F) and (2G) apply in a way corresponding to the way in\nwhich they apply for the purposes of paragraph 25(1)(g).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32eb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32eb-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32eb-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b66af32aae7926445826e3d2ced9867e4eba82e5b71a4c5fa3f0bae1fe99177a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32eb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32EB Certification of manufacturing steps outside Australia",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 345,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The person in relation to whom a biological, other than a Class 1\nbiological, is included in the Register may apply to the Secretary\nfor a certification under this section of a step in the manufacture of\nthe biological that is to be carried out outside Australia.\n(2) If an application is made to the Secretary under this section, the\nSecretary may, by writing, certify that the manufacturing and\nquality control procedures used in that step are acceptable. The\nSecretary must give the person written notice of the certification.\n(3) In deciding whether to give the certification, subsections 25(2),\n(2E), (2F) and (2G) apply in a way corresponding to the way in\nwhich they apply for the purposes of paragraph 25(1)(g)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32eb-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32EB(1) Certification of manufacturing steps outside Australia",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32eb-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
