      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition on biological entry",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Secretary may cancel the entry of a biological from the Register.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The entry must be cancelled."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ga-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Temporal Interval",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal interval for cancellation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The cancellation is effective immediately.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The cancellation is effective from the date of notice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32gb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32GB Immediate cancellation of biological from the Register after",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32gb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.355",
      "values:originalText": "failure to comply with information gathering notice\n(1) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the person in relation\nto whom a biological is included in the Register, cancel the entry\nof the biological from the Register if:\n(a) the Secretary gives to the person a notice under section 32JA\nrequiring the person to give to the Secretary information, or\nto produce to the Secretary documents, relating to the\nbiological; and\n(b) the notice under section 32JA is given for the purposes of\nascertaining whether any of the certifications by the person\nunder subsection 32DA(3) or 32DCA(4) in relation to the\nbiological are incorrect; and\n(c) the person fails to comply with the notice under section 32JA\nwithin a further 14 days after the end of the period specified\nin that notice.\n(2) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the person in relation\nto whom a biological is included in the Register, cancel the entry\nof the biological from the Register if:\n(a) the Secretary gives to the person a notice under section 32JA\nrequiring the person to give to the Secretary information, or\nto produce to the Secretary documents, relating to whether\nthe biological is being:\n(i) supplied in Australia; or\n(ii) imported into Australia; or\n(iii) exported from Australia; and\n(b) either:\n(i) the information or documents given are to the effect that\nthe biological is not being supplied in Australia,\nimported into Australia or exported from Australia; or\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "failure to comply with information gathering notice\n(1) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the person in relation\nto whom a biological is included in the Register, cancel the entry\nof the biological from the Register if:\n(a) the Secretary gives to the person a notice under section 32JA\nrequiring the person to give to the Secretary information, or\nto produce to the Secretary documents, relating to the\nbiological; and\n(b) the notice under section 32JA is given for the purposes of\nascertaining whether any of the certifications by the person\nunder subsection 32DA(3) or 32DCA(4) in relation to the\nbiological are incorrect; and\n(c) the person fails to comply with the notice under section 32JA\nwithin a further 14 days after the end of the period specified\nin that notice.\n(2) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the person in relation\nto whom a biological is included in the Register, cancel the entry\nof the biological from the Register if:\n(a) the Secretary gives to the person a notice under section 32JA\nrequiring the person to give to the Secretary information, or\nto produce to the Secretary documents, relating to whether\nthe biological is being:\n(i) supplied in Australia; or\n(ii) imported into Australia; or\n(iii) exported from Australia; and\n(b) either:\n(i) the information or documents given are to the effect that\nthe biological is not being supplied in Australia,\nimported into Australia or exported from Australia; or\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
