      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ha",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32HA Public notification, and recall, of biologicals",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32ha"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.360",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may, by notice in writing, impose requirements,\nrelating to a biological, on a person if:\n(a) any of the circumstances referred to in the 2nd column of an\nitem in the following table occur in relation to the biological;\nand\n(b) the person is referred to in the 3rd column of that item.\nCircumstances in which requirements may be imposed\nItem\nCircumstance relating to biological\nPerson subject to\nrequirements\nIt is supplied while it is included in the\nRegister, but the Secretary is satisfied that it\ndoes not conform with a standard applicable to\nit\nThe person in relation to\nwhom it is included in the\nRegister\nIt is a biological, other than a Class 1\nbiological, and it is supplied while it is included\nin the Register, but the Secretary is satisfied\nthat the manufacturing principles have not been\nobserved in its manufacture\nThe person in relation to\nwhom it is included in the\nRegister\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nPublic notification, and recall, of biologicals  Division 8\nSection 32HA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nCircumstances in which requirements may be imposed\nItem\nCircumstance relating to biological\nPerson subject to\nrequirements\nIt is supplied while:\n(a) the person is exempt under\nsubsection 32CA(1) in relation to the\nbiological or the biological is exempt under\nsubsection 32CA(2); or\n(b) it is exempt under section 32CB; or\n(c) it is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CK(1); or\n(d) it is the subject of an authority under\nsubsection 32CM(1) or (7A); or\n(e) it is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CO(1), (1A) or (2);\nbut the Secretary is satisfied that it does not\nconform with a standard applicable to it\nThe person supplying it\nIt is a biological, other than a Class 1\nbiological, and it is supplied while:\n(a) the person is exempt under\nsubsection 32CA(1) in relation to the\nbiological or the biological is exempt under\nsubsection 32CA(2); or\n(b) it is exempt under section 32CB; or\n(c) it is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CK(1); or\n(d) it is the subject of an authority under\nsubsection 32CM(1) or (7A); or\n(e) it is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CO(1), (1A) or (2);\nbut the Secretary is satisfied that the\nmanufacturing principles have not been\nobserved in its manufacture\nThe person supplying it\n4A.\nIt is supplied and the Secretary is satisfied that:\n(a) if there are one or more absolute\nprohibitions in force for the purposes of\nsubsection 9K(1) or (3)—the supply\ncontravenes one or more of those\nThe person supplying it\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary may, by notice in writing, impose requirements,\nrelating to a biological, on a person if:\n(a) any of the circumstances referred to in the 2nd column of an\nitem in the following table occur in relation to the biological;\nand\n(b) the person is referred to in the 3rd column of that item.\nCircumstances in which requirements may be imposed\nItem\nCircumstance relating to biological\nPerson subject to\nrequirements\nIt is supplied while it is included in the\nRegister, but the Secretary is satisfied that it\ndoes not conform with a standard applicable to\nit\nThe person in relation to\nwhom it is included in the\nRegister\nIt is a biological, other than a Class 1\nbiological, and it is supplied while it is included\nin the Register, but the Secretary is satisfied\nthat the manufacturing principles have not been\nobserved in its manufacture\nThe person in relation to\nwhom it is included in the\nRegister\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nPublic notification, and recall, of biologicals  Division 8\nSection 32HA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nCircumstances in which requirements may be imposed\nItem\nCircumstance relating to biological\nPerson subject to\nrequirements\nIt is supplied while:\n(a) the person is exempt under\nsubsection 32CA(1) in relation to the\nbiological or the biological is exempt under\nsubsection 32CA(2); or\n(b) it is exempt under section 32CB; or\n(c) it is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CK(1); or\n(d) it is the subject of an authority under\nsubsection 32CM(1) or (7A); or\n(e) it is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CO(1), (1A) or (2);\nbut the Secretary is satisfied that it does not\nconform with a standard applicable to it\nThe person supplying it\nIt is a biological, other than a Class 1\nbiological, and it is supplied while:\n(a) the person is exempt under\nsubsection 32CA(1) in relation to the\nbiological or the biological is exempt under\nsubsection 32C",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ha-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ha-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b8704ece98d6847693b714453eb76eadcc8f17405d135858207e62dc7fca44f1",
      "skos:note": "The Secretary may impose requirements on a person supplying a biological if certain circumstances occur."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32ha",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32HA Public notification, and recall, of biologicals",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 360,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may, by notice in writing, impose requirements,\nrelating to a biological, on a person if:\n(a) any of the circumstances referred to in the 2nd column of an\nitem in the following table occur in relation to the biological;\nand\n(b) the person is referred to in the 3rd column of that item.\nCircumstances in which requirements may be imposed\nItem\nCircumstance relating to biological\nPerson subject to\nrequirements\nIt is supplied while it is included in the\nRegister, but the Secretary is satisfied that it\ndoes not conform with a standard applicable to\nit\nThe person in relation to\nwhom it is included in the\nRegister\nIt is a biological, other than a Class 1\nbiological, and it is supplied while it is included\nin the Register, but the Secretary is satisfied\nthat the manufacturing principles have not been\nobserved in its manufacture\nThe person in relation to\nwhom it is included in the\nRegister\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nPublic notification, and recall, of biologicals  Division 8\nSection 32HA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nCircumstances in which requirements may be imposed\nItem\nCircumstance relating to biological\nPerson subject to\nrequirements\nIt is supplied while:\n(a) the person is exempt under\nsubsection 32CA(1) in relation to the\nbiological or the biological is exempt under\nsubsection 32CA(2); or\n(b) it is exempt under section 32CB; or\n(c) it is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CK(1); or\n(d) it is the subject of an authority under\nsubsection 32CM(1) or (7A); or\n(e) it is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CO(1), (1A) or (2);\nbut the Secretary is satisfied that it does not\nconform with a standard applicable to it\nThe person supplying it\nIt is a biological, other than a Class 1\nbiological, and it is supplied while:\n(a) the person is exempt under\nsubsection 32CA(1) in relation to the\nbiological or the biological is exempt under\nsubsection 32CA(2); or\n(b) it is exempt under section 32CB; or\n(c) it is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CK(1); or\n(d) it is the subject of an authority under\nsubsection 32CM(1) or (7A); or\n(e) it is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 32CO(1), (1A) or (2);\nbut the Secretary is satisfied that the\nmanufacturing principles have not been\nobserved in its manufacture\nThe person supplying it\n4A.\nIt is supplied and the Secretary is satisfied that:\n(a) if there are one or more absolute\nprohibitions in force for the purposes of\nsubsection 9K(1) or (3)—the supply\ncontravenes one or more of those\nThe person supplying it\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
    {
