    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32hc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32HC Criminal offences for non-compliance with requirements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32hc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.364",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the\nperson under section 32HA; and\n(c) the act or omission has resulted in, will result in, or is likely\nto result in, harm or injury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the\nperson under section 32HA.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the\nperson under section 32HA.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nPublic notification, and recall, of biologicals  Division 8\nSection 32HD\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(6) An offence against subsection (5) is an offence of strict liability.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the\nperson under section 32HA; and\n(c) the act or omission has resulted in, will result in, or is likely\nto result in, harm or injury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the\nperson under section 32HA.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the\nperson under section 32HA.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nPublic notification, and recall, of biologicals  Division 8\nSection 32HD\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(6) An offence against subsection (5) is an offence of strict liability.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32hc-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32hc-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32hc-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32hc-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "22c82f786479c14cb09a14160b0d25cbc03c11101f7caceb46772625617fab8d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32hc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32HC Criminal offences for non-compliance with requirements",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 364,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the\nperson under section 32HA; and\n(c) the act or omission has resulted in, will result in, or is likely\nto result in, harm or injury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the\nperson under section 32HA.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the\nperson under section 32HA.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nPublic notification, and recall, of biologicals  Division 8\nSection 32HD\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(6) An offence against subsection (5) is an offence of strict liability."
    },
    {
