    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32jd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32JD Self-incrimination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32jd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.371",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is not excused from giving information or producing a\ndocument under section 32JA on the ground that the information or\nthe production of the document might tend to incriminate the\nperson or expose the person to a penalty.\n(2) However, in the case of an individual:\n(a) the information given or the document produced; and\n(b) giving the information or producing the document; and\n(c) any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or\nindirect consequence of giving the information or producing\nthe document;\nare not admissible in evidence against the individual:\n(d) in criminal proceedings, except proceedings for an offence\nagainst subsection 32JB(1), (1B), (2), (5) or (6); or\n(e) in civil proceedings, except proceedings under section 42Y\nfor a contravention of section 32JC.\nSubdivision C—Obtaining information or documents for\nbiologicals covered by exemptions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person is not excused from giving information or producing a\ndocument under section 32JA on the ground that the information or\nthe production of the document might tend to incriminate the\nperson or expose the person to a penalty.\n(2) However, in the case of an individual:\n(a) the information given or the document produced; and\n(b) giving the information or producing the document; and\n(c) any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or\nindirect consequence of giving the information or producing\nthe document;\nare not admissible in evidence against the individual:\n(d) in criminal proceedings, except proceedings for an offence\nagainst subsection 32JB(1), (1B), (2), (5) or (6); or\n(e) in civil proceedings, except proceedings under section 42Y\nfor a contravention of section 32JC.\nSubdivision C—Obtaining information or documents for\nbiologicals covered by exemptions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32jd-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32jd-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5ab30f047ec55cf21b204c002636edb20936c0ed7d776bca01097072f9ce7187"
    },
    {
