    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32jh-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32JH(2) Secretary may require information etc. about biologicals",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32jh-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.376",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 32JE, 32JF, 32JG\nor 32JH; and\n(b) the person gives information or produces a document in\ncompliance or purported compliance with the notice; and\n(c) the information or document is false or misleading in a\nmaterial particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 32JE, 32JF, 32JG\nor 32JH; and\n(b) the person gives information or produces a document in\ncompliance or purported compliance with the notice; and\n(c) the information or document is false or misleading in a\nmaterial particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32jh"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32jh-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32jh-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32jh-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a2c8711943ee9f6cacad211b7224d6047adaafeab3d1df75a58f105cb84af182",
      "skos:note": "Giving false information in response to a notice is an offence. Must provide information or documents within a specified period and in the form specified by the notice.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32jh-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32JH(2) Secretary may require information etc. about biologicals",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 376,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 32JE, 32JF, 32JG\nor 32JH; and\n(b) the person gives information or produces a document in\ncompliance or purported compliance with the notice; and\n(c) the information or document is false or misleading in a\nmaterial particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA."
    },
