      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32jj",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32JJ Civil penalty for giving false or misleading information or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32jj"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.378",
      "values:originalText": "document in compliance with a notice\nA person contravenes this section if:\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 32JE, 32JF, 32JG\nor 32JH; and\n(b) the person gives information or produces a document in\ncompliance or purported compliance with the notice; and\n(c) the information or document is false or misleading in a\nmaterial particular.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—5,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—50,000 penalty units.",
      "skos:definition": "document in compliance with a notice\nA person contravenes this section if:\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 32JE, 32JF, 32JG\nor 32JH; and\n(b) the person gives information or produces a document in\ncompliance or purported compliance with the notice; and\n(c) the information or document is false or misleading in a\nmaterial particular.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—5,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—50,000 penalty units.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32jj-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32jj-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4fb152d0f61815fed84acf184caa1c9b05ddfc83a1798985bc019c1bf439bddd",
      "skos:note": "Giving false or misleading information in compliance with a notice is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32jj",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32JJ Civil penalty for giving false or misleading information or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 378,
      "values:originalText": "document in compliance with a notice\nA person contravenes this section if:\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 32JE, 32JF, 32JG\nor 32JH; and\n(b) the person gives information or produces a document in\ncompliance or purported compliance with the notice; and\n(c) the information or document is false or misleading in a\nmaterial particular.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—5,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—50,000 penalty units."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32jj-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32jj"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32jj-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits giving false or misleading information in compliance with a notice.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32jk",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32JK Self-incrimination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32jk"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.378",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is not excused from giving information or producing a\ndocument under section 32JE, 32JF, 32JG or 32JH on the ground\nthat the information or the production of the document might tend\nto incriminate the person or expose the person to a penalty.\n(2) However, in the case of an individual:\n(a) the information given or the document produced; and\n(b) giving the information or producing the document; and\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nObtaining information or documents  Division 9\nSection 32JL\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(c) any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or\nindirect consequence of giving the information or producing\nthe document;\nare not admissible in evidence against the individual:\n(d) in criminal proceedings, except proceedings for an offence\nagainst subsection 32JI(1), (1A), (2) or (3); or\n(e) in civil proceedings, except proceedings under section 42Y\nfor a contravention of section 32JJ.\nSubdivision D—Inspecting, copying and retaining documents",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person is not excused from giving information or producing a\ndocument under section 32JE, 32JF, 32JG or 32JH on the ground\nthat the information or the production of the document might tend\nto incriminate the person or expose the person to a penalty.\n(2) However, in the case of an individual:\n(a) the information given or the document produced; and\n(b) giving the information or producing the document; and\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nBiologicals  Part 3-2A\nObtaining information or documents  Division 9\nSection 32JL\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(c) any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or\nindirect consequence of giving the information or producing\nthe document;\nare not admissible in evidence against the individual:\n(d) in criminal proceedings, except proceedings for an offence\nagainst subsection 32JI(1), (1A), (2) or (3); or\n(e) in civil proceedings, except proceedings under section 42Y\nfor a contravention of section 32JJ.\nSubdivision D—Inspecting, copying and retaining documents",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32jk-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32jk-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5a141b684615404fa6718f6d48185cebb5808f5ac8e143a71f690acf799aeb94"
    },
