        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "65c05402790361096b09ba5075c5d77f23b1f7d378696fbdfa09353c6c41b3ef",
      "skos:note": "Must provide access to documents for inspection and copying.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-32jm-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32JM(4) Secretary may retain documents",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 379,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Until a certified copy is supplied, the Secretary must provide the\nperson otherwise entitled to possession of the document, or a\nperson authorised by that person, reasonable access to the\ndocument for the purposes of inspecting and making copies of the\nwhole or a part of the document.\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
