    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-35b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "35B Criminal offences relating to breaching a condition of a licence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-35b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.384",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person holds a licence; and\n(b) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(c) the act or omission breaches a condition of the licence; and\n(d) the act or omission has resulted in, will result in, or is likely\nto result in, harm or injury to any person.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nManufacturing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-3\n\nSection 35C\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person holds a licence; and\n(b) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(c) the act or omission breaches a condition of the licence.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person holds a licence; and\n(b) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(c) the act or omission breaches a condition of the licence.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(6) An offence against subsection (5) is an offence of strict liability.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person holds a licence; and\n(b) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(c) the act or omission breaches a condition of the licence; and\n(d) the act or omission has resulted in, will result in, or is likely\nto result in, harm or injury to any person.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nManufacturing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-3\n\nSection 35C\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person holds a licence; and\n(b) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(c) the act or omission breaches a condition of the licence.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person holds a licence; and\n(b) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(c) the act or omission breaches a condition of the licence.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(6) An offence against subsection (5) is an offence of strict liability.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-35b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-35b-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-35b-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-35b-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "02313874176523de19d0d6e1d970fc312694bb1783de6dbedd474e7334f2d0eb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-35b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "35B Criminal offences relating to breaching a condition of a licence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 384,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person holds a licence; and\n(b) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(c) the act or omission breaches a condition of the licence; and\n(d) the act or omission has resulted in, will result in, or is likely\nto result in, harm or injury to any person.\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nManufacturing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-3\n\nSection 35C\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person holds a licence; and\n(b) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(c) the act or omission breaches a condition of the licence.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person holds a licence; and\n(b) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(c) the act or omission breaches a condition of the licence.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(6) An offence against subsection (5) is an offence of strict liability."
    },
