    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ac",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41AC Criminal offence for contravening a requirement in a notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ac"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.406",
      "values:originalText": "under section 41AB\nA person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person has been given a notice under section 41AB; and\n(b) the person omits to do an act; and\n(c) the omission contravenes a requirement in the notice.\nPenalty: 400 penalty units.",
      "skos:definition": "under section 41AB\nA person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person has been given a notice under section 41AB; and\n(b) the person omits to do an act; and\n(c) the omission contravenes a requirement in the notice.\nPenalty: 400 penalty units.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ac-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ac-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ef30cf0b81e2401c874c7ab17c67d338f6b72782dd25e9f6da05399b8de4cf2c",
      "skos:note": "Failure to comply with a notice results in an offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ac",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41AC Criminal offence for contravening a requirement in a notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 406,
      "values:originalText": "under section 41AB\nA person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person has been given a notice under section 41AB; and\n(b) the person omits to do an act; and\n(c) the omission contravenes a requirement in the notice.\nPenalty: 400 penalty units."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ac-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ac"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ac-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to comply with a notice.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Given a notice under section 41AB, the person must do an act.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Failure to do so results in an offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ad",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41AD False or misleading information—offence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ad"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.406",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nManufacturing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-3\n\nSection 41AE\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 41AB; and\n(b) the person gives information to the Secretary in compliance,\nor purported compliance, with the notice; and\n(c) the person does so knowing that the information:\n(i) is false or misleading; or\n(ii) omits any matter or thing without which the information\nis misleading.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply as a result of subparagraph (1)(c)(i)\nif the information is not false or misleading in a material particular.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2).\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply as a result of subparagraph (1)(c)(ii)\nif the information did not omit any matter or thing without which\nthe information is misleading in a material particular.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (3).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nManufacturing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-3\n\nSection 41AE\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 41AB; and\n(b) the person gives information to the Secretary in compliance,\nor purported compliance, with the notice; and\n(c) the person does so knowing that the information:\n(i) is false or misleading; or\n(ii) omits any matter or thing without which the information\nis misleading.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply as a result of subparagraph (1)(c)(i)\nif the information is not false or misleading in a material particular.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2).\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply as a result of subparagraph (1)(c)(ii)\nif the information did not omit any matter or thing without which\nthe information is misleading in a material particular.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (3).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ad-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ad-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ad-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "de58535ff921edfe8208c345102a7961ff3a52b8d1cf42e76a31916c18451583"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ad",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41AD False or misleading information—offence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 406,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\nMedicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3\nManufacturing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-3\n\nSection 41AE\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 41AB; and\n(b) the person gives information to the Secretary in compliance,\nor purported compliance, with the notice; and\n(c) the person does so knowing that the information:\n(i) is false or misleading; or\n(ii) omits any matter or thing without which the information\nis misleading.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply as a result of subparagraph (1)(c)(i)\nif the information is not false or misleading in a material particular.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2).\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply as a result of subparagraph (1)(c)(ii)\nif the information did not omit any matter or thing without which\nthe information is misleading in a material particular.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (3)."
    },
    {
