    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ae",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41AE False or misleading documents—offence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ae"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.407",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person produces a document to the Secretary; and\n(b) the person does so knowing that the document is false or\nmisleading; and\n(c) the document is produced in compliance, or purported\ncompliance, with a notice given under section 41AB.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the document is not false or\nmisleading in a material particular.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2).\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person produces a document to the Secretary; and\n(b) the person does so knowing that the document is false or\nmisleading; and\n(c) the document is produced in compliance, or purported\ncompliance, with a notice given under section 41AB.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the document is not false or\nmisleading in a material particular.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2).\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ae-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ae-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "381c1be6f26eabd1e34ed5b4df258a3abcf14561615bc10b13d1e1eaa7533ecf"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ae",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41AE False or misleading documents—offence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 407,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person produces a document to the Secretary; and\n(b) the person does so knowing that the document is false or\nmisleading; and\n(c) the document is produced in compliance, or purported\ncompliance, with a notice given under section 41AB.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the document is not false or\nmisleading in a material particular.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2).\n\nChapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"
    },
