      "cml:logicSummary": "Permits admissibility of self-incrimination evidence in certain proceedings.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(e) proceedings for a pecuniary penalty order against the individual for a contravention of a civil penalty provision.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "is admissible in evidence in: (e) proceedings for a pecuniary penalty order against the individual for a contravention of a civil penalty provision;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ag-ss-2-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Right",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Establishes right to self-incrimination protection.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) However, in the case of an individual:",
      "cml:conclusionText": "the information given or the document produced; or the giving of the information or the production of the document; or any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or indirect consequence of giving the information or producing the document; is not admissible in evidence in: (d) criminal proceedings against the individual, except proceedings under, or arising out of, section 41AD or 41AE;"
    },
    {
